      "name": "InvokeRenderingCallback",
      "signature": "int InvokeRenderingCallback(int renderMode)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Initializes rendering frame counter and invokes rendering callback.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Increment global frame counter (DAT_6f9e9c34) by 1\n2. Loop until counter is non-zero (skip if overflow occurs)\n3. Invoke registered rendering callback function via pointer\n4. Return success status (1)\n\nParameters:\n- renderMode (int): Rendering mode to pass to callback function\n\nReturns:\n- 1: Success, callback invoked and frame counter incremented\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Frame counter loops on overflow, ensuring it never stays at 0\n- Callback function pointer stored at DAT_6fa0a0e0\n- Used for synchronizing rendering operations with frame updates",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "MNE",
