      "name": "ValidateEditBoxAndSetMask",
      "signature": "int ValidateEditBoxAndSetMask(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Validates edit box content and sets bitmask based on text presence.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get Unicode text from edit box child control (g_dwInventorySlot7)\n2. If text is NULL, mask type is 0 (empty)\n3. Convert Unicode text to ANSI string (max 31 chars)\n4. Calculate string length using inline strlen loop\n5. If string length > 0, set mask type to 1 (has content)\n6. Call SetUnitBitMask on g_dwInventorySlot5 with mask type\n7. Return 1 (always succeeds)\n\nParameters: None (reads from global inventory slots)\n\nReturns:\n  int - Always returns 1\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - NULL edit box child pointer results in mask type 0\n  - Empty string (length 0) results in mask type 0\n  - Any non-empty string results in mask type 1\n\nGlobal Dependencies:\n  g_dwInventorySlot7 - Edit box control handle (input)\n  g_dwInventorySlot5 - Target control for bitmask (output)\n\nCalled Functions:\n  D2Win_GetEditBoxChild - Gets child Unicode text from edit box\n  Unicode::unicode2Win - Converts Unicode to ANSI\n  SetUnitBitMask - Sets bitmask on inventory slot control",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:570cf27911ed739015d6358c26cd5f08",
