      "name": "CreateBnetUIObjectByDescriptorIndex",
      "signature": "void * CreateBnetUIObjectByDescriptorIndex(int nDescriptorIndex)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Creates a Battle.net UI object from descriptor table by index and adds it to child array.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Assert child count is below MAX_CHILDREN (32/0x20)\n2. If assertion fails, call FogAssert and terminate via FUN_6fa12bdd(-1)\n3. Calculate descriptor address: g_BnetUIObjectDescriptors + (nDescriptorIndex * 0x30)\n4. Call CreateObjectByTypeFactory with descriptor pointer\n5. Store returned object pointer in g_apSubChildrenArray[g_nNumSubChildren]\n6. Increment g_nNumSubChildren counter\n7. Return (void implicit)\n\nParameters:\n  nDescriptorIndex (ECX): Index into g_BnetUIObjectDescriptors table (48-byte stride)\n\nReturns:\n  void (object pointer stored in global array, not returned)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Asserts if g_nNumSubChildren >= 32 (0x20) - MAX_CHILDREN limit\n  - Assertion message: \"sgnNumSubChildren < MAX_CHILDREN\"\n  - Source file: C:\\Projects\\Diablo2\\Source\\D2Multi\\Src\\... line 0x1086 (4230)\n\nGlobals Used:\n  g_nNumSubChildren (0x6fa21734): Current count of sub-children in array\n  g_apSubChildrenArray (0x6fa20a20): Array of pointers to child UI objects\n  g_BnetUIObjectDescriptors (0x6fa1b150): Table of UI object descriptors (48 bytes each)\n\nStructure Layout (Descriptor):\n  Offset  Size  Description\n  0x00    0x30  Full descriptor record (48 bytes per entry)",
