      "name": "InvokeCallbackIfRegistered",
      "signature": "int InvokeCallbackIfRegistered(int callbackParam)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Invokes a registered callback function if one is set.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load callback function pointer from global address 0x6fa0a0e0\n2. Test if the pointer is null (zero)\n3. If null, skip callback invocation and jump to return\n4. If not null, load parameter from stack [ESP+4]\n5. Push parameter and invoke callback via indirect call\n6. Return success status (1)\n\nParameters:\n  callbackParam (int): Parameter to pass to the callback function if registered\n\nReturns:\n  int: Returns 1 (success) always, regardless of whether callback was invoked\n\nPurpose:\n  This function serves as a dispatch mechanism for registered callbacks. It allows\n  optional callback functionality without requiring a callback to always be set.\n  Used for event handling or optional hook mechanisms.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If no callback is registered (pointer at 0x6fa0a0e0 is null), function returns\n    immediately without invoking anything\n  - Return value is always 1, indicating successful execution whether or not\n    callback was actually invoked",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
