      "comment": "Adds a game entry to the global game list if not already present.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if game already exists by scanning game ID list\n2. If game ID matches existing entry, return early (duplicate check)\n3. Calculate offset for new entry (count * 0x3b stride)\n4. Copy game ID (short at input+0x08) to entry+0x33\n5. Initialize entry+0x37 DWORD to 0\n6. Copy flags (short at input+0x14) to entry+0x31\n7. Copy game name string (from input+0x1c) via strlen + memcpy to entry+0x01\n8. Copy description string (from input+0x2c) via strlen + memcpy to entry+0x11\n9. Increment global game list count\n\nParameters:\n  pGameInfo (ECX) - Pointer to game info structure:\n    +0x08: wGameId (short) - Game type/ID for duplicate detection\n    +0x14: wFlags (short) - Game flags\n    +0x1c: szGameName (char[16]) - Null-terminated game name\n    +0x2c: szDescription (char[16]) - Null-terminated description\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Early return if game ID already exists in list\n  - String copy uses optimized DWORD copy then byte copy for remainder\n\nStructure Layout (GameListEntry, stride 0x3b = 59 bytes):\n  Offset  Size  Field              Type    Description\n  0x00    1     padding            byte    Unused padding\n  0x01    16    szGameName         char[]  Game name string\n  0x11    16    szDescription      char[]  Description string\n  0x31    2     wFlags             short   Game flags from input+0x14\n  0x33    2     wGameId            short   Game ID from input+0x08\n  0x37    4     dwReserved         dword   Initialized to 0\n\nGlobal Data:\n  g_nGameListCount (0x6fa3e9d8) - Current count of games in list\n  g_aGameListEntries (0x6fa30140) - Base of game list array",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
