      "name": "IsValidPrintableCharacter",
      "signature": "int IsValidPrintableCharacter(int unused1, int unused2, char * pCharToValidate)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Validates if a character is a printable ASCII character (0x20-0x7F).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load the character from the pointer at pCharToValidate\n2. Compare character with 0x20 (space, minimum printable ASCII)\n3. If character < 0x20, jump to return_invalid\n4. Sign-extend character value to full integer\n5. Compare with 0x80 (128, minimum non-ASCII)\n6. If character >= 0x80, jump to return_invalid\n7. Character is in valid printable range [0x20-0x7F], return 1 (true)\n8. Invalid character, return 0 (false)\n\nParameters:\n- unused1 (int): Unused parameter (callers may pass variable values)\n- unused2 (int): Unused parameter (callers may pass variable values)\n- pCharToValidate (char *): Pointer to character to validate\n\nReturns:\n- 1 (true) if character is printable ASCII [0x20-0x7F inclusive]\n- 0 (false) if character is outside valid range\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Magic number 0x20: Minimum valid printable character (space)\n- Magic number 0x80: Boundary for ASCII vs extended ASCII (128)\n- Magic number 0x7F: Maximum valid printable character (DEL, though excluded by >= 0x80 check)\n- Unused parameters suggest this function may be part of an interface with fixed signature",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
