      "name": "InitializeBnetPanelState",
      "signature": "bool InitializeBnetPanelState(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "bool",
      "comment": "Initializes Battle.net panel state by resetting inventory and game list controls.\n\nClassification: Initialization/Wrapper function - Called to prepare Battle.net UI panel.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call ResetInventoryPanelState() to clear inventory panel state\n2. Call InitializeGameListPanelControls() to set up game list panel\n3. Reset button frame values for UI objects 7, 8, 9 to 0 (clear button states)\n4. Return TRUE indicating successful initialization\n\nParameters: None\n\nReturns: bool - Always returns TRUE (1)\n\nCallees:\n- ResetInventoryPanelState: Clears inventory slots and resets sub-children\n- InitializeGameListPanelControls: Initializes game list panel UI controls\n- SetButtonFrameValues: Sets button animation frame state\n\nReferences: Referenced from function pointer table at 0x6fa1b290\n\nNote: Function body incorrectly bounded in Ghidra - actual code continues past \nsingle CALL to include all 5 function calls and return.",
