      "name": "ResetInventoryPanelState",
      "signature": "void ResetInventoryPanelState(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Resets the inventory panel state by clearing all inventory slots and sub-children.\n\nClassification: Cleanup function - Called during panel transitions/close operations.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call FUN_6fa10090 to perform initial cleanup\n2. Call FUN_6fa0f490 to perform secondary cleanup\n3. Dispatch inventory item handlers for 8 fixed inventory slots (g_dwInventorySlot1-8)\n4. Set current input item from g_dwCurrentInputItem\n5. Set current input pointer from g_pCurrentInputPointer\n6. Loop through g_apSubChildrenArray dispatching handlers for each sub-child (0 to g_nNumSubChildren-1)\n7. Reset g_nNumSubChildren to 0\n8. Reset current input item from g_dwCurrentInputItem\n9. Reset g_dwInventorySubState to 0\n10. Call FUN_6fa117b0 for additional cleanup\n11. Reset g_dwInventoryExtraState to 0\n12. Dispatch handlers for inventory slots 9 and 10\n13. If g_dwSpecialModeFlag == 1, call FUN_6fa127f0\n14. If g_dwInventoryPanelMode == 3, reset it to 0\n15. If g_pInventoryBitMaskTarget != NULL, call SetOrClearBitMask with value 1\n\nParameters: None\n\nReturns: void\n\nCallers: FUN_6fa08db0, FUN_6fa11510, FUN_6fa11080, FUN_6fa11030, FUN_6fa11a10,\n         FUN_6fa111c0, FUN_6fa07300, FUN_6fa08ae0, FUN_6fa09080 (9 callers total)\n\nGlobals Modified:\n- g_nNumSubChildren: Reset to 0\n- g_dwInventorySubState: Reset to 0\n- g_dwInventoryExtraState: Reset to 0\n- g_dwInventoryPanelMode: Reset to 0 if was 3",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.04b",
      "method": "CAL",
