      "name": "ResetInventoryPanelAndSlots",
      "signature": "void ResetInventoryPanelAndSlots(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Resets all inventory panel state and UI elements to default values.\n\nCalled during inventory panel closure or game state reset. Clears all 10 inventory slots, \nresets sub-children array, clears state flags, and disables all button frames.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call FUN_6fa10090() - auxiliary inventory cleanup\n2. Call FUN_6fa0f490() - secondary inventory cleanup\n3. Dispatch handler for all 8 primary inventory slots (g_dwInventorySlot1-8)\n4. Restore current input item and pointer from globals\n5. Loop through g_apSubChildrenArray dispatching handler for each child (0 to g_nNumSubChildren)\n6. Clear g_nNumSubChildren to 0\n7. Restore current input item again\n8. Clear g_dwInventorySubState to 0\n9. Call FUN_6fa117b0() - tertiary cleanup\n10. Clear g_dwInventoryExtraState to 0\n11. Dispatch handler for inventory slots 9 and 10\n12. If g_dwSpecialModeFlag == 1, call FUN_6fa127f0() (special mode handler)\n13. If g_dwInventoryPanelMode == 3, reset it to 0\n14. If g_pInventoryPanelState != NULL, call SetOrClearBitMask with flag 1\n15. Reset all 4 button frames (g_pButtonFrame1-3, g_pButtonFrame1 again) to frame 0\n16. Clear g_dwInventoryPanelMode to 0\n\nParameters: None\n\nReturns: void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Slot 1-8 are cleared before the sub-children loop\n- Slots 9-10 are cleared after the sub-children loop\n- Button frame 1 is reset twice (possible redundancy or intentional)\n- Special mode handling only triggers when g_dwSpecialModeFlag == 1\n- Panel mode 3 has special reset behavior",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.04b",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:b4487220fabfa234c7f1b0dc3475efa3",
