      "name": "ResetInventoryPanelState",
      "signature": "int ResetInventoryPanelState(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "ResetInventoryPanelState - Resets all inventory panel UI state and button frames\n\nClassification: Cleanup/Reset function - resets inventory UI state to default values\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Reset button frame values to 0 for all button frames (Frame1, Frame2, Frame3)\n2. Check game list data flags at offset 0x1ea for bits 0x08 and 0x04\n3. If either flag bit is clear, set unit bit mask to 1 for Frame2 and Frame3\n4. Set unit bit mask to 1 for Frame1\n5. Set Frame1 bit mask based on g_dwButtonFrame1State (1 if state is 0, else 0)\n6. Call FUN_6fa10090 (likely additional UI reset)\n7. Call FUN_6fa0f490 (likely additional state cleanup)\n8. Dispatch inventory item handlers for all 8 primary inventory slots (1-8)\n9. Set current input item and input pointer from global state\n10. Loop through sub-children array, dispatching handlers for each\n11. Reset g_nNumSubChildren to 0\n12. Set current input item again (refresh)\n13. Reset g_dwInventorySubState to 0\n14. Call FUN_6fa117b0 (likely finalize sub-state)\n15. Reset g_dwInventoryExtraState to 0\n16. Dispatch handlers for inventory slots 9 and 10\n17. If g_dwSpecialModeFlag equals 1, call FUN_6fa127f0\n18. If g_dwInventoryPanelMode equals 3, reset it to 0\n19. If g_pInventoryPanelState is not NULL, set/clear bit mask with value 1\n\nParameters:\n- None (void)\n\nReturns:\n- int: Always returns 1 (success)\n\nGlobals Accessed:\n- g_pButtonFrame1, g_pButtonFrame2, g_pButtonFrame3: Button frame pointers\n- g_pGameListData: Game list data structure (checks flags at offset 0x1ea)\n- g_dwButtonFrame1State: Button frame 1 state flag\n- g_dwInventorySlot1-10: Inventory slot identifiers\n- g_dwCurrentInputItem, g_pCurrentInputPointer: Current input state\n- g_apSubChildrenArray, g_nNumSubChildren: Dynamic sub-children list\n- g_dwInventorySubState, g_dwInventoryExtraState: Inventory state flags\n- g_dwSpecialModeFlag: Special mode indicator\n- g_dwInventoryPanelMode: Panel mode (3 = special state)\n- g_pInventoryPanelState: Inventory panel state pointer\n\nFlag Bits (g_pGameListData + 0x1ea):\n- 0x04: Unknown flag - controls button frame visibility\n- 0x08: Unknown flag - controls button frame visibility\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Sub-children loop only executes if g_nNumSubChildren > 0\n- Special mode handler (FUN_6fa127f0) only called when flag == 1\n- Panel mode reset only when mode == 3\n- Panel state bit mask only set when pointer is non-NULL\n- No callers found - likely called via function pointer table",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.08",
