      "name": "ParseGameNodeDescriptionString",
      "signature": "byte ParseGameNodeDescriptionString(void * this, uint * param_1, uint param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "return_type": "byte",
      "comment": "ParseGameNodeDescriptionString - Parses a game description string and populates game node fields\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate string length of description using strlen loop (SCASB.REPNE pattern)\n2. Clear game node flags field at offset 0x8A to zero\n3. Check dwFlags bits to determine game type code:\n   - Flag 0x02 set: return type 0x11 (Private game)\n   - Flag 0x08 set: return type 0x12\n   - Flag 0x01 set: return type 0x10\n   - Flag 0x04 set: return type 0x15\n   - Flag 0x1400 set: return type 0x13\n   - No flags + short string: return type 0x07 (Unknown)\n4. If string too short (<4 bytes), skip product code parsing\n5. Read 4-byte product code from description start, copy to node offset 0x00\n6. Match product code against known values:\n   - 0x44545354 \"TSDT\": type 0x0A if extended parsing\n   - 0x44325850 \"D2XP\": parse extended D2 format\n   - 0x44324456 \"D2DV\": parse extended D2 format\n   - 0x44325354 \"D2ST\": parse extended D2 format\n   - 0x43484154 \"CHAT\": type 0x14 (Chat)\n   - 0x4452544c \"RLTD\": type 0x0A\n   - 0x44534852 \"RSHR\": type 0x0A\n   - 0x53534852 \"SSHR\": type 0x0D\n   - 0x4a535452 \"RSTR\": type 0x0D\n   - 0x53455850 \"SXEP\": type 0x0E\n   - 0x53544152 \"STAR\": type 0x0D\n   - 0x5732424e \"W2BN\": type 0x0F\n7. For D2 products (D2XP, D2DV, D2ST), parse comma-separated fields:\n   - Field 1 to offset 0x46 (game name)\n   - Field 2 to offset 0x36 (game password?)\n   - DecodeVariableInt14 for value\n   - Copy 11 bytes to offset 0x66 (class data), pad remaining with 0xFF\n   - If class data valid, parse trailer:\n     - Byte at offset 0x86 (adjusted by -1)\n     - Copy 11 bytes to offset 0x76, pad with 0xFF\n     - Byte to offset 0x88 (ushort)\n     - DecodeVariableInt14 to offset 0x8A\n     - DecodeVariableInt14 to offset 0x8C\n     - Bytes to offsets 0x94, 0x95, 0x96 (convert 0xFF to 0)\n8. For unknown products: set code to \"NKNU\", copy node name to offset 0x36\n9. Final loop: initialize 16 bytes at offsets 0x66 and 0x76 with special pattern\n\nParameters:\n  this (ECX)         - void *: Pointer to GameNode structure to populate\n  pszDescription     - char *: Game description string (product code + comma-separated fields)\n  dwFlags            - uint: Flags controlling parsing behavior and type selection\n                       Bit 0x01: Type 0x10\n                       Bit 0x02: Type 0x11 (Private game)\n                       Bit 0x04: Type 0x15\n                       Bit 0x08: Type 0x12\n                       Bit 0x1400: Type 0x13\n\nReturns:\n  byte: Game type classification code (0x07-0x16)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  Product Codes (4-char LE):\n    0x554e4b4e = \"NKNU\" (Unknown product fallback)\n    0x44545354 = \"TSDT\"\n    0x44325850 = \"D2XP\" (Diablo II: Lord of Destruction)\n    0x44324456 = \"D2DV\" (Diablo II)\n    0x44325354 = \"D2ST\" (Diablo II Stress Test?)\n    0x43484154 = \"CHAT\" (Chat channel)\n    0x4452544c = \"RLTD\"\n    0x44534852 = \"RSHR\"\n    0x53534852 = \"SSHR\"\n    0x4a535452 = \"RSTR\"\n    0x53455850 = \"SXEP\"\n    0x53544152 = \"STAR\" (StarCraft)\n    0x5732424e = \"W2BN\" (Warcraft II Battle.net Edition)\n\nGameNode Structure Layout:\n  Offset  Size   Field\n  0x00    4      Product code (DWORD)\n  0x04    0x32   Node name string\n  0x36    0x10   Parsed field 2 / fallback name\n  0x46    0x10   Parsed field 1 (game name)\n  0x66    0x10   Class data array (padded with 0xFF)\n  0x76    0x10   Secondary data array (padded with 0xFF)\n  0x86    1      Class byte (adjusted -1 from input)\n  0x88    2      Trailer byte 1 (ushort)\n  0x8A    2      Flags (short from DecodeVariableInt14)\n  0x8C    2      Value (short from DecodeVariableInt14)\n  0x94    1      Color/attribute byte 1\n  0x95    1      Color/attribute byte 2\n  0x96    1      Color/attribute byte 3",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.08",
