      "name": "ProcessCharSelectChatCallback",
      "signature": "int ProcessCharSelectChatCallback(int nUnused, char * lpszText)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Processes incoming chat text for the character selection screen callback.\n\nCallback function invoked from COM/network callback table to handle chat\nmessages. Converts ANSI text to Unicode, validates length, strips a specific\npattern (string ID 0xF9A), and displays in the character select text box.\n\nClassification: Callback/Handler\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize 576-element Unicode buffer (0x240 = 576) on stack\n2. Convert ANSI lpszText to Unicode using win2Unicode\n3. Check string length < 500 characters\n4. If too long: Assert failure and abort (FogAssert line 740)\n5. Get filter pattern from ValidateStringId(0xF9A) via EAX\n6. Search for pattern occurrences in converted text\n7. For each occurrence found (while not at string end):\n   a. Calculate remaining string length after pattern\n   b. Shift remaining text left to overwrite pattern (Unicode_memmove)\n   c. Search for next occurrence\n8. Add processed text to character select text box (context=3)\n9. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\n  nUnused - Unused callback parameter (always ignored)\n  lpszText - ANSI string containing chat message text\n\nReturns:\n  1 - Success (text processed and displayed)\n  Does not return if string too long (assert failure)\n\nLocal Variables (decompiler names):\n  aUStack_480 (awszUnicodeBuffer) - 576-char Unicode buffer for converted text\n  iVar3 (nCounter/nPatternLen) - Loop counter / pattern string length\n  pUVar2 (pwszIterator) - Current position in Unicode buffer\n  iVar1 (nRemainingLen) - Length of string after pattern match\n  extraout_EAX (pwszFilterPattern) - Filter pattern from ValidateStringId\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - String length >= 500: Triggers FogAssert and aborts\n  - Empty pattern match: Loop terminates when pattern followed by null\n  - Multiple pattern occurrences: All removed in single pass\n\nGlobals Accessed:\n  szAssertUnicodeStrlenLimit (0x6fa1d8c4) - Assert message for length check\n  szPathComCallbackCpp (0x6fa1d7fc) - Source file path for assert\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x240 (576) - Unicode buffer size in characters\n  500 - Maximum allowed string length\n  0xF9A (3994) - String ID for filter pattern\n  3 - Text box context value (color/formatting)\n  0x2e4 (740) - Source line number for assert\n\nCross-References:\n  Referenced from callback table at 0x6fa1d7b4\n  Calls: Unicode::win2Unicode, Unicode::strlen, ValidateStringId\n  Calls: Unicode::strstr, Unicode_memmove, CharSelectTextBoxAddText\n  Calls: FogAssert, FUN_6fa12bdd (abort)\n\nNote: Function body incomplete in Ghidra listing (only entry instruction).\nDecompiler analysis is speculative. Variables cannot be renamed due to\nmissing function body definition. See script RecreateFunction_6fa0d6d0.java\nto fix the function body if needed.",
