      "name": "FetchAndFilterGameListByDifficulty",
      "signature": "void FetchAndFilterGameListByDifficulty(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Fetches game list from callback vtable and filters by player difficulty level.\nCalled during multiplayer game list refresh to populate the visible game list\nwith games matching the player's current difficulty setting.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call callback vtable function at offset 0x38 to get raw game list data\n2. Return early if no data returned (NULL pointer)\n3. Extract game count from first dword and store in g_nGameListCount\n4. Initialize filtered entry counter (nFilteredCount) to 0\n5. For each game entry in the raw list:\n   a. Set entry flag word to 1 at (pnDestEntry - 2)\n   b. Copy game ID from source[3] to pnDestEntry[0]\n   c. Calculate string length using REPNE SCASB (strlen equivalent)\n   d. Copy game name string to (pnDestEntry - 0x36) using MOVSD.REP/MOVSB.REP\n   e. If g_pTextControl not NULL, convert game name to Unicode\n   f. Assert game name pointer is valid, exit on failure\n   g. Skip past game name string (find null terminator)\n   h. Skip past second string (description), find difficulty byte\n   i. Extract difficulty level byte after second string\n   j. Calculate max difficulty threshold: ((flags & 0x1f00) / 0x500) + 1\n   k. Apply difficulty filter:\n      - If expansion bit (0x04) NOT set: filter if (difficulty - '0') > threshold\n      - If expansion bit set: filter if (difficulty - '3') > threshold, or if difficulty <= '2'\n   l. If game passes filter: copy description, increment nFilteredCount, advance pnDestEntry by 0x3b\n   m. If game filtered out: decrement g_nGameListCount\n   n. Skip past remaining string to next entry\n6. Call FUN_6fa0edb0 to finalize the filtered game list display\n\nParameters: None (uses global state)\n\nReturns: void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- NULL game list data from callback: exits immediately after cleanup call\n- NULL string pointers during parsing: triggers FogAssert and exits with code -1\n- Difficulty filtering differs between expansion (bit 4 set) and classic modes\n- Classic mode: difficulty characters '0'-'9' where '0' is Normal\n- Expansion mode: difficulty characters '3'-'9' where '3' is Normal\n\nStructure Layout (Game Entry - 0x3b bytes stride):\nOffset  Size  Field           Description\n-0x38   2     wEntryFlag      Entry validity flag (set to 1)\n-0x36   50    szGameName      Null-terminated game name string\n0x00    4     dwGameId        Game ID from source data\n+0x11   ?     szDescription   Game description string (copied from source)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x38 - Offset to GetGameList function in callback vtable\n0x3b - Stride between game list entries (59 bytes)\n0x1ea - Offset to difficulty flags in g_pGameListData\n0x1f00 - Mask for difficulty level bits (bits 8-12)\n0x500 - Division factor for difficulty level calculation\n0x04 - Expansion mode flag bit\n0x30 - ASCII '0' for classic difficulty base\n0x33 - ASCII '3' for expansion difficulty base\n0x32 - ASCII '2' for filtering expansion games in classic mode",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.08",
