      "name": "ProcessGameJoinRequest",
      "signature": "int ProcessGameJoinRequest(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "ProcessGameJoinRequest - Processes a game join request from the Battle.net multiplayer UI.\n\nThis function handles the user's request to join a game by name. It retrieves the game name\nand password from the UI edit boxes, validates the input, searches for matching games in\nthe local cache or via callback, verifies difficulty requirements, and initiates the join.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call GetUnitBitMask on game list container to validate UI state\n2. Return 0 if validation fails\n3. Get game name Unicode string from g_pGameNameEditBox via D2Win_GetEditBoxChild\n4. Get password Unicode string from g_pPasswordEditBox via D2Win_GetEditBoxChild\n5. Return 0 if game name is NULL\n6. Convert game name from Unicode to ANSI (local_200, 256 bytes max)\n7. Convert password from Unicode to ANSI (local_100, 256 bytes max)\n8. Apply TitleCaseString to both game name and password\n9. Call Ordinal_10002 to check direct join path (MCP connection check)\n10. If Ordinal_10002 returns non-zero:\n    a. Call InitializeGameJoinSession with port=0, game name, password\n    b. Dispatch cleanup handlers for 11 UI controls\n    c. Set current input item to g_apBnetUIObjects[10]\n    d. Display string 0x147b via ValidateStringId\n    e. Return 1 (success)\n11. Search local game list (g_aGameListEntriesDest) for matching game name:\n    a. Loop through g_nGameListCount entries (stride 0x3B bytes)\n    b. Compare each entry name at offset +1 with local_200 using inline strcmp\n    c. If match found:\n       - Extract IP address from offset +0x37 (g_aGameListIpAddrs)\n       - Extract port from offset +0x33 (g_awGameListPorts)\n       - Call InetNtoaToStaticBuffer with IP address\n       - Call InitializeGameJoinSession with port, game name, password\n       - Dispatch cleanup handlers, return 1\n12. If not in local cache, query callback vtable at offset 0x38:\n    a. Call g_pCallbackVtable[0x38] to get game info struct\n    b. If result NULL or count <= 0, goto failure\n    c. Extract IP address from struct offset +0x10 (in_addr union)\n    d. Extract port from struct offset +0x1D (stored in uStack_209)\n    e. Copy game name string to abStack_23b (16 bytes)\n    f. Skip to next null-terminated field (password/description)\n    g. Skip to difficulty byte field\n13. Validate difficulty requirements:\n    a. Read player flags from g_pGameListData+0x1EA\n    b. Calculate max allowed difficulty: ((flags & 0x1F00) / 0x500) + 1\n    c. If expansion bit (0x4) not set:\n       - Compare game difficulty (byte - 0x30) vs max allowed\n       - Fail if game difficulty > max allowed\n    d. If expansion bit set:\n       - Compare game difficulty (byte - 0x33) vs max allowed\n       - Also check byte >= 0x33 (Hell requirement)\n       - Fail if either check fails\n14. Copy description string to acStack_22b (34 bytes)\n15. Compare game name from callback with user's input (local_200)\n16. If names don't match, return 0\n17. If match, join game via InetNtoaToStaticBuffer + InitializeGameJoinSession\n18. Dispatch cleanup handlers and return 1\n\nFailure Path (LAB_6fa10e9f):\n- Display error string 0x1411 via ValidateStringId\n- Call InitSubPanelUI to show error panel\n- Return 0\n\nParameters: None (uses global UI state)\n\nReturns:\n  1 - Game join initiated successfully\n  0 - Join failed (validation, no match, or difficulty mismatch)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- NULL game name returns 0 immediately\n- Empty/invalid game list container returns 0\n- Difficulty validation differs for expansion vs classic:\n  - Classic: difficulty byte - 0x30 (ASCII '0')\n  - Expansion: difficulty byte - 0x33 (ASCII '3')\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x3B (59): Stride of game list entry structure\n- 0x100 (256): Max string buffer size for game name/password\n- 0x1F00: Difficulty level mask in player flags\n- 0x500 (1280): Difficulty divisor\n- 0x4: Expansion flag bit in player flags\n- 0x1EA (490): Offset to player flags in g_pGameListData\n- 0x147B (5243): String ID for successful join message\n- 0x1411 (5137): String ID for join failure message\n\nGlobal Data:\n- g_pGameListContainer: UI container for game list\n- g_pGameNameEditBox: Edit box for game name input\n- g_pPasswordEditBox: Edit box for password input\n- g_nGameListCount: Number of games in local cache\n- g_aGameListEntriesDest: Array of cached game list entries\n- g_awGameListPorts: Port numbers array at entry offset +0x33\n- g_aGameListIpAddrs: IP addresses at entry offset +0x37\n- g_pCallbackVtable: Callback vtable for network queries\n- g_pGameListData: Player/game state data structure\n- g_apBnetUIObjects[10]: Target UI object for input focus",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.08",
