      "name": "ResetGameListPanelButtonStates",
      "signature": "bool ResetGameListPanelButtonStates(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "bool",
      "comment": "Resets the Battle.net game list panel button states and clears difficulty level.\n\nClassification: Initialization function (UI reset)\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Set g_pBnetGameListPanel button frame to 1 (active/selected state)\n2. Set g_pBnetGameListScrollUp button frame to 0 (inactive)\n3. Set g_pBnetGameListScrollDown button frame to 0 (inactive)\n4. Clear g_nDifficultyLevel to 0\n5. Clear byte at offset 0x20B in g_pGameListData structure (filter/state flag)\n6. Return TRUE\n\nParameters:\n- pUnused (void *): Unused parameter, passed on stack (stdcall convention)\n\nReturns:\n- bool: Always returns TRUE (1)\n\nGlobals Modified:\n- g_nDifficultyLevel (0x6fa3e9dc): Set to 0\n- g_pGameListData->field_20B: Set to 0\n\nCalled By: UI initialization routines, panel state reset handlers\n\nNote: Function body appears malformed in Ghidra (single instruction).\nActual code spans 0x6fa110d0-0x6fa11122 based on byte analysis.",
