      "name": "InitializeProfileCreationPanel",
      "signature": "void InitializeProfileCreationPanel(char * lpszChannelName, char * lpszCharacterName, dword dwSlotIndex, dword dwSlotParam)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Initializes the profile creation panel UI for Battle.net character profile editing.\n\nCalled when user selects a game slot to create or edit a character profile. Sets up\nall UI elements including text input fields, labels, and buttons for profile data entry.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Strip channel name prefix from lpszChannelName via SkipChannelNamePrefix\n2. Reset button frame states for UI objects 6-9 to disabled (value 0)\n3. Call ShowProfileSexSelectionPanel to parse profile data into local buffers:\n   - szSexBuffer: character sex/gender\n   - szAgeBuffer: character age\n   - szLocationBuffer: character location\n   - abDescriptionBuffer: multi-line description text\n4. If parsing fails (returns 0), exit early\n5. Reset inventory panel state and set g_dwProfileEditState = 1\n6. Create 6 profile edit items via CreateObjectByTypeFactory:\n   - Item1: Base profile object\n   - Item2: Parsed channel name (converted to Unicode)\n   - Item3: Sex field (converted to Unicode)\n   - Item4: Age field (converted to Unicode)\n   - Item5: Location field (converted to Unicode)\n   - Item6: Description lines container\n7. Parse description buffer by CRLF delimiter (\\r\n):\n   - Loop calling FUN_6fa13275 (strtok-like) until NULL returned\n   - Each line converted to Unicode and added to Item6\n8. Create profile unknown object and set as current input item\n9. If g_dwButtonFrame1State == 0, create optional button\n10. Create 6 label UI objects with localized string IDs:\n    - 0x1493: Label 1 (Sex prompt)\n    - 0x1494: Label 2 (Age prompt)\n    - 0x1495: Label 3 (Location prompt)\n    - 0x1496: Label 4 (Description prompt)\n    - 0x1497: Label 5 (Additional field)\n    - 0x1492: Title label\n11. Restore default input pointer\n12. Copy lpszCharacterName to g_szProfileCharacterName using optimized memcpy:\n    - strlen via REPNE SCASB\n    - Copy DWORDs via REP MOVSD\n    - Copy remaining bytes via REP MOVSB\n13. Store dwSlotIndex and dwSlotParam to globals\n\nParameters:\n  lpszChannelName (ECX): Channel name with optional prefix to strip\n  lpszCharacterName (EDX): Character name to store for profile\n  dwSlotIndex (Stack+0x4): Game slot index being edited\n  dwSlotParam (Stack+0x8): Additional slot parameter\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Early exit if ShowProfileSexSelectionPanel returns 0 (parsing failure)\n- Optional button creation only if g_dwButtonFrame1State == 0\n\nString IDs:\n  0x1492: Profile title\n  0x1493-0x1497: Field labels (Sex, Age, Location, Description, Additional)\n\nDecompiler Artifacts:\n  extraout_var (undefined3): Phantom variable from CONCAT31 for extended return check - not renameable",
