      "name": "FormatChannelEventMessage",
      "signature": "int FormatChannelEventMessage(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "FormatChannelEventMessage - Formats locale-specific Battle.net channel event messages for display\n\nWARNING: Function boundaries incomplete. Actual body: 0x6fa0d8d0-0x6fa0d9cd (253 bytes).\nDelete and recreate function in Ghidra to enable full decompilation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load nDisplayFlags parameter from stack [ESP+8] into EAX\n2. Allocate 0x674 byte (1652) stack frame for wide string buffers\n3. Save callee-saved registers EBP, ESI, EDI onto stack\n4. Push format string pointer (e.g., \"The channel \"%s\" is full...\")\n5. Call Unicode string copy/conversion routine to prepare source\n6. Initialize loop counter EDI to 0x240 (576) for wide char processing\n7. Loop: Call string operation via IAT at 0x6fa19040\n8. Advance source pointer ESI by 2 (sizeof wchar_t), decrement EDI\n9. Continue loop until EDI reaches zero\n10. Call memory allocator for output buffer (SMemAlloc-style)\n11. Compare string length result against 0x1F4 (500) max length\n12. If length >= 500: Format and copy message to output, set return 1\n13. If length < 500: Load error message resources, call error handler\n14. Restore registers EBP, ESI, EDI from stack\n15. Deallocate stack frame (ADD ESP, 0x674)\n16. Return to caller with RET 8 (callee cleans 2 DWORD params)\n\nParameters:\n  nLocaleIndex (int, Stack[0x4]): Index selecting locale string resource table entry\n  nDisplayFlags (int, Stack[0x8]): Formatting flags controlling message output style\n\nReturns:\n  int: 1 on successful message formatting\n  int: Error code if formatting fails or buffer exceeds 500 chars\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Max output length 500 chars (0x1F4) enforced\n  - Uses wide character conversion internally for Unicode support\n  - Called via function pointer table, not direct call\n\nCalled From:\n  Function pointer table at 0x6fa1d7d0 (Battle.net channel event dispatch)\n\nString Resources:\n  0x6fa1d9b0: \"The channel \"%s\" is full...\"\n  0x6fa1d8e4: \"%s has joined the channel.\"\n  0x6fa1d8fe: \"%s has left the channel.\"\n  0x6fa1d918: \"You have joined channel: %s\"",
