      "name": "ReleaseAllResources",
      "signature": "void ReleaseAllResources(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Releases and nullifies all cached game resources.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save ESI register (non-volatile, used for zero constant)\n2. Initialize ESI to 0 (used as comparison constant)\n3. For each of 53 resource pointers in global memory:\n   a. Load resource pointer from global address into ECX\n   b. Compare pointer against 0 to check if allocated\n   c. Jump to next resource if pointer is null\n   d. Call ReleaseResourceAndNotify with pointer in ECX\n   e. Store 0 to global address to nullify pointer\n4. Restore ESI register\n5. Return to caller\n\nReturns: void\n\nThis function ensures complete cleanup of all game resources by checking each pointer before release, preventing attempts to release null or stale pointers. The repetitive pattern suggests it was generated from an array of global resource pointers spanning memory range 0x6fa09f40 to 0x6fa0a088.",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "API",
