      "name": "InitializeModuleList",
      "signature": "void InitializeModuleList(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Iterates through linked list of game modules and initializes each one.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load module list head pointer from DAT_6fa0a0f0\n2. If list is empty (head is NULL), skip loop and go to cleanup\n3. Enter loop to process each module node:\n   - Load next node pointer from current node's offset +0x204\n   - Call InitializeModule(0x1b75, 0) to initialize the module type 0x1b75\n4. Continue loop until current node pointer becomes NULL\n5. Clear the module list head pointer (set DAT_6fa0a0f0 to 0)\n6. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nNone (void function)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Empty list: If DAT_6fa0a0f0 is NULL on entry, loop is skipped entirely\n- Module list cleanup: Head pointer is explicitly zeroed after initialization\n- Magic value 0x1b75: Module type identifier passed to InitializeModule\n\nStructure Layout:\nThe module nodes form a singly-linked list with offset +0x204 containing\nthe next node pointer. Each node is processed sequentially until a NULL\npointer is encountered.",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:23c92ea1f1223735f85688a6eb44c1d5",
