      "name": "InitializeObjectStateAndModify",
      "signature": "void InitializeObjectStateAndModify(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Initializes object state and applies bitfield modifications.\\n\\nThis function performs a two-phase initialization sequence:\\n1. Loads a state configuration value from a global memory location (0x6fa09fa8)\\n2. Sets this value as a structure field using the SetStructureFieldDword wrapper\\n3. Applies bitfield modifications to the object via ModifyObjectBitfield\\n4. Performs a tail call to the actual handler function via indirect jump\\n\\nThe function uses __stdcall convention with implicit parameter passing through ESI register and operates as a thunk that routes to dynamically determined handler code.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Load configuration value from DAT_6fa09fa8 into EAX\\n2. Push EAX and ESI as parameters for SetStructureFieldDword\\n3. Call SetStructureFieldDword to apply the configuration\\n4. Zero EDX register (implicit parameter for ModifyObjectBitfield)\\n5. Load ESI into ECX (implicit this/context pointer)\\n6. Tail jump to handler at 0x6f9d7c14 (which loads from DAT_6f9e61cc)",
