      "name": "ValidateGameEntityModes",
      "signature": "void ValidateGameEntityModes(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Validates and synchronizes entity modes for core game entities.\n\nThis function ensures all managed entities have current mode states. It processes\na fixed set of 6 primary entities and conditionally processes 2 additional entities\nbased on a global flag. This is typically called during game initialization or\nstate refresh operations.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load first primary entity pointer from 0x6fa09fd4 and validate its mode (EDX=0)\n2. Load second primary entity pointer from 0x6fa09fd8 and validate its mode (EDX=0)\n3. Load third primary entity pointer from 0x6fa09fdc and validate its mode (EDX=0)\n4. Load fourth primary entity pointer from 0x6fa09fe0 and validate its mode (EDX=0)\n5. Load fifth primary entity pointer from 0x6fa09fe4 and validate its mode (EDX=0)\n6. Load sixth primary entity pointer from 0x6fa09fe8 and validate its mode (EDX=0)\n7. Test global flag at 0x6f9e9c44 for extended entity processing\n8. If flag is set, load seventh entity pointer from 0x6fa09fec and validate mode\n9. If flag is set, load eighth entity pointer from 0x6fa09ff0 and validate mode\n10. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\nNone - Function operates on global entity pointers and flags.\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Global flag at 0x6f9e9c44 controls processing of extended entities 7-8\n- When flag is 0, only primary 6 entities are processed\n- EDX parameter is always 0 when calling ValidateAndSetEntityMode\n- All entity pointers loaded from consecutive memory addresses in data section",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "API",
