      "name": "FinalizeGameStateUpdate",
      "signature": "void FinalizeGameStateUpdate(void * pDataBuffer, int statusFlags, int contextFlags)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Finalizes game state after dispatching handlers and updates timeout timestamp.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if state condition flag (DAT_6fa0a03c) is enabled\n2. If disabled: skip all state finalization and exit immediately\n3. If enabled: copy data buffer to global state location using CopyMemoryWithAlignment with size 0x7fffffff\n4. Calculate status flags based on contextFlags and statusFlags parameters:\n   - If contextFlags is zero: statusFlags determines value (9 if nonzero, else 0)\n   - If contextFlags is nonzero: status value is 0x13 if statusFlags is zero, else 0x0b (8)\n5. Store calculated status value in DAT_6f9e9c50 and DAT_6f9e9c58 (duplicate write)\n6. Initialize timeout counters: DAT_6f9e9c54 and DAT_6f9e9c5c both set to 0xffffffff\n7. Call ExportDataWithEncoding with contextFlags parameter\n8. Get current system tick count via GetTickCount\n9. Calculate timeout deadline: current_ticks + 1000ms\n10. Store timeout deadline in DAT_6fa0a098\n11. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\n- pDataBuffer (EBX): Memory region to be copied (size parameter for CopyMemoryWithAlignment)\n- statusFlags (ESI): Status condition flag (zero or nonzero)\n- contextFlags (EDI): Context identifier (zero or nonzero), passed to ExportDataWithEncoding\n\nReturns:\n- void: No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Global flag DAT_6fa0a03c acts as master enable for all state finalization\n- Function uses unaffected register parameters (__stdcall) passed by caller ProcessGameStateDispatch\n- Timeout is always set to current_time + 1000ms regardless of parameter values\n- Status flag calculation creates two possible states (0x09 or 0x00 when EDI=0, 0x13 when EDI!=0 and ESI=0, 0x0b when EDI!=0 and ESI!=0)\n- Memory copy uses maximum size (0x7fffffff) suggesting copy size determined elsewhere",
