      "name": "StoreGameState",
      "signature": "void StoreGameState(void * this, byte stateValue)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Stores game state values into global state variables.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load state value parameter from stack at [ESP + 0x4]\n2. Store state byte value into global DAT_6f9e9c50\n3. Store implicit this pointer (ECX register) into global DAT_6f9e9c54\n4. Return to caller with 1 stack parameter popped (RET 0x4)\n\nParameters:\n  stateValue (byte): State byte to store, typically a game mode or state flag\n\nReturns:\n  void: Function stores values in globals and returns normally\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - This function uses __thiscall convention with implicit this pointer in ECX\n  - The this pointer (ECX) represents the game context or object instance\n  - Global DAT_6f9e9c50 stores the state byte value for subsequent access\n  - Global DAT_6f9e9c54 stores the context pointer for state machine transitions\n\nStructure Layout:\n  Global locations used for state management:\n  Address        Size  Purpose\n  0x6f9e9c50     1     Current state value (byte)\n  0x6f9e9c54     4     Context pointer or object reference",
