      "name": "EnqueueGameCommand",
      "signature": "void EnqueueGameCommand(uint commandIndex)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Enqueues a game command into the command queue.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Check if queue counter exceeds maximum (0x1f/31)\\n2. If exceeded, trigger cleanup and abort with error code -1\\n3. Calculate command table entry address using commandIndex * 0x30\\n4. Call ProcessGameCommand with command pointer\\n5. Store result in command output array at queue counter offset\\n6. Increment queue counter\\n\\nParameters:\\ncommandIndex - Index into command table to process (in EAX)\\n\\nReturns:\\nvoid - Function always terminates or enqueues command\\n\\nSpecial Cases:\\n- Max queue size is 32 entries (0x20)\\n- Command table stride is 0x30 bytes per entry\\n- Queue counter stored at global 0x6fa09f24\\n- Command results array at 0x6fa08e80\\n\\nStructure Layout:\\nCommand Queue Counter: 0x6fa09f24 (uint, 1 entry)\\nCommand Results: 0x6fa08e80 (uint[32], 128 bytes total)\\nCommand Table: 0x6f9e9d30 (48-byte stride)",
