      "name": "FindPathPatternInString",
      "signature": "int FindPathPatternInString(char * pSearchString, int normalizedPathHash, int substringLength)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Searches for a path pattern within a string by testing substrings at valid boundaries.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Return 0 if substringLength is 0 (empty substring)\n2. Calculate full string length using CalculateStringLength()\n3. Compute valid search range (stringLength - substringLength)\n4. Return 0 if range is negative (substring longer than string)\n5. For each position from 0 to maximum valid position:\n   a. Check left boundary: position 0 or previous character must not be alphanumeric\n   b. Check right boundary: if position+substring reaches end OR next character must not be alphanumeric\n   c. If boundaries valid: temporarily null-terminate at substring end\n   d. Call NormalizePathString() on substring starting at position\n   e. Restore original character at substring end\n   f. If normalized hash matches normalizedPathHash, return 1 (success)\n6. Return 0 if no match found after checking all positions\n\nParameters:\n  pSearchString: Pointer to null-terminated string to search in\n  normalizedPathHash: Hash value to match (from NormalizePathString)\n  substringLength: Length of substring to extract and test\n\nReturns:\n  1 if a substring matching the normalized hash is found at a valid boundary\n  0 if no match found or substringLength is 0\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Boundaries are enforced: substring must be preceded/followed by non-alphanumeric characters\n  - This prevents partial path matching (e.g., won't match \"path\" in \"mypath\")\n  - The function temporarily modifies the string during testing but restores original characters\n  - Used for path pattern validation in command processing",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
