      "name": "CleanupUIAndResources",
      "signature": "int CleanupUIAndResources(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Cleanup UI controls and global resources before shutdown.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Load global UI control array pointer from 0x6fa0a0d0\\n2. Initialize EDX to zero (parameter for callback processing)\\n3. Process unicode/callback handlers for cleanup\\n4. Destroy all UI control array entries and free memory\\n5. Return success code (1) to indicate cleanup completed\\n\\nParameters:\\nNone - operates on global UI control state\\n\\nReturns:\\n1 (int) - Success code indicating cleanup completed\\n\\nSpecial Cases:\\nThis function is part of the UI shutdown sequence and must be called before\\napplication exit. The global UI control pointer at 0x6fa0a0d0 is accessed\\ndirectly without parameter passing, indicating it's a static singleton resource.\\nBoth ProcessUnicodeWithCallback and DestroyUIControlArray modify global state.",
