      "name": "DisplayAndClearActiveResource",
      "signature": "int DisplayAndClearActiveResource(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Displays and clears the currently active resource.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load the active resource state pointer from the global resource state table\n2. Test if the resource pointer is null (inactive)\n3. If resource is null, jump to return_success and return 1\n4. If resource is active, call ClearResourceState to deallocate it\n5. Load the text parameter from ESP + 0x4 (passed via stack)\n6. Load the active resource pointer again\n7. Push parameters for text rendering: color=3, X=0, Y=0\n8. Call RenderTextBoxUnicodeText to display the resource text\n9. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nint - Always returns 1 (success)\n\nNotes:\nThe function checks a global resource state (DAT_6fa0a0d4) which acts as a handle \nfor the currently active resource. If a resource is active, the function performs \ncleanup and renders its associated text box with specific formatting (color code 3).\nThe RET 0x4 instruction suggests a hidden parameter passed via stack.",
