      "name": "DequeueThreadSafeItem",
      "signature": "int DequeueThreadSafeItem(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Thread-safe dequeue operation that retrieves and removes the first item from a global linked-list queue.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Acquire critical section lock for thread-safe access\n2. Load current queue head pointer from global variable DAT_6fa0a0e8\n3. If queue is not empty, save the item and advance queue head to next item\n4. Release critical section lock\n5. Return the dequeued item (or 0 if queue was empty)\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nint - Pointer to dequeued queue node, or 0 if queue is empty\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Returns 0 when queue is empty (DAT_6fa0a0e8 is NULL)\n- Uses offset +0xc within node structure as \"next\" pointer field\n- Critical section ensures atomic operation in multi-threaded context\n\nStructure Layout:\nQueue Node structure (inferred from offset +0xc):\nOffset  Size  Field Name  Type     Description\n0       ?     ...         ?        Node data/payload\n0xc     4     pNext       void*    Pointer to next node in queue",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
