      "comment": "Creates a linked list node structure for queue management\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 0xc bytes from memory pool (0xc17 byte allocation)\n2. Initialize all four fields (offsets 0, 4, 8, C) to zero\n3. If allocation succeeded:\n   a. If pStringData is NULL: store nParam1 at offset +4, nParam2 at offset +8, NULL at offset +0\n   b. If pStringData is non-NULL:\n      - Call CalculateStringLength(pStringData) to determine string size\n      - Allocate 0xc22 bytes for string buffer\n      - If string buffer allocated: copy pStringData content into buffer (max 0x7fffffff bytes)\n      - Store buffer pointer at offset +0\n      - Store nParam1 at offset +4, nParam2 at offset +8\n4. Return pointer to initialized node or NULL if initial allocation failed\n\nParameters:\n  nParam1: First integer parameter (stored at node offset +4)\n  nParam2: Second integer parameter (stored at node offset +8)\n\nReturns:\n  Pointer to allocated and initialized node structure (12+ bytes)\n  NULL if initial memory allocation fails (0xc17 bytes)\n\nNode Structure Layout:\n  Offset 0 (4 bytes): Pointer to string buffer or NULL\n  Offset 4 (4 bytes): First parameter (nParam1)\n  Offset 8 (4 bytes): Second parameter (nParam2)\n  Offset C (4 bytes): Reserved/Next pointer (initialized to 0)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If pStringData is NULL, only stores integer parameters without allocating string buffer\n  - If string buffer allocation fails (0xc22), string pointer remains NULL but function succeeds\n  - All initial fields cleared to zero before use\n  - Memory is allocated from tracking pool for lifecycle management",
