      "name": "RenderTextWithLineBreaks",
      "signature": "void RenderTextWithLineBreaks(char * pText, int renderFlags)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Renders multi-line text by splitting on newlines and rendering each line separately.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate text length by scanning for null terminator\n2. If text is empty (length <= 1), render empty line and return\n3. If first character is null, skip to empty string handling\n4. For each line in text:\n   a. Scan from current position to find next newline (0x0A)\n   b. If newline found, replace with null terminator\n   c. Render the line using RenderTextBoxWithUnicodeConversion\n   d. If renderFlags is non-zero, render an additional line break\n   e. Restore the newline character in the original string\n   f. Move to next line\n\nParameters:\n- pText: Pointer to text string with embedded newlines (passed in EAX)\n- renderContext: Rendering context passed to RenderTextBoxWithUnicodeConversion (EBX implicit)\n- renderFlags: If non-zero, adds extra line between each rendered line\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Empty string (length <= 1): Renders once with empty string\n- String without newlines: Renders the entire string once\n- Text is modified in-place (newlines replaced with nulls during render)\n- Uses local variable EDI to track newline positions for restoration\n- The renderContext parameter (EBX) is passed as implicit register parameter\n\nStructure Layout:\nThe function modifies the input string temporarily by replacing newlines with nulls.\nNo permanent data structures are accessed.",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "API",
