      "comment": "Converts a time value to milliseconds using 64-bit multiplication.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Add offset constant (0xb6109100) to input timeValue\n2. Set EDX register based on comparison with constant (0x49ef6eff)\n3. Perform 64-bit multiplication by 10,000,000 (0x989680)\n4. Store resulting 64-bit milliseconds value at output buffer\n\nParameters:\ntimeValue (uint): Input time value to be converted\n\nReturns:\nVoid - Result stored as 64-bit value via ESI pointer\n\nSpecial Cases:\nOffset constant (0xb6109100) suggests this handles epoch-based timestamps\nMultiplication by 10,000,000 converts to milliseconds with high precision\nUses __allmul for 64-bit multiplication to handle overflow",
