      "name": "DestroyAllUIControls",
      "signature": "void DestroyAllUIControls(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Destroys all UI controls in the game interface\n\nCleans up UI control resources by iterating through a control pointer array and\ncalling DestroyUIControl on each non-null element. Then destroys an additional\ncontrol stored in a separate global variable.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize ESI to point to start of UI control pointer array at 0x6fa0912c\n2. Loop through control pointers:\n   - Check if pointer is non-null\n   - If non-null, call DestroyUIControl to free resources and set pointer to 0\n   - Increment ESI by 4 bytes (next pointer)\n   - Continue until ESI >= 0x6fa09130 (end of array)\n3. Load global control pointer from 0x6fa09f7c into EAX\n4. If pointer is non-null, call DestroyUIControl and set to 0\n5. Return to caller\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function performs cleanup only, no return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Control pointer array: 0x6fa0912c to 0x6fa09130 (4-byte elements, 1 pointer)\n- Individual control: 0x6fa09f7c (separate from array)\n- Null pointers are skipped without attempting destruction\n- Destruction zeros the pointer after cleanup",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:c1de6ed0ed2cfd1fff472a8291886567",
