      "name": "DispatchCommandHandler",
      "signature": "void DispatchCommandHandler(void * this, int commandId, wchar_t * pOutputBuffer)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Command dispatcher that routes command IDs to specific handlers and copies results to output buffer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load command ID from EAX parameter (values 0-6, default for >6)\n2. Compare command ID against upper bound of 6\n3. If command ID > 6, jump to default handler\n4. Otherwise, use command ID as index into jump table at 0x6f9d8e30\n5. For each case (0-7):\n   a. Load magic number specific to command into ECX (0xfab, 0xfaa, 0xfa9, 0xfa8, 0xfa7, 0x2771, 0x2772, 0x1507)\n   b. Call dispatch_command_handler(magicNumber) with magic in ECX\n   c. Receive string pointer in EAX from handler\n   d. Store handler result in EDX\n   e. Load destination buffer pointer from ESI into ECX\n   f. Call Unicode::strcpy(ECX, EDX) to copy result string to output buffer\n6. Return via JMP to common exit point at 0x6f9e6048 (indirect jump table lookup)\n\nParameters:\n- commandId (EAX): Command identifier (0-6 for specific handlers, >6 uses default)\n- pOutputBuffer (ESI): Destination buffer for handler result string (wchar_t*)\n\nReturns:\n- void (result written to pOutputBuffer via Unicode::strcpy)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Magic numbers appear to be internal command identifiers: 0xfab-0xfa7 (4011-4007 in decimal) for commands 0-4, 0x2771-0x2772 (10097-10098) for commands 5-6, 0x1507 (5383) for default\n- Command IDs >= 7 route to default handler with magic 0x1507\n- Each case follows identical pattern: load magic, call handler, copy result\n- Exit via shared indirect jump at 0x6f9e6048 suggests return is handled via jump table lookup, not typical RET",
