      "name": "CleanupScreenshot",
      "signature": "void CleanupScreenshot(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Cleans up and releases the global screenshot node resource.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load the global screenshot node pointer from DAT_6fa09f38\n2. Test if the pointer is non-null (already initialized)\n3. If non-null, call CleanupScreenshotNode with the node pointer and flag=1\n4. Zero out the global screenshot node pointer to prevent use-after-free\n5. Return to caller\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value. Safely clears screenshot resources.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If DAT_6fa09f38 is already null, skips cleanup call (already freed)\n- Always zeros the global pointer after cleanup to prevent dangling references\n- Uses __stdcall calling convention (callee cleanup)",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
