      "name": "ProcessGameObjectInitialization",
      "signature": "void ProcessGameObjectInitialization(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Initializes game object with validation and property setup.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load state flags from ESI+0x3c7 and check bit 0x4 (DISABLED flag)\n2. Test bit 0x8 (FROZEN flag) and jump to computation if set\n3. Call FindAndValidateD2ExpMpq to validate object expansion requirement\n4. If validation fails, check threshold at ESI+0x1ea against value 0x5\n5. If threshold check passes (NC), set initialization flag EDI to 0x1, else 0x5\n6. Load game type byte from ESI+0x1ea into EDX\n7. Compute pointers to property arrays: ESI+0x39d and ESI+0x3ad\n8. Call ComputeParameterValue with (edx, edi, array1_ptr, array2_ptr)\n9. Test result and store at global 0x6fa09f38\n10. If result is non-zero, perform three property setup operations:\n    a. Call SetObjectProperty(result, 0x42)\n    b. Call SetObjectProperty(result, 0x23b)\n    c. Call ClampValueInStructure(result, 0x0)\n    d. Call ComputeParameterValue(result, 0x0)\n\nParameters:\nImplicit first parameter in ESI (game object/unit pointer)\n\nReturns:\nvoid (property result stored in global 0x6fa09f38)",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
