      "name": "ValidatePeerAddressIfEnabled",
      "signature": "int ValidatePeerAddressIfEnabled(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Validates peer address if the peer validation feature is enabled.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load global configuration pointer from DAT_6fa09f14\n2. Check if validation is enabled by testing byte at offset 0x229\n3. If disabled (byte == 0): return 0 (success)\n4. If enabled (byte != 0):\n   - Call GetPeerAddress to validate peer connectivity\n   - If result is 0 (peer invalid): return 0xFFFFFFFF (error code)\n   - If result is non-zero (peer valid): return 0 (success)\n\nParameters:\n(none - uses global game state)\n\nReturns:\nint - 0 for success or peer disabled, 0xFFFFFFFF for peer validation failure\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- The validation flag at offset 0x229 in the global configuration structure controls whether peer validation is required\n- When peer validation is disabled, the function immediately returns success\n- When enabled, GetPeerAddress must return non-zero for successful validation\n- Returns -1 (0xFFFFFFFF) specifically to indicate peer failure condition\n\nStructure Layout:\nThis function accesses DAT_6fa09f14 (likely game state or configuration):\nOffset  Size  Field             Type        Description\n0x229   1     peerValidEnabled  byte        Flag controlling peer validation requirement",
