      "name": "QueryRegistryValueEx",
      "signature": "bool QueryRegistryValueEx(void * this, LPCSTR pValueName, LPBYTE pOutputBuffer, DWORD bufferSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "return_type": "bool",
      "comment": "Queries a registry value from HKEY_CURRENT_USER and copies data to output buffer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize output size to 0\n2. Open registry key HKEY_CURRENT_USER with read access (0x20019 = KEY_QUERY_VALUE | KEY_READ)\n3. Set output size to requested buffer size\n4. Query registry value by name with no type checking\n5. If successful, check return value and close key, returning status\n6. If query fails, close key and return false\n7. If key open fails, return false immediately\n\nParameters:\n- pValueName: Value name to query within the registry key\n- pOutputBuffer: Pointer to buffer to receive value data\n- bufferSize: Size of output buffer in bytes (also receives actual data size)\n\nReturns:\n- true: Value successfully retrieved and copied to output buffer\n- false: Registry key not found, value not found, or query failed\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Output size is updated to reflect actual data size after query\n- Uses HKEY_CURRENT_USER (0x80000002) as registry root\n- Access flags 0x20019 allows both query and enumerate operations\n- Returns false on any API failure (open, query, or close)",
