      "name": "RenderGameInterfaceTextBox",
      "signature": "void RenderGameInterfaceTextBox(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Renders game interface text box with entity list information\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocates 0x600 (1536) byte stack buffer for text accumulation\n2. Initializes buffer by calling string default constructor on each 2-byte word\n3. Checks if active entity list exists at DAT_6fa09f88\n4. Iterates through linked entity list (offset 0x200 = next, 0x204 = link field)\n5. For each entity with count < 0x200, calculates remaining buffer space\n6. Appends entity text using _strncat with UTF-8 to Unicode conversion\n7. Sets render state flag based on error condition\n8. Calls ModifyEntityStateBitFlags to update entity rendering state\n9. Renders final text box to screen using RenderTextBoxUnicodeText\n\nParameters:\n  None\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Stops processing when entity count reaches 0x200 limit\n  - Uses flag at ESP+0x8 to track error/success state\n  - Processes linked list with null termination check at offset 0x204\n  - Silent failure if DAT_6fa09f88 is null (no active entity)\n\nStructure Layout:\n  Entity List Node:\n    Offset Size Field           Type    Description\n       +0x0  4   object_ptr     void*   Pointer to game object\n     +0x200  4   next_ptr       void*   Pointer to next entity in list\n     +0x204  4   link_ptr       void*   Linked list forward pointer",
