      "name": "InitializeResourceState",
      "signature": "void InitializeResourceState(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Initialize resource state for game session.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call ClearResourceState() to reset any previous state\n2. Initialize 2 Unicode string objects in local buffer via constructor loop\n3. Format string to stack buffer using sprintf with format string at 0x6f9e7860\n4. Convert formatted ASCII string to Unicode using win2Unicode converter\n5. Load global resource list from DAT_6fa08e4c\n6. Allocate and append 4 new list nodes to the resource list\n7. Navigate list to specific index position (via NavigateListByIndex)\n8. Load game context pointer from DAT_6fa0a03c\n9. Call final initialization function with EDX=0 (no additional flags)\n10. Set global sentinel DAT_6fa09f30 to 0xfffffffe to mark initialization complete\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value, modifies global state\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Sentinel value 0xfffffffe indicates successful resource initialization\n- The function uses stack-allocated Unicode buffer for temporary string conversion\n- Loop count hardcoded to 2 for exactly 2 Unicode object constructors\n- List node allocation count hardcoded to 4 nodes\n- Uses multiple global data pointers: context (0x6fa0a03c), resource list (0x6fa08e4c), sentinel (0x6fa09f30)",
