      "name": "ProcessInitialGameCommands",
      "signature": "void ProcessInitialGameCommands(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Initializes game state by processing 15 sequential game commands with counter overflow detection.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize 7 local Unicode string buffers (32 bytes each, offsets -0xE0 to -0x20)\n2. Call constructor closure 0x10 times per buffer (16 iterations) to initialize Unicode objects\n3. Load 7 Windows ANSI strings from data addresses and convert each to Unicode format\n   - Strings: 0x6f9e781c, 0x6f9e7818, 0x6f9e7814, 0x6f9e7810, 0x6f9e780c, 0x6f9e7808, 0x6f9e7804\n4. Initialize global counter at 0x6fa09f24 to track command processing progress\n5. Process 15 sequential game commands in strict order if counter < 0x20 (32)\n   - Each command: check counter, call ProcessGameCommand with command buffer pointer\n   - Store result in array at 0x6fa08e80 indexed by counter\n   - Increment counter\n   - Call ValidateAndSetEntityMode or RenderUnicodeTextInBox based on command\n6. Check special condition at 0x6f9e9c44 after command 10; if zero, exit early\n7. If counter reaches 0x20 at any point, call GetReturnAddress, CleanupAndAbort, and _exit(-1)\n8. Normal completion returns after processing command 15\n\nReturns:\nReturns nothing (void). Function always exits - either normally after complete command sequence\nor through forced exit via _exit(-1) on counter overflow.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Counter overflow (0x6fa09f24 >= 0x20) triggers fatal error path\n- Early exit if 0x6f9e9c44 is zero after command 10\n- Command commands stored in global array at 0x6fa08e80 with 4-byte stride\n- Each command result from ProcessGameCommand stored separately in globals:\n  DAT_6fa09fd4, DAT_6fa09fd8, DAT_6fa09fdc, DAT_6fa09fe0, DAT_6fa09fe4,\n  DAT_6fa09fe8, DAT_6fa09fec, DAT_6fa09ff0\n\nCalling Convention:\n__stdcall: All parameters on stack, callee cleanup",
