      "name": "InitializeGameStateCommands",
      "signature": "void InitializeGameStateCommands(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Initializes game state by sequentially processing command contexts and setting up all game system resources.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call ProcessInitialGameCommands to initialize base systems\n2. Check if command queue has available slots (< 32 limit)\n3. Process first game command context (address 0x6f9eb1a0)\n4. Process UI command context (address 0x6f9eb080) with difficulty-based frame settings:\n   - If difficulty == 3 (hard): use frame type 0x2b54\n   - Otherwise: use frame type 0x14c8\n5. Process additional command contexts (0x6f9eb0b0, 0x6f9eb0e0, 0x6f9eb140, 0x6f9eb110)\n6. Call SetGlobalState with each command result to update game state\n7. Process final initialization command (0x6f9eb170)\n8. Configure rendering and gameplay parameters:\n   - Set rendering frame type 0x10\n   - Validate and set difficulty level\n   - Set entity parameter field -6 (0xfffffffa)\n   - Set multiple slot values (0, 0x23, 0xa5, 0xc3, 0xdc)\n   - Set array element field 0x10 at multiple indices\n9. Call InitializeResourceState to complete setup\n10. Process final command context (0x6f9eb530)\n11. Clear initialization flag (DAT_6fa0911c = 0)\n12. If queue overflows at any step, call CleanupAndAbort and exit with code -1\n\nParameters:\n  None\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value, function completes initialization or aborts on error\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  Queue overflow: If command counter exceeds 32 slots (0x20), function terminates process with CleanupAndAbort\n  Difficulty handling: Difficulty level determines frame type for rendering system\n  Magic numbers: 0x20 = queue size limit, 0x13e8 = error code for queue overflow",
