      "name": "UpdateGameState",
      "signature": "int UpdateGameState(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Updates game state by computing a bounded position value and storing state flags.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load base position from global DAT_6fa09180 (ECX)\n2. Load maximum position from global DAT_6fa08e48 (EAX)\n3. Load offset increment from global DAT_6f9e9c54 (EDX)\n4. Calculate available range: EAX - ECX\n5. Calculate new position: ECX + EDX\n6. Compare new position against available range (CMP ECX, EAX)\n7. If new position exceeds range (JGE), keep it; otherwise use calculated value\n8. Store computed position to DAT_6f9e9c54\n9. Store state byte from DAT_6f9e9c58 to DAT_6f9e9c50\n10. Return 1 (success)\n\nReturns:\n  1 (success) - Operation completed successfully\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Uses bounded comparison: min(base + offset, max - base)\n  - State value (byte) is unconditionally copied regardless of bounds check\n  - Function always returns success (1)\n  - RET 0x4 indicates stdcall with 1 parameter passed but ignored",
