      "name": "UpdateGameFrame",
      "signature": "int UpdateGameFrame(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Updates game frame timing and state management. This function loads frame timing values, calculates the frame delta by subtracting a reference counter from current time, and conditionally clears the result if the delta is non-positive. It stores timing state bytes and frame delta back to global variables, then returns 1 to indicate successful frame update.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Load current frame timestamp from global variable\\n2. Load reference/previous frame value for comparison\\n3. Load frame state byte from global storage\\n4. Calculate frame delta by subtraction\\n5. Check if delta is less than or equal to zero using SETLE\\n6. Store frame state byte to global output location\\n7. Conditionally clear delta if result was non-positive (AND with mask -1 or 0)\\n8. Store computed delta back to global frame counter\\n9. Return success status (1)\\n\\nReturns:\\nint - Always returns 1 indicating successful frame update",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:7299ebfc978a9fc5bc58df1aa08f91cf",
