      "name": "SearchListForPrefixMatch",
      "signature": "int SearchListForPrefixMatch(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Searches a linked list for the first node with a matching 2-character prefix.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Retrieve current window context and index\n2. Calculate maximum visible line count and clamp to max boundary\n3. Loop through list elements starting from current index:\n   a. Get next list node element at current index\n   b. Convert Unicode string to ANSI (stringBuffer, 256 bytes)\n   c. Compare first 2 bytes against search prefix at 0x6f9e7860\n   d. If match found: calculate aligned index (16-byte boundary) and store\n   e. If no match: increment index and continue loop\n4. Return 1 if match found, 0 if reached max index without match\n\nReturns:\n  1 = Matching element found (index stored in DAT_6f9e9c3c, DAT_6f9e9c54)\n  0 = No match found in range or reached boundary\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Index is clamped to DAT_6fa08e4c (max boundary)\n  - Result index is always aligned to 16-byte boundary\n  - Compares only first 2 bytes of converted string\n  - Called by FUN_6f9dc3a0 for UI updates",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:9fcdbfb5f52553928b00d3b4283fc6e2",
