      "name": "ProcessCommandQueue",
      "signature": "void ProcessCommandQueue(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Processes a sequential queue of game commands and stores results.\n\nThis function processes exactly 7 game commands in a fixed sequence, storing\neach result in a global command result array. Each command is processed only\nif the command counter (DAT_6fa09f24) has not exceeded 32 (0x20) entries.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if command counter < 32 (buffer size limit)\n2. For each of 7 command structures (DAT_6f9eaea0 through DAT_6f9eaff0):\n   - Call ProcessGameCommand with command structure pointer\n   - Store result in command result array at [DAT_6fa08e80 + counter*4]\n   - Increment command counter\n   - Check if counter >= 32 (buffer full condition)\n3. After command 6, call dispatch_command_handler and RenderUnicodeTextInBox\n4. After all 7 commands complete, call SetGlobalState with final result\n5. Return to caller\n6. If buffer full at any point, call error handler and exit process\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value, process exits on error via CleanupAndAbort\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Magic number 0x20 (32) is the maximum command queue size\n- Commands 1-6 are processed in strict sequence\n- Commands are stored at array index counter*4 indicating 4-byte result values\n- Ordinal 0x13e8 is used in error path for return address lookup\n- Function terminates process on buffer overflow condition",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "CAL",
