      "name": "InitializeCharacterCreationUI",
      "signature": "void InitializeCharacterCreationUI(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Initializes character creation UI by creating three entity instances and setting up UI controls.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if global entity count (DAT_6fa09f24) exceeds capacity (0x20 = 32 max entities)\n2. If count >= 0x20, call GetReturnAddress and CleanupAndAbort then exit with error code -1\n3. Create first entity using ProcessGameCommand(&DAT_6f9ea360)\n4. Store entity handle in global entity array at index DAT_6fa09f24\n5. Increment global entity counter\n6. Set created entity as current event target via SetCurrentEventTarget(entityHandle, 0)\n7. Modify entity bit flags using ModifyEntityBitFlags(entityHandle, 1)\n8. Check if entity count < 0x20 before proceeding\n9. Create second entity using ProcessGameCommand(&DAT_6f9ea3c0)\n10. Store entity handle in global array and increment counter\n11. Set bit flags on second entity\n12. Check if entity count < 0x20 before proceeding\n13. Create third entity using ProcessGameCommand(&DAT_6f9ea3f0)\n14. Store entity handle in global array and increment counter\n15. Set bit flags on third entity\n16. Render UI text box with RenderTextBoxUnicodeText(0, 0, 0)\n17. Store UI event handler (register EBX) to global DAT_6fa0a0e0\n18. If handler is NULL, set to default DestroyUIControls function\n19. Record current game tick via GetTickCount() to DAT_6fa09f2c\n20. If capacity exceeded at any check, abort and exit with error\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Capacity overflow: If creating any entity would exceed 0x20 entity limit, function aborts with exit code -1\n- Three sequential creation attempts: Each entity must be created and tracked separately\n- Hardcoded entity array address: DAT_6fa08e80 with 4-byte entries indexed by DAT_6fa09f24\n- Entity indices: Entity configuration pointers at DAT_6f9ea360, DAT_6f9ea3c0, DAT_6f9ea3f0\n- Bit flag value: Always sets flag 0x1 on created entities for character UI initialization\n\nStructure Layout (Global Entity Array):\nOffset  Size  Field Name           Type    Description\n0x0     4     entityCount          DWORD   Current number of entities (0x6fa09f24)\n0x0     4     entityArray          DWORD*  Array of entity handles starting at 0x6fa08e80\nEach entity entry: 4 bytes (DWORD handle)\nMax capacity: 0x20 entries (32 entities)\nHandler storage: 0x6fa0a0e0 (UI event callback)\nTick timestamp: 0x6fa09f2c (creation time)",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
