      "name": "InitializePlayerCommands",
      "signature": "void InitializePlayerCommands(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Initializes up to 4 player command entities and configures their event targets.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Destroy existing UI control array\\n2. Validate command index is below maximum threshold (0x20 = 32)\\n3. Process up to 4 game commands in sequence, storing entity pointers in array\\n4. For each command: store result, increment index, set event target, set entity flags\\n5. Render UI text boxes after processing commands 3 and 4\\n6. Abort with error if index exceeds limit during processing\\n\\nParameters:\\nNone. Uses global command index (0x6fa09f24) and command array (0x6fa08e80).\\n\\nReturns:\\nvoid. If any validation fails, calls CleanupAndAbort and exits with code -1.\\n\\nSpecial Cases:\\n- Maximum of 32 entities can be stored (0x20 limit)\\n- Four distinct command sources: 0x6f9ea420, 0x6f9ea480, 0x6f9ea4b0, 0x6f9ea4e0\\n- Nested validation ensures no overflow between commands\\n- Rendering occurs only after 3rd and 4th commands are processed\\n\\nStructure Layout:\\nCommand Array @ 0x6fa08e80 (32 entries, 4 bytes each):\\nOffset  Size  Field Name         Type      Description\\n0       4     commandEntity[0]   uint32    First command entity pointer\\n4       4     commandEntity[1]   uint32    Second command entity pointer\\n8       4     commandEntity[2]   uint32    Third command entity pointer\\n12      4     commandEntity[3]   uint32    Fourth command entity pointer",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
