      "name": "ValidateLicenseKeyString",
      "signature": "int ValidateLicenseKeyString(char * pInputString)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Validates a license key string by parsing alphanumeric segments separated by dashes or spaces.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get total length of input string using CalculateStringLength\n2. Initialize buffer index to 0, character index to 0\n3. Loop through input string character by character:\n   a. Check if current buffer has space for more characters (max 16 chars)\n   b. Load current character from input string\n   c. Check if character is alphanumeric (A-Z, a-z, 0-9):\n      - If valid, append to segment buffer and increment buffer index\n   d. Check for dash (-) or space ( ) characters:\n      - These are allowed separators between segments\n   e. If buffer reached 16 characters:\n      - Clear terminator byte and call ValidateLicenseKey to validate segment\n      - Check if validation passed and license type is valid (0x6, 0x7, 0xa, 0xc)\n      - If valid type found, return 1 (success)\n   f. Reset buffer index to 0 for next segment\n   g. Move to next character in input string\n4. Return 0 if no valid license segment found\n5. Return 1 if valid license segment with correct type found\n\nParameters:\npInputString - Pointer to null-terminated input string containing license key data\n\nReturns:\n1 if valid license key segment found with supported type\n0 if no valid license segment or unsupported license type\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- License key is processed in 16-character segments separated by dashes or spaces\n- Valid license types are: 0x6, 0x7, 0xa (10), 0xc (12)\n- Any character outside alphanumeric range except dash/space resets the buffer\n- Function scans entire input for any valid segment, returns on first match",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
