      "name": "ProcessChatCommand",
      "signature": "int ProcessChatCommand(char * pInputString)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Processes a game chat command string, parsing tokens and dispatching to appropriate handlers.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate input string length by scanning until null terminator\n2. Call CompareStringsWithLocaleInfo to check if input matches a known command\n3. If comparison fails, return 0 (command not recognized)\n4. Validate command format: must end with space or null terminator\n5. If validation fails, return 0\n6. Load global command string from address 0x6fa09198 and calculate its length\n7. If command string is empty, initialize Unicode buffer and format error message\n8. If command string exists, copy input string to local buffer and tokenize using space delimiter\n9. Parse tokens with Strtok, counting tokens until 2 are found or no more tokens\n10. On second token (index 2), call function at DAT_6fa0917c+0x68 to validate game state\n11. If validation passes, call dispatch_command_handler and ProcessAndQueueGameCommands\n12. If validation fails, format error message with command and parameter\n13. Convert formatted message to Unicode format\n14. Check if rendering is enabled (DAT_6fa0a0c8)\n15. If rendering enabled, call RenderTextBoxUnicodeText to display message\n16. Return 1 (command processed)\n\nParameters:\n- pInputString: Pointer to input chat command string (EAX at entry)\n- (implicit ECX): Context pointer used for Unicode conversion\n\nReturns:\n- 1 if command was matched and processed\n- 0 if command not recognized or validation failed\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Empty global command string triggers error message \"Nobody to reply to\"\n- Single token input triggers usage message \"Correct usage is...\"\n- Failed game state validation returns error without processing\n- Rendering only occurs if DAT_6fa0a0c8 is non-zero (rendering enabled flag)\n\nStack Layout (relative to ESP after SUB ESP, 0x508):\n- [ESP+0x14]: Formatted output buffer (256 bytes)\n- [ESP+0x114]: Input string copy buffer (256 bytes)\n- [ESP+0x214]: Unicode output buffer (512 bytes)\n- [ESP+0x50c]: Token delimiter word (2 bytes)",
