      "name": "ProcessPlayerChannelNotification",
      "signature": "int ProcessPlayerChannelNotification(char * pCommandString, char * pPlayerName)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Validates and processes a player channel notification (join/leave message).\n\nCompares two command strings for locale support and constructs a Unicode notification message with player name. Conditionally renders notification to channel based on system flags.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate length of player name string (pPlayerName)\n2. Call CompareStringsWithLocaleInfo() on command string validation\n3. Verify character at locale offset is space (0x20) or null (0x00)\n4. Call second CompareStringsWithLocaleInfo() check on pCommandString\n5. Check DAT_6fa0a090 flag (inverted) - determines which template string to use\n6. Initialize Unicode buffer (unicodeBuffer) with 256 wchar_t elements\n7. Copy template string to notification text buffer:\n   - If flag=0: copy 13 dwords from s_Player_entering_leaving_notifica_6f9e78b8\n   - If flag=1: copy 12 dwords + 1 word from s_Player_entering_leaving_notifica_6f9e78ec\n8. Convert ASCII notification text to Unicode format into unicodeBuffer\n9. Check DAT_6fa0a0c8 flag - if set, render the notification to UI\n10. Return 1 on success, 0 on validation failure\n\nParameters:\n- pCommandString (EAX): Pointer to command string for locale validation\n- pPlayerName (EBX): Pointer to player name string to process\n\nReturns:\n- 1 if notification processed and rendered successfully\n- 0 if command validation failed\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Space character (0x20) is treated as valid terminator alongside null (0x00)\n- DAT_6fa0a090 flag controls which notification template is used\n- DAT_6fa0a0c8 flag controls whether notification is rendered to UI\n- Unicode buffer sized for 256 characters (512 bytes)",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:85c64f0a37b6e6f173e4543e3bfbb71b",
