      "name": "ProcessSlashCommand",
      "signature": "void ProcessSlashCommand(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Processes slash commands by copying message buffer, incrementing chat counter, and validating/dispatching chat commands.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Copy 0x900 bytes from DAT_6fa092b8 to DAT_6fa093b8 using memmove\n2. Manually copy same buffer byte-by-byte from pCommandBuffer to DAT_6fa092b8 destination\n3. Increment global chat message counter DAT_6fa0a08c by 1\n4. Cap counter at maximum value of 10 (0xa)\n5. Call ProcessChatCommand with pCommandBuffer (first validation attempt)\n6. If ProcessChatCommand returns 0, call ProcessChatCommand again (second validation attempt)\n7. If second call returns 0, call ProcessPlayerChannelNotification for join/leave event\n8. If all validations pass (return 0), check game state validity via DAT_6fa0917c+0x68 function pointer\n9. If game state is invalid, call error handler at DAT_6fa0917c+0x14\n10. If game state valid, call dispatch_command_handler to process command\n11. Call ProcessAndQueueGameCommands to queue the command for execution\n12. Return from function\n\nParameters:\nNone (void) - Uses implicit ESI register containing pCommandBuffer (pointer to command string)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n1. Message counter capped at 10 entries maximum\n2. Double validation: ProcessChatCommand called twice (redundant validation pattern)\n3. If any validation fails (non-zero return), function returns immediately\n4. Game state check determines if command is dispatched or error handler invoked\n5. Implicit register parameter ESI contains the command buffer pointer\n6. Two exit points: early return at 0x6f9db127, or jump to error handler at 0x6f9db131\n\nMemory Access Pattern:\n[0x6fa093b8]: Destination buffer for first memmove (0x900 bytes)\n[0x6fa092b8]: Source buffer for memmove and copy loop\n[0x6fa0a08c]: Message counter global (incremented, capped at 0xa)\n[0x6fa0917c]: Global function pointer table\n  +0x68: Game state validation function pointer\n  +0x14: Error handler function pointer",
