      "name": "FormatFileTimeAsDateString",
      "signature": "void FormatFileTimeAsDateString(FILETIME * pFileTime, int bufferSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Converts a FILETIME structure to a formatted date string using Windows locale settings.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate and initialize a 512-character Unicode buffer with default constructors\n2. Convert FILETIME to SYSTEMTIME structure for locale-based formatting\n3. Format SYSTEMTIME as a date string using Windows locale (0x400 = user default locale)\n4. Convert the ANSI date string to Unicode using the system code page\n5. Convert the Unicode string to UTF-8 encoding in the output buffer\n6. Return the formatted UTF-8 date string in the output buffer\n\nParameters:\n  pFileTime: Pointer to FILETIME structure to convert\n  bufferSize: Size of output buffer in bytes for the formatted date string\n\nReturns:\n  void (result stored in output buffer)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Unicode buffer initialized to 512 characters\n  - Conversion flags set to 1 for handling multi-byte characters\n  - Uses user default locale (0x400) for date formatting\n  - String length set to -1 to auto-detect null termination\n\nStructure Layout:\n  Stack allocation: 0x210 (528 bytes)\n  - 0xc: SYSTEMTIME structure (16 bytes)\n  - 0x1c: Unicode buffer (1024 bytes = 512 characters \u00d7 2 bytes each)",
