      "name": "ProcessQueuedWorkItems",
      "signature": "void ProcessQueuedWorkItems(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Dequeues and processes work items from a thread-safe queue.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Enters critical section to safely access the work queue\n2. Retrieves and removes the first item from DAT_6fa0a0e8 (linked list head)\n3. Leaves critical section to minimize lock contention\n4. If an item was dequeued:\n   a. Checks item[0x8] field; if non-zero, calls ClearResourceState()\n   b. Checks item[0x0] field; if non-zero:\n      - Calls RenderTextWithLineBreaks() with DAT_6fa0a0c8\n      - If item[0x0] still non-zero, calls InitializeModule(0xc32, 0)\n   c. Always calls InitializeModule(0xc33, 0)\n   d. Calls NavigateListByIndex() to process the item\n5. Repeats until queue is empty (piVar1 becomes NULL)\n\nParameters:\nNone - operates on global shared state\n\nReturns:\nvoid - infinite loop until termination\n\nQueue Item Structure:\nOffset 0x0: int - primary status/flag field\nOffset 0x4: int - secondary parameter field\nOffset 0x8: int - resource clear flag\nOffset 0xc: pointer - next item in linked list",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
