      "name": "InitializeCharacterCreationAndRendering",
      "signature": "bool InitializeCharacterCreationAndRendering(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "bool",
      "comment": "Initializes the character creation UI and rendering engine.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if flag at DAT_6fa09f14 + 0x229 is set; return true if not set\n2. Retrieve handler interface pointer at DAT_6fa0917c\n3. Call handler's method at offset +0x68 to initialize handler state\n4. Validate peer address via GetPeerAddress(); return true if invalid\n5. Clear error flag DAT_6fa0a09c to 0\n6. Call dispatch_command_handler() to initialize command system\n7. Call InitializeCharacterCreationUI() to set up character creation interface\n8. Retrieve data structure via handler's offset +0x44 method call\n9. Validate retrieved data: must not be null and must have count > 8 at offset 0\n10. Extract data pointer by adding 4 bytes (skip count field)\n11. Initialize worker thread with extracted data via InitializeWorkerThread()\n12. Process rendering queue with CheckWorkerThreadAndInitializeRendering callback\n13. Destroy UI control array (cleanup)\n14. Check error flag DAT_6fa0a09c; return false if set\n15. Verify peer address again via GetPeerAddress()\n16. Check global state via GetGlobalState(); return false if state != 0\n17. Call ProcessAndEncodeBufferWrapper() with buffer at DAT_6fa09f14 + 0xb9\n18. Process final rendering queue with callback at 0x6f9d8f20\n19. Destroy UI control array (final cleanup)\n20. Retrieve final global state and return true if state == 0, false otherwise\n\nParameters:\nNone - function operates on global state\n\nReturns:\nbool - Returns true if character creation initialization succeeds, false otherwise\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Returns true immediately if flag at offset 0x229 is not set (early exit)\n- Returns true if peer address is invalid (GetPeerAddress != 0)\n- Returns false if handler interface is null (DAT_6fa0917c == 0)\n- Returns false if handler initialization fails\n- Returns false if retrieved data structure is null or has count <= 8\n- Returns false if error flag is set during processing\n- Return value calculation uses NEG/SBB/INC sequence for boolean conversion",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
