      "name": "ProcessInventoryInputDialog",
      "signature": "void ProcessInventoryInputDialog(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Process inventory dialog input and render UI controls.\n\nThis function orchestrates the complete UI lifecycle for inventory management input\nhandling. It processes game commands for multiple input fields, validates and renders\ntext components, performs string comparisons for buffer matching, and handles Unicode\nstring conversion and processing.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Process five game command inputs via ProcessGameCommand(), storing results in\n   global variables _DAT_6fa0a018 through _DAT_6fa0a028\n2. For each command result: dispatch handler via dispatch_command_handler() and\n   render text via RenderUnicodeTextInBox()\n3. Process final command value and store in _DAT_6fa0a02c, then SetGlobalState()\n4. Process sixth command (DAT_6f9ea870) and store in DAT_6fa0a030\n5. Call ValidateAndSetStructureField() to update structure field\n6. Call SetScreenshotMode() and SetEntityField0x26c() for mode setup\n7. Process final command (DAT_6f9ea8d0) and store in DAT_6fa0a038\n8. Retrieve UI buffer pointer via vtable function at offset 0x20 from DAT_6fa0917c\n9. If target field at offset 0x37d is not null, render text in UI control\n10. Load source buffer at offset 0x35d and target buffer at offset 0x37d\n11. Perform byte-pair string comparison: iterate through buffers comparing pairs of\n    bytes until mismatch found or null terminator reached\n12. If comparison indicates strings differ (iVar3 != 0), render text in UI control\n13. Loop through string buffer at pbVar2, iterating until null terminator found\n14. When string ends (currentChar == 0), enter final processing:\n    - ConvertStringToUnicodeAndProcess() to convert input\n    - SetActiveUIControl() to activate the control\n    - HandleTextInputDoubleClick() to process double-click event\n    - NavigateListByIndex() to navigate list\n    - ValidateAndGetObjectField() to retrieve Unicode string\n15. If Unicode string returned, call unicode2Win() to convert to Windows string,\n    limited to 0x1f characters and stored in unicodeBuffer[32]\n16. Calculate converted string length by iterating until null terminator\n17. ModifyObjectBitfield() to set completion flag in bitfield\n18. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\nNone - function operates on global game state, UI contexts, and implicit\n  this pointer in calling context\n\nReturns:\nvoid - function completes all dialog processing and returns control to caller\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- String comparison uses byte-pair (word) iteration for efficiency over single\n  byte comparison\n- Both string buffers are null-terminated wide strings\n- Unicode conversion output limited to 0x1f (31) characters to fit unicodeBuffer\n- Multiple string comparisons performed in nested loops for validation\n- Function uses several global data pointers (_DAT_6fa0a018 through _DAT_6fa0a038)\n  to maintain state across command processing\n- Vtable lookup at offset 0x20 suggests polymorphic object behavior\n- String buffer offsets 0x35d and 0x37d suggest fixed structure layout\n- String iteration continues beyond first null terminator to process multiple\n  null-separated strings in buffer",
