      "name": "LaunchGameExecutableOrFallback",
      "signature": "int LaunchGameExecutableOrFallback(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Launches the game executable via file association or falls back to direct game loop.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Query application path from global context via indirect function pointer\n2. Return 1 if path is null (early exit)\n3. Initialize 2048-byte buffer for file association registry key (1024 bytes + 1024 bytes)\n4. Query HKEY_CLASSES_ROOT registry for file extension handler\n5. If handler found, construct full command line by:\n   a. Querying registry for shell\\open\\command value (e.g., \"C:\\Path\\game.exe\")\n   b. Appending file extension marker (0x2 bytes from DAT_6f9e74d8)\n   c. Copying application path to end of command line\n6. Create process with constructed command line\n7. If CreateProcessA succeeds, close thread/process handles and return 1\n8. If registry lookup fails or CreateProcessA fails, call dispatch_command_handler and ProcessAndQueueGameCommands (game loop fallback)\n9. Call cleanup function via global context function pointer\n10. Return 1 to indicate success\n\nParameters:\nvoid - No parameters\n\nReturns:\nint - Always returns 1 (success/completion indicator)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Empty path returns early with value 1\n- Registry queries may fail silently and fallback to game loop\n- CreateProcessA failure triggers normal game loop dispatch instead of exiting\n- Fixed buffer sizes: 1024 bytes for each registry string buffer, 2 bytes for extension marker\n- Uses __stdcall convention with 0x4 bytes cleanup (RET 0x4)\n\nStructure Layout:\nRegistry key format: HKEY_CLASSES_ROOT\\[FileType]\\shell\\open\\command\nProcess creation uses STARTUPINFOA (0x44 bytes) and PROCESS_INFORMATION structures\nTemporary command buffer: 1024 bytes for combined command line",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
