      "name": "InitializeCharacterCreationFlow",
      "signature": "bool InitializeCharacterCreationFlow(void * context, int unused)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "bool",
      "comment": "Character Creation Flow Initialization\\n\\nInitializes the character creation UI system by setting up the rendering context, dispatching initial commands, and rendering the UI. This function establishes the character creation environment and prepares the display.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Store context pointer and parameters in global state variables\\n2. Call profile_sex virtual function handler with initialization flag\\n3. Initialize command dispatch handler\\n4. Initialize character creation UI components\\n5. Set up rendering parameters and process rendering queue\\n6. Clean up and destroy UI control arrays\\n7. Return success status based on initialization result\\n\\nParameters:\\ncontext: Game context pointer passed in ECX register\\nunused: Additional parameter passed in EDX (unused in this function)\\n\\nReturns:\\nbool: true if initialization succeeded (DAT_6fa09118 == 0), false otherwise\\n\\nCalling Convention:\\n__fastcall - First parameter (context) in ECX, second parameter (unused) in EDX, callee cleanup with RET 0x4\\n\\nSpecial Cases:\\n- The function uses global state variables (DAT_6fa0917c, DAT_6fa09118) to manage initialization state\\n- Returns inverted success status: true when DAT_6fa09118 == 0 (zero = success)",
