      "name": "InitializeGameEntityState",
      "signature": "int InitializeGameEntityState(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Initializes game entity state and resource allocation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call ValidateGameEntityModes to validate current entity modes\n2. Call ValidateAndSetEntityMode to ensure entity mode is properly set\n3. Check if current entity mode (at 0x6f9e9c50) is either 0x10 or 0x7\n4. If mode is neither value, proceed with initialization:\n   a. Set resource allocation limit to 0xc8 (200) at address 0x6fa08e4c\n   b. Call InitializeResourceState to initialize game resources\n   c. Set initialization flag to 1 at address 0x6f9e9c40\n   d. Call CalculateInventoryOffset(7) to get inventory offset for slot 7\n   e. Store calculated offset in entity mode field at 0x6f9e9c50\n   f. Clear inventory state counter at address 0x6f9e9c54 to 0\n5. Return 1 indicating successful initialization\n\nReturns:\n- 1: Initialization completed successfully\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If entity mode is already 0x10 or 0x7, skips all initialization and returns immediately\n- Magic number 0xc8 (200) represents resource allocation limit\n- Magic number 7 represents inventory slot index for calculation",
