      "name": "ProcessStateChangeAndEncodeCommand",
      "signature": "uint ProcessStateChangeAndEncodeCommand(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Processes state changes and encodes a command packet if state differs.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Get current system tick count via GetTickCount()\\n2. Check if command processing timeout has expired (currentTickCount > DAT_6fa0a098)\\n3. If timeout not expired or DAT_6fa0a03c is zero, skip processing (early exit)\\n4. Call SearchListForPrefixMatch() to search for matching list entry\\n5. If search returned result OR DAT_6f9e9c40 is set, proceed to state comparison\\n6. Compare stored command state (DAT_6fa09f30) with current state (DAT_6f9e9c54)\\n7. Compare stored command mode (DAT_6f9e9c3c) with current mode (DAT_6f9e9c38)\\n8. If either state or mode differs, execute state change handling:\\n   - Copy state byte from DAT_6f9e9c50 to DAT_6f9e9c58\\n   - Copy command value from DAT_6f9e9c54 to DAT_6f9e9c5c\\n   - Call EncodeCommand0x11() to encode the 0x11 command packet\\n   - Update timeout timer: DAT_6fa0a098 = GetTickCount() + 1000ms\\n   - Cache current state values for next iteration\\n9. Return 1 (success)\\n\\nReturns:\\n  1 (always returns success)\\n\\nSpecial Cases:\\n  - Timeout value stored at DAT_6fa0a098 is in milliseconds (1000ms intervals)\\n  - Search result check is OR'd with DAT_6f9e9c40 flag for command force-send\\n  - State comparison uses both command value and mode byte to detect changes\\n  - Early exit paths (timeout not expired or disabled): skip to return\\n",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
