      "name": "DisplayGameMessageAndProcessCommands",
      "signature": "int DisplayGameMessageAndProcessCommands(void * pMessageText, int messageType)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Displays a game message to the player and processes associated game state updates.\\n\\nThis function is called when the game needs to display UI messages such as ladder player data,\\nerror notifications, or status updates. It coordinates cleanup, entity state management, UI\\nrendering, and persistence of message context for later retrieval.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Call CleanupGameUIAndState() to reset UI state and close any open overlays\\n2. Check if global entity pointer (DAT_6fa09f88) is non-null\\n3. If entity exists: Call ModifyEntityStateBitFlags() to reset entity state flags\\n4. Call ValidateAndSetEntityMode() four times to process and validate four separate entity\\n   mode configurations (likely for different entity types or UI elements)\\n5. Store ProcessGameCommand result in global DAT_6fa0a0d8 (game command output buffer)\\n6. Call RenderUnicodeTextInBox() to render the message text to screen\\n7. Store messageType parameter in global DAT_6fa0a0e0 for later retrieval\\n8. Return 1 to indicate successful message display\\n\\nParameters:\\npMessageText (void*) - Pointer to Unicode text string to display in message box. Contains\\n   formatted message text that may include player names, skill tiers, experience values, or\\n   error descriptions depending on caller context.\\nmessageType (int) - Integer context value stored in DAT_6fa0a0e0, used by caller to track\\n   message type (e.g., ladder display, error notification, status update). Value passed\\n   through without modification and retrieved by subsequent calls.\\n\\nReturns:\\nint - Always returns 1 (success code indicating message was processed)\\n\\nSpecial Cases:\\n- DAT_6fa09f88 is checked for validity; if NULL, ModifyEntityStateBitFlags skipped\\n- Four consecutive calls to ValidateAndSetEntityMode suggest independent configuration of\\n  four separate entity modes or UI state variables\\n- Globals modified: DAT_6fa0a0d8 (command output), DAT_6fa0a0e0 (message type context)\\n- Called from 12 locations including InitializeGameStateSecondary, ProcessLadderPlayerSkillData,\\n  and InitializeGameUIAndSettings for various UI notification scenarios",
