      "name": "CalculateInventoryOffset",
      "signature": "int CalculateInventoryOffset(int baseOffset)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Calculates the inventory offset for an item/skill based on its type.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Checks if itemType (passed in EAX) is in range 9-16: returns 9 + baseOffset\\n2. Checks if itemType is in range 0-7: returns baseOffset unchanged\\n3. Checks if itemType is in range 19-26: returns 19 + baseOffset\\n4. Checks if itemType is in range 27-34: returns 27 + baseOffset\\n5. If itemType is outside all ranges: calls CleanupAndAbort with error code 0x1996\\n\\nParameters:\\n- baseOffset: Offset value to combine with item type (passed in ECX)\\n- itemType: Implicit parameter in EAX determining which offset to apply\\n\\nReturns:\\nInteger offset value calculated from baseOffset and itemType ranges\\n\\nStructure Layout:\\nThe function implements a skill/item type mapping table:\\nOffset | Range | Calculation\\n0x0    | 0-7   | baseOffset (skills 0-7)\\n0x9    | 9-16  | baseOffset + 9 (skills 9-16)\\n0x13   | 19-26 | baseOffset + 19 (skills 19-26)\\n0x1b   | 27-34 | baseOffset + 27 (skills 27-34)\\n\\nThis pattern suggests 4 skill trees with different base offsets in the character structure, commonly used for player skill groups in Diablo II.\\\"",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:1d30edb6c3d8f89bd2f5faff7a3a3d2c",
