      "name": "InitializeEntityWithIdAndName",
      "signature": "uint InitializeEntityWithIdAndName(word entityId, char * entityName)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Initializes entity state with provided ID and name, supporting dual code paths based on flag check.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Set global state flag to 2 (initialization in progress)\n2. Call FUN_6f9dbe00() to initialize entity structure\n3. Load base address of entity structure from global DAT_6fa09f14\n4. Store entity ID parameter at struct offset +0x19 (2 bytes)\n5. Copy name string (from EDI) to struct offset +0x1b until null terminator\n6. Copy config string (from EBX) to struct offset +0x241 until null terminator\n7. Check flag byte at struct offset +0x229 (0=branch A, non-zero=branch B)\n8. BRANCH A (flag=0): Initialize with entity name path\n   a. Set state code to 7 at struct offset +0x15\n   b. Copy entity name parameter to struct offset +0x33\n   c. Set global DAT_6fa0a0dc to 1\n   d. Call SetSystemConfigValue(0)\n   e. Call InitializeRenderingState()\n   f. Return 1 (success)\n9. BRANCH B (flag!=0): Initialize with peer address encryption path\n   a. Call GetPeerAddress() to retrieve peer entity address\n   b. If peer lookup returns 0, error path: reset flag, dispatch handler, return 0\n   c. If peer lookup succeeds, load word from DAT_6f9e9c34\n   d. Set state code to 3 at struct offset +0x15\n   e. Increment word value, repeat if result equals 0 (wrap around on overflow)\n   f. Call EncodeBuffersWithKey(encodedWord) for encryption\n   g. Store encrypted word in global DAT_6fa09f18\n   h. Call ModifyEntityStateBitFlags() to apply state changes\n   i. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\nentityId (word): Entity identification number, stored at struct offset +0x19\nentityName (char*): Pointer to null-terminated entity name string, copied to offset +0x33\n\nReturns:\nuint: 1 if initialization completed successfully, 0 if peer address lookup failed\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Overflow handling on word increment: loop continues until non-zero result\n- String copy operations terminate on null byte (0x00)\n- State flag at offset +0x229 determines initialization strategy\n- Magic offsets: 0x19 (ID), 0x1b (name), 0x241 (config), 0x229 (flag), 0x15 (state code), 0x33 (entity name dest)\n- Error recovery: If peer lookup fails, resets state flag to 0 before returning\n\nStructure Layout:\nEntity State Structure (stride variable):\nOffset | Size | Field Name       | Type     | Description\n------ | ---- | ---------------- | -------- | -----------\n0x15   | 4    | stateCode        | uint     | State: 2=init, 3=processing, 7=complete\n0x19   | 2    | entityId         | word     | Entity identification number\n0x1b   | 26   | entityNameField  | char[26] | Entity name buffer\n0x33   | 200  | entityNameBuffer | char[200]| Full entity name\n0x229  | 1    | pathSelector     | byte     | Flag: 0=name path, non-zero=encryption path\n0x241  | 256  | configBuffer     | char[256]| Configuration data buffer",
