      "name": "InitializeConfigurationState",
      "signature": "int InitializeConfigurationState(char * pConfigString)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Initializes the configuration state by copying multiple source buffers to configuration offsets and checking system readiness.\n\nThis function handles the core initialization of the game configuration system by copying strings from three source buffers (at offsets +0x00, +0x10, +0x20) to their destination locations in the global configuration structure (at offsets +0x1b, +0x241, +0x259). It validates the configuration state and either initializes rendering if unconfigured or manages peer connectivity if already initialized.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call FUN_6f9dbe00 to prepare initialization\n2. Load configuration base from DAT_6fa09f14\n3. Copy three source buffers via string copy loops:\n   - Copy from pSourceBuffer+0x00 to configBase+0x1b\n   - Copy from pSourceBuffer+0x10 to configBase+0x241\n   - Copy from pSourceBuffer+0x20 to configBase+0x259\n4. Set flag DAT_6fa09f20 to 1\n5. Check configuration flag at configBase+0x229:\n   - If 0 (unconfigured): copy pConfigString to configBase+0x33, initialize rendering, return 1\n   - If 1 (configured): get peer address via GetPeerAddress\n6. If peer address is 0: dispatch command handler and return 0\n7. If peer address non-zero: increment counter and initialize peer connection, return 1\n\nParameters:\n- pConfigString (char*): Configuration string to copy to destination at offset +0x33 if system unconfigured\n\nReturns:\n- 1 on successful initialization or if system already configured\n- 0 if peer address check failed\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- The three source buffers are accessed via EDI register which is unaffected by function calls (implicit parameter)\n- DAT_6fa09f20 flag controls initialization state tracking\n- Counter increment loop at 0x6f9dcdd0 ensures atomic counter increment (skips if overflow)\n- Function uses __stdcall convention with caller cleanup of 4-byte parameter",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "CAL",
