      "name": "InitializeGameAfterStateReset",
      "signature": "void InitializeGameAfterStateReset(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Initializes the game engine after clearing game state. Rebuilds UI controls,\nprocesses game commands, sets up entity and skill states, and reinitializes\nthe character slot properties. Called once during game initialization from\nInitializeGameEngine when transitioning from menu to active gameplay.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if GameStateGlobalData flag is set; exit if not\n2. Clear GameStateGlobalData and call _sprintf to format debug log with\n   character name and difficulty strings to debugLogBuffer[256]\n3. Destroy all UI controls and clean up screenshot node if allocated\n4. Set game state from global DAT_6fa09f40 and initialize DAT_6fa09f38 to 0\n5. Process 11 game command objects (0x6f9e9d30 through 0x6f9ea150) and store\n   results in global command state variables DAT_6fa09138 through DAT_6fa0a0d0\n6. Modify object bitfield and call SetScreenshotMode, SetEntityField0x26c\n7. Set active UI control to DAT_6fa0a0d0 result and validate structure fields\n8. Initialize character slot properties\n9. Modify entity bitfield for entities at DAT_6fa09164, DAT_6fa09168,\n   DAT_6fa0916c, DAT_6fa09170 with flag value 1 using ModifyEntityBitFlags\n10. Loop from offset 0x28 to 0x2bc (step 0x3c, 13 iterations) calling\n    CheckActiveSkillStateBits with threshold 0x3c, value 100 to populate\n    skill state array at DAT_6fa08e50\n11. Process final game command (0x6f9ea0f0) and modify entity state bitflags\n12. Process command (0x6f9ea270) and conditionally validate structure field\n    if DAT_6fa09f28 is non-zero\n13. Clean up stack (0x100 bytes) and return to caller\n\nReturns: void (no return value)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If GameStateGlobalData is 0 at entry, entire initialization is skipped\n- Screenshot node cleanup (step 3) only occurs if DAT_6fa09f38 is non-NULL\n- Final structure field validation (step 12) only occurs if DAT_6fa09f28 != 0\n- Skill state loop (step 10) processes exactly 13 slots using stride 0x3c bytes\n- Uses __stdcall convention: parameters on stack with callee cleanup via RET",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
