      "name": "ProcessPeerStateTransition",
      "signature": "void ProcessPeerStateTransition(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Processes peer state transitions and dispatches game commands based on peer connection status.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Test implicit EAX parameter: 0 = no peer/idle state, non-zero = peer exists\\n2. If EAX == 0 (idle branch):\\n   a. Check DAT_6fa09f20 (state machine): if 0 and DAT_6fa0a0d8 != 0, call FUN_6f9dbe00\\n   b. Load game state pointer DAT_6fa09f14, read flags at offset +0x1eb (word)\\n   c. Test bits 3 (0x8) and 2 (0x4): if either not set, call ModifyObjectBitfield twice\\n   d. Call ModifyObjectBitfield a third time unconditionally\\n   e. Check DAT_6fa09f88 (entity state): if non-zero, call ModifyEntityStateBitFlags and return\\n3. If EAX != 0 (peer active branch):\\n   a. Call GetPeerAddress to validate peer connection\\n   b. If GetPeerAddress returns 0:\\n      - Call dispatch_command_handler to get command pointer\\n      - Call ProcessAndQueueGameCommands to process queued commands\\n   c. If GetPeerAddress != 0:\\n      - Save ActivateEntityState function pointer\\n      - Clear state machine DAT_6fa09f20 to 0\\n      - Call dispatch_command_handler to get command pointer\\n      - Call FUN_6f9dc610 with command pointer and ActivateEntityState\\n      - Check DAT_6fa09f88: if non-zero, call ModifyEntityStateBitFlags and return\\n4. Return to caller\\n\\nParameters:\\n  Implicit (EAX): int peerStatus - 0 if no peer/idle, non-zero if peer connection exists\\n\\nReturns:\\n  void - No explicit return value. Modifies global state via ModifyEntityStateBitFlags call.\\n\\nSpecial Cases:\\n  State machine values at DAT_6fa09f20: 0=idle, 1=encoding, 2=processing, 3=active\\n  Game state pointer at DAT_6fa09f14 controls main game state with flags at +0x1eb\\n  Entity state flag at DAT_6fa09f88: non-zero indicates entity state change needed\\n  Global configuration at DAT_6fa0a0d8: initialization flag for game setup\\n  Calling patterns show this is core event dispatch routine called from game loop\\\"",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
