      "comment": "Processes entity mode flags and notifies of field changes via Unicode conversion.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Retrieve current entity mode flags via GetEntityModeFlags()\n2. Return early (0) if mode flags are zero (entity not ready)\n3. Validate and retrieve object field data via ValidateAndGetObjectField()\n4. If field data exists:\n   - Convert field Unicode data to Windows format into 256-byte buffer\n   - Call FUN_6f9dc690 to notify and finalize entity mode changes\n5. Return success status (1) indicating operation completed\n\nParameters:\n- None (implicit entity state accessed via globals at 0x6fa0a028 and 0x6fa0a030)\n\nReturns:\n- 0 (int): Entity mode flags are zero, early termination\n- 1 (int): Operation completed successfully, notification sent\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Local stack buffer unicodeBuffer is 256 bytes (0x100) allocated via SUB ESP,0x100\n- ValidateAndGetObjectField may return null pointer, skipping notification\n- Function uses __stdcall convention with callee stack cleanup (RET 0x4)",
