      "name": "ProcessGameInitializationCommands",
      "signature": "void ProcessGameInitializationCommands(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Processes and validates initial game commands during startup sequence.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize global state variables (0x6fa09fd4-0x6fa09ff0) to 0\n2. Set initial game speed threshold (0x6fa08e4c) to 1000ms\n3. Check if peer address is available (0x6fa09f14 + 0x229)\n4. If peer is valid and returned address is 0:\n   - Dispatch command handler with command code 0x1413\n   - Call cleanup function and return early\n5. Validate command buffer not full (counter at 0x6fa09f24 < 0x20)\n6. If space available:\n   - Process first command from 0x6f9eb020, store result at 0x6fa08e80[counter*4]\n   - Increment counter\n   - Process second command from 0x6f9eb050, store result\n   - Increment counter again\n7. Dispatch second command handler\n8. Render unicode text in game window\n9. Initialize game state command system\n10. Set global configuration values (0x6fa09f30=0xfffffffe, 0x6f9e9c58=0x23, etc.)\n11. Call SetGlobalStateValues to finalize initialization\n12. If counter would exceed 0x20 (buffer overflow):\n    - Get return address with marker 0x13e8\n    - Call cleanup function with error address\n    - Exit process with code -1\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function terminates either via return after successful initialization or via _exit(-1) on error\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Buffer overflow: Allows max 32 (0x20) command results before fatal error\n- Early exit: If peer address check returns 0, skips main initialization\n- Magic values: Command code 0x1413, offset 0x229 for peer check, buffer size 0x20\n- Global speed threshold: Set to 1000ms (0x3e8)\n\nParameters:\nNone - Function initializes global state directly",
