      "name": "BroadcastChatMessage",
      "signature": "int BroadcastChatMessage(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Broadcasts a formatted chat message to all connected clients after validation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check input validation: if EAX is zero OR message starts with '/' OR global DAT_6fa09f08 is zero, copy message as-is\n2. For non-slash messages when DAT_6fa09f08 is valid:\n   a. Load path configuration from DAT_6fa09f08 + 4\n   b. Search for wildcard character '*' using FindCharInString\n   c. If '*' found at non-null position and next char is null terminator, use that position; else use path start\n   d. Format message as \"/whisper %s %s\" with sprintf into DAT_6fa08f18 buffer\n3. Validate message using FindPathPatternInString against two pattern addresses from DAT_6fa09f14\n4. If FindPathPatternInString returns 0:\n   a. Call ValidateLicenseKeyString to verify message content\n   b. If license validation also returns 0, halt with bad instruction\n5. On successful validation:\n   a. Call dispatch_command_handler to queue message for dispatch\n   b. Call dispatch_command_handler again with result code\n6. Call InitializePlayerCommands for post-processing\n7. Clear DAT_6fa08f18 buffer and return 0\n\nParameters:\nIMPLICIT EDI - Pointer to message string buffer (unaffected register from caller)\nIMPLICIT EAX - Behavior control flag (0=copy-only, non-zero=validate and dispatch)\n\nReturns:\nint - Always returns 0 (success indicator)\n\nSpecial Cases:\nMessage starting with '/' - Treated as raw command, bypasses whisper formatting\nDAT_6fa09f08 null - Disables path validation and formatting\nMissing '*' in path - Uses entire path configuration string\nLicense validation failure - Triggers halt_baddata() for invalid content\nGlobal state - Uses DAT_6fa09f08 for path config, DAT_6fa09f14 for pattern validation\nOutput buffer - DAT_6fa08f18 holds formatted/validated message for dispatch",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:a24e31fd4231ba9aacc30e9d2613e821",
