      "name": "ProcessUnicodeStringWithTokenizer",
      "signature": "uint ProcessUnicodeStringWithTokenizer(Unicode * pInputString)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Processes a Unicode string by validating, converting, and tokenizing it.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize global marker to 0xffffffff\n2. Calculate length of input Unicode string using strlen\n3. Return 0 if string length equals 0 (empty string)\n4. Check if global initialization flag (DAT_6fa0917c) is set\n5. If flag not set, get return address (0x1237), call cleanup/abort handler, and exit with code -1\n6. Convert Unicode string to Windows encoding (CP1252) into 256-byte buffer (acStack_200)\n7. Copy converted string byte-by-byte into second 256-byte buffer (acStack_100) until null terminator\n8. Set delimiter buffer (acStack_204) to space character (0x20)\n9. Call strtok to parse acStack_100 using space delimiter\n10. If strtok returns null (no token found), call ProcessUnicodeWithCallback() and return 1\n11. Otherwise, call func_0x042ac340 and return its result\n\nParameters:\npInputString (Unicode *): Input string in Unicode/wide-character format\n\nReturns:\n0 - Empty input string (length 0)\n1 - No token found after strtok call\nOther - Return value from func_0x042ac340 when token found\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Empty strings return immediately (0)\n- Missing initialization flag triggers abort sequence with return code -1\n- String conversion limited to 256 bytes (potential overflow if Unicode length > 256)\n- Strtok uses space (0x20) as single delimiter character",
