      "name": "CleanupAndReinitializeGameState",
      "signature": "int CleanupAndReinitializeGameState(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Cleanup UI controls and reinitialize game state to default configuration.\n\nDESCRIPTION:\nPerforms comprehensive cleanup of UI elements and reinitializes core game state variables\nto prepare for a fresh game session. This function is typically called during game\ninitialization or when resetting to a clean state.\n\nALGORITHM:\n1. Call CleanupUIControls to remove all UI control elements from the interface\n2. Call FUN_6f9dd0d0 to initialize game state variables and command handlers\n3. Set byte at 0x6f9e9c50 to 0x13 (state marker, possibly enum value 19)\n4. Zero out dword at 0x6f9e9c54 (likely state counter or timer)\n5. Return 1 to indicate successful completion\n\nPARAMETERS:\nNone\n\nRETURNS:\n1 - Success, game state initialized\n\nSPECIAL CASES:\nMagic value 0x13 at offset 0x6f9e9c50 appears to be a game state enum value.\nThe paired location at 0x6f9e9c54 is reset to 0, suggesting it may be a counter\nor timer for the current game state.",
