      "name": "ProcessCharacterCreationUICommands",
      "signature": "void ProcessCharacterCreationUICommands(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Processes a sequence of 5 character creation UI element commands.\\n\\nThis function orchestrates the processing of UI elements used during character creation\\nby iteratively processing each UI element's command configuration, dispatching the\\ncommand handler, and rendering the text box for display.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. For each of 5 UI elements (in sequence):\\n   - Call ProcessGameCommand with UI element configuration struct\\n   - Store returned command ID in global variable (DAT_6fa09d90, DAT_6fa09d94, etc.)\\n   - Set ECX to element ID constant (0x1493, 0x1494, 0x1496, 0x1497, 0x1492)\\n   - Call dispatch_command_handler() to process the command\\n   - Call RenderUnicodeTextInBox() to render the UI element\\n\\nParameters:\\nNone - all UI element configurations are accessed via global data structures\\nin the DAT_6f9eb740-DAT_6f9eb890 address range.\\n\\nReturns:\\nvoid - no return value; results stored in global variables at DAT_6fa09d90-DAT_6fa09da8\\n\\nUI Element Configurations:\\n- Element 1: DAT_6f9eb740 -> ID 0x1493 -> DAT_6fa09d90\\n- Element 2: DAT_6f9eb770 -> ID 0x1494 -> DAT_6fa09d94\\n- Element 3: DAT_6f9eb7a0 -> ID 0x1496 -> DAT_6fa09d98\\n- Element 4: DAT_6f9eb7d0 -> ID 0x1497 -> DAT_6fa09d9c\\n- Element 5: DAT_6f9eb890 -> ID 0x1492 -> DAT_6fa09da8\\n\\nCalling Context:\\nCalled by ProcessProfileCreationUI and InitializeCharacterCreationUI during\\ncharacter creation UI initialization sequence.",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
