      "name": "IsValidCharacterName",
      "signature": "int IsValidCharacterName(undefined4 param_1, undefined4 param_2, char * pCharacter)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Validates if a character is a valid alphanumeric or allowed special character for names.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load character from input pointer\n2. Subtract 0x20 (space character) and compare against 0x3F range\n3. If in range, use lookup table at 0x6f9e197c to determine valid classification\n4. Use jump table at 0x6f9e1974 to dispatch to handler based on classification\n5. If lookup table indicates valid (space, apostrophe, hyphen, underscore), return 1\n6. If outside lookup range, check explicit character ranges for digits (0x30-0x39), uppercase letters (0x41-0x5A), and lowercase letters (0x61-0x7A)\n7. Return 1 if character matches any valid range, 0 otherwise\n\nParameters:\n- param_1: undefined4 - Unused parameter\n- param_2: undefined4 - Unused parameter\n- pCharacter: char * - Pointer to character to validate\n\nReturns:\n- 1 (true) if character is valid (alphanumeric or space/apostrophe/hyphen/underscore)\n- 0 (false) if character is invalid\n\nValid Characters:\n- Digits: 0-9 (0x30-0x39)\n- Uppercase: A-Z (0x41-0x5A)\n- Lowercase: a-z (0x61-0x7A)\n- Special: space (0x20), apostrophe (0x27), hyphen (0x2D), underscore (0x5F)",
