      "name": "ParseUnicodeFieldToInteger",
      "signature": "long ParseUnicodeFieldToInteger(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Extracts and parses a numeric value from a Unicode object field. Retrieves a Unicode string, converts it to UTF-8 format with a 5-character limit, then parses the resulting string as a long integer using the C standard _atol() function. Used for converting Unicode-encoded numeric fields in game data structures to integer values.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Retrieve Unicode object field via ValidateAndGetObjectField()\\n2. Allocate 8 bytes of stack space for UTF-8 buffer\\n3. Call Unicode::toUtf() to convert Unicode to UTF-8 (max 5 characters)\\n4. Call _atol() to parse UTF-8 string as long integer\\n5. Return the parsed integer value\\n\\nParameters:\\nNone (uses implicit global context object accessed via ECX)\\n\\nReturns:\\nEAX - The parsed integer value from the Unicode field\\n\\nSpecial Cases:\\n- Buffer limited to 5 UTF-8 characters for safety\\n- Invalid numeric strings return 0 via _atol() default behavior\\n- Function uses __stdcall convention (caller cleans stack via RET with immediate)",
