      "name": "InitializeMaxPlayerSettings",
      "signature": "void InitializeMaxPlayerSettings(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Initializes maximum player count setting during game UI setup.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate local stack space for configuration data (8 bytes)\n2. Initialize buffer pointer and configuration parameters\n3. Call configuration check function (func_0x1018bd60)\n4. If configuration not yet initialized, call config setup function (func_0x1018bec0) with Diablo II identifier and MAX_PLAYER string\n5. Load the player count value from configuration\n6. Validate player count is within valid range (must be > 0 and < 9)\n7. If valid, format player count into configuration string using sprintf\n8. Call ConvertStringToUnicodeAndProcess to apply the setting\n9. Clean up stack frame and return\n\nParameters:\n(none - no parameters)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Magic numbers: 9 is the maximum valid player count (exclusive), 0x34 (hex 52) is formatting directive\n- Configuration file references: s_Diablo_II_6f9e74ec (config file name), s_MAX_PLAYER_6f9e74f8 (setting key)\n- Boundary validation: Player count must satisfy both: count < 9 AND count > 0\n- If count is outside valid range [1, 8], function skips string formatting and exits\n\nStructure Layout:\nConfiguration buffer used for player count formatting:\nOffset | Size | Field Name      | Type | Description\n0      | 4    | configPtr       | ptr  | Pointer to configuration entry\n4      | 4    | unused          | uint | Reserved/padding\nTotal size: 8 bytes",
