      "name": "HandleFailedNetworkInputCleanup",
      "signature": "void HandleFailedNetworkInputCleanup(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Cleanup handler for failed network input processing.\n\nThis function is invoked when peer address lookup fails during network message processing. It handles UI state cleanup and processes a string from the structured data array.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if UI control pointer (DAT_6fa09cc4) is active\n2. If not active, exit early without processing\n3. Load input value from EAX and multiply by 0x3b (structure stride) to get array offset\n4. Add base offset 0x6f9ebf20 to calculate structure address\n5. Call ClearResourceState to reset UI state\n6. Scan for null terminator starting at offset +0x11 to calculate string length\n7. If string length is 0, skip rendering and go to navigation\n8. If string length > 0:\n   a. Call RenderTextInUIControl twice to update display\n   b. Calculate string length and store in stack parameter\n9. Call NavigateListByIndex with XOR EDX=0 (null parameter)\n10. Test if ESI+0x1 is non-zero for final condition check\n11. If condition met, call ConvertStringToUnicodeAndProcess with string length\n12. Call SetActiveUIControl(0) to clear active UI control\n13. Return\n\nParameters:\nNone (input value in EAX from caller context)\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- UI control inactive: Function exits immediately without processing\n- Empty string: Skips rendering, continues to navigation\n- String stride: 0x3b (59 bytes) structure size\n- String offset within structure: +0x11 (17 bytes from base)\n- Multiple render calls: RenderTextInUIControl called twice for double update",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
