      "name": "SearchAndNavigateTextInUIList",
      "signature": "void SearchAndNavigateTextInUIList(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Searches a UI list for matching text and navigates to the matching item.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if UI control data is initialized (DAT_6fa09cc0)\n2. Retrieve search text from linked list and convert Unicode to Windows format\n3. Validate window data and clear resource state twice\n4. Get peer address to determine if additional processing is needed\n5. Copy item structure data (0x3b bytes per item) from source to destination\n6. Iterate through all items and render them in the UI control\n7. If search text exists and items are present, search through all items\n8. For each item, perform byte-by-byte string comparison with search text\n9. When match is found, clamp index to valid range and navigate to item\n10. If no match found or no search text, navigate to default index (0)\n11. Call final navigation function to apply the selection\n\nParameters:\nUses global UI control state and data structures:\n- DAT_6fa09cc0: UI control pointer\n- DAT_6fa09dcc: Item count\n- DAT_6fa09dc8: Copy of item count (for validation)\n- DAT_6f9ebf20: Source item data (0x3b byte structure stride)\n- DAT_6f9fa598: Destination item data buffer\n- DAT_6f9fa5c9: First item field (ushort, offset +0)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Modifies global UI state and triggers navigation to matching item\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Item structure is 0x3b (59) bytes per element\n- String comparison is case-sensitive, byte-by-byte\n- Copy operation handles word (DWORD) and byte remainder separately\n- Empty or null search text defaults to index 0\n- Item count is validated before searching",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:85d742e040880c863ac8ccf9aa1bcda8",
