      "name": "RegisterEntityRecord",
      "signature": "void RegisterEntityRecord(undefined * pEntityRecord)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Registers a new entity record into a global table if not duplicate.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Initialize search index counter to 0\\n2. While current entry count > 0: search for matching entity ID (offset +0x8)\\n3. If match found: return immediately (duplicate prevention)\\n4. Calculate new entry offset (entry_count \\u00d7 0x3b)\\n5. Copy entity ID (short) to array at [offset+0x0]\\n6. Initialize flags (dword) at [offset+0x4] to 0\\n7. Copy status value (short) from offset +0x14 to [offset+0x6]\\n8. Copy first string (from offset +0x1c, up to null terminator) to table\\n9. Copy second string (from offset +0x2c, up to null terminator) to table\\n10. Increment global entry counter (DAT_6fa09dcc)\\n\\nParameters:\\n- pEntityRecord: Pointer to entity record structure with fields:\\n  +0x08: Entity unique ID (short)\\n  +0x14: Status value (short)\\n  +0x1c: First string buffer (null-terminated)\\n  +0x2c: Second string buffer (null-terminated)\\n\\nReturns: void\\n\\nSpecial Cases:\\n- Returns early on duplicate ID to prevent re-registration\\n- Array entry size is fixed at 0x3b (59) bytes\\n- Strings copied are null-terminated and unbounded in source\\n- Global table counter drives array indexing for uniqueness\\n\\nStructure Layout:\\nTable entry (0x3b bytes):\\n  Offset  Size  Field       Type      Description\\n  +0x00   0x2   entityID    short     Unique entity identifier\\n  +0x04   0x4   reserved    dword     Reserved/flags field\\n  +0x08   0x2   status      short     Entity status value\\n  +0x0a   variable string1   char[]    First string (name/label)\\n  variable variable string2   char[]    Second string (description)\\n  Total: 0x3b bytes per entry",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:831c71658c48ab4341d12e2d000647fc",
