      "name": "RenderAndProcessGameUI",
      "signature": "int RenderAndProcessGameUI(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Renders game UI components and processes command dispatch based on entity mode state.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call FUN_6f9dbe00() to initialize rendering state\n2. Load current entity mode from global DAT_6fa09f34 into ESI\n3. Call ValidateAndSetEntityMode() four times for different UI element groups\n4. Process game commands for three UI button groups and store results in DAT_6fa09dbc, DAT_6fa09db0, DAT_6fa09db4\n5. Call dispatch_command_handler() and RenderUnicodeTextInBox() for initial rendering\n6. If entity mode (ESI) == 0: render extended UI panels with rendering text boxes\n7. Calculate render offset using NEG ECX, SBB ECX pattern with constants 0x120e and 0x2ae\n8. Process second command group and render final UI elements\n9. Check entity mode again (0x27c9) for conditional rendering blocks\n10. If entity mode == 0: render large secondary UI panel with many text box elements\n11. Process final command group (DAT_6f9eb950) via ProcessGameCommand()\n12. Call SetGlobalState() with command result\n13. Set DAT_6fa09dc0 = 1 as completion flag\n14. Call NavigateListByIndex() to update list navigation state\n15. Return 1 indicating successful completion\n\nParameters:\nNone (void function), operates on global UI state variables\n\nReturns:\n1 on successful completion\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Entity mode 0 enables extended rendering with additional UI panels\n- Non-zero entity mode skips secondary rendering blocks\n- The function uses magic constants 0x120e and 0x2ae for UI offset calculations\n- Multiple render calls may accumulate partial rendering state across calls\n- Global variables cache command results (DAT_6fa09dbc, DAT_6fa09db0, DAT_6fa09db4)",
