      "signature": "int ValidateProfileSexField(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Validates and processes the profile sex/gender field from Unicode to Windows format.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Check if game mode flag (DAT_6fa09dac) equals 2\\n2. If not active, skip validation and call fallback handler FUN_6f9e1510\\n3. Retrieve three Unicode string values via ValidateAndGetObjectField:\\n   - pSexUnicode: the sex/gender value\\n   - pDescriptionUnicode: profile description\\n   - pLocationUnicode: profile location\\n4. Convert each Unicode string to Windows ANSI format:\\n   - sexBufferWin: 8-byte buffer for sex string\\n   - descriptionBufferWin: 40-byte buffer for description\\n   - locationBufferWin: 204-byte buffer for location\\n5. Build parameter array with pointers to converted strings\\n6. Call virtual function at offset 0x74 of vtable (DAT_6fa0917c)\\n7. Test validation result - if 0 (success), return 1\\n8. If validation fails or mode not active, return 1\\n\\nReturns:\\n  int: Always returns 1 (success/completion)\\n\\nSpecial Cases:\\n  - DAT_6fa09dac != 2: Skips validation logic, goes directly to fallback handler\\n  - Validation result 0 = success, non-zero = failure (both treated same, return 1)\\n  - String conversion handles Unicode to Windows ANSI encoding\\n  - Uses stack-based buffers for temporary string storage",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
