      "name": "ProcessAndIncrementNumericField",
      "signature": "int ProcessAndIncrementNumericField(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Retrieves a numeric field value, applies threshold processing, and converts result to Unicode.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load object context pointer from global [0x6fa09d3c]\n2. Call ValidateAndGetObjectField() to retrieve field value as Unicode string\n3. Convert Unicode string to UTF-8 buffer (max 5 bytes) using toUtf()\n4. Parse UTF-8 string to integer using _atol()\n5. Apply minimum threshold: if value < 99 (0x63), increment by 1\n6. Format result using sprintf with format string at 0x6f9e74e8\n7. Convert formatted string to Unicode and process via ConvertStringToUnicodeAndProcess()\n8. Return success status (1)\n\nParameters:\nNone - Function uses implicit ECX context pointer from global\n\nReturns:\nint - Status code: 1 for success\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Threshold value 99 (0x63) is a sentinel: values below are auto-incremented\n- UTF-8 buffer limited to 5 bytes, truncates longer values\n- Global context pointer at 0x6fa09d3c must be initialized\n- Format string at 0x6f9e74e8 controls output formatting\n\nNotes:\nUses __stdcall calling convention with RET 0x4 cleanup (4 bytes popped by callee)",
