      "name": "RenderGameInfoDialog",
      "signature": "void RenderGameInfoDialog(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Renders game information dialog displaying game name, elapsed time, difficulty level, and party roster with character classes. Uses game dialog control structure in EBX with text and player data arrays.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if game info dialog is active (DAT_6fa09cc4)\n2. Clear existing UI resources\n3. Calculate and render game name string length\n4. Render game name and separators if non-empty\n5. Calculate and format elapsed time (hours:minutes:seconds from milliseconds at offset +0xc)\n6. Render formatted time display\n7. Check difficulty level byte at offset +0x11\n8. If level is 0, render as \"Level X\"\n9. If level is 1-99, calculate level range and render as \"Level X to Y\"\n10. Check player count byte at offset +0x12\n11. If count is 1-7, render player count display\n12. Render separator line\n13. Loop through player roster (count at offset +0x14):\n    - Check if player slot is active (name not null at offset +0x8c + index*0x10)\n    - Render player name\n    - Load player class ID from offset +0x6c at -0x20 (class type)\n    - Switch on class ID 0-6 (Amazon, Sorceress, Necromancer, Paladin, Barbarian, Druid, Assassin)\n    - Load player level from offset +0x6c (ushort)\n    - Format and render \"Level N ClassName\"\n    - Render text box with unicode conversion\n    - Increment loop counter and continue\n14. Navigate dialog list after rendering complete\n\nParameters:\n  IMPLICIT EBX - Game dialog info structure pointer\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nStructure Layout:\n  Offset   Size    Field          Type        Description\n  +0x0c    4       elapsedTime    uint        Milliseconds elapsed\n  +0x10    1       baseLevel      byte        Base difficulty level\n  +0x11    1       levelMod       byte        Level variance modifier\n  +0x12    1       playerCount    byte        Number of active players\n  +0x14    4       totalSlots     int         Total player roster slots\n  +0x2c    N       gameName       char[]      Null-terminated game name\n  +0x6c    N       levels         ushort[]    Player character levels\n  +0x8c    N       names          char[]      Player status indicators\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Time formatting uses divisors: 0xe10 ms/hour, 0x3c s/min\n  - Level range calculation: clamps minimum to 1 and maximum to 99\n  - Player count limited to 1-7 (skips if 0 or 8+)\n  - Class type at offset -0x20 from level pointer for class ID\n  - Sentinel check: levelMod == 100 skips all level rendering",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:13827772c73e490a6b8e0e313085322b",
