      "name": "ValidateStringCharacter",
      "signature": "bool ValidateStringCharacter(byte * pChar)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "bool",
      "comment": "Validates a single character based on global configuration flags.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Load input byte from EAX parameter pointer\\n2. Read global flag word at DAT_6fa09f14 + 0x1eb\\n3. Calculate validation threshold from bits [12:8], divide by 5, add 1\\n4. If flag bit 4 is clear: validate as numeric range (threshold < char - 0x30)\\n5. If flag bit 4 is set: validate as extended range (0x32 < char <= threshold + 0x33)\\n6. Return true if character passes validation, false otherwise\\n\\nParameters:\\n  pChar (byte *) - Pointer to character to validate (passed in EAX)\\n\\nReturns:\\n  (bool) - true if character passes validation, false if invalid\\n\\nSpecial Cases:\\n  - Numeric mode (flag bit 4 clear): expects digits 0-9 with threshold limit\\n  - Extended mode (flag bit 4 set): expects range 0x33-0x39 (3-9) with threshold limit\\n  - Magic values: 0x30 = ASCII '0', 0x32 = ASCII '2', 0x33 = ASCII '3'\\n  - Threshold calculation: (flags >> 8) & 0x1f divides by 5 + 1\\n  \\nStructure Layout:\\n  Offset  Size  Field              Type    Description\\n  0x1eb   2     flagWord           ushort  Configuration flags\\n          [12:8] = threshold bits (0-31)\\n          [4]    = mode bit (0=numeric, 1=extended)\\n          [2:0]  = other control bits",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:82bcdb32105d8145cd81751021240f28",
