      "name": "PrepareAndRenderEncodedText",
      "signature": "void PrepareAndRenderEncodedText(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Prepares and renders encoded text data for UI display.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract control flags from global state (0x6fa09f14 + 0x1eb)\n2. Compute encoding control flags based on bit patterns:\n   - If flag 0x04 set, add control flag 0x04\n   - If flag 0x20 set, add control flag 0x08\n   - Based on threshold checks (0x400, 0x500, 0x800, 0xa00), OR additional flags 0x02 or 0x03\n3. Call vtable function at offset 0x38 with computed control flags to get text data array\n4. For each entry in returned array:\n   a. Initialize entry marker at offset -0x04 to 0x0001\n   b. Copy field from array offset +0x0c (4 bytes)\n   c. Scan first field (null-terminated string)\n   d. Scan second field (null-terminated string)\n   e. Skip to third field and get character code (ASCII value)\n   f. Calculate character range divisor: ((flags >> 8) & 0x1f) / 5 + 1\n   g. Validate character code based on control flags:\n      - If flag 0x04 clear: accept codes 0x30 to (divisor + 0x30)\n      - If flag 0x04 set: accept codes 0x33 to (divisor + 0x33), reject 0x00-0x32\n   h. If valid, copy field data to output buffer, increment entry counter\n   i. If invalid, decrement entry count (skip entry)\n5. Check if rendering needed (DAT_6fa09cc0 != 0)\n6. Call RenderTextInUIControl() to display text\n7. Call FUN_6f9e1f80() for cleanup\n8. On error (null pointer in fields), call CleanupAndAbort and exit with code -1\n\nParameters:\nNone (uses global state and side effects)\n\nReturns:\nvoid (no return value)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- NULL pointer validation: Returns 0xad error code to CleanupAndAbort if field pointer is NULL\n- Character validation: Validates character codes against range based on global flags\n- Rendering optional: Only calls RenderTextInUIControl if DAT_6fa09cc0 is set\n- Entry filtering: Skips invalid entries by decrementing counter without adding to output",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
