      "name": "ProcessEntityCommand",
      "signature": "uint ProcessEntityCommand(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Processes incoming entity command/record by validating, looking up entity in the known entity list, and dispatching to appropriate handler.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate entity mode flags via GetEntityModeFlags() - if 0, return 0\n2. Retrieve entity peer address and name from ValidateAndGetObjectField()\n3. If peer address null, return 0\n4. Convert both unicode strings to Windows encoding using unicode2Win()\n5. Apply title case transformation to both strings via TitleCaseString()\n6. Attempt initial peer address lookup via GetPeerAddress()\n7. If peer lookup succeeds, extract peer address and dispatch command to handler\n8. If peer lookup fails, search entity list (DAT_6fa09dcc count) comparing converted name\n9. For each entity in list (offset stride 0x3b), perform byte-by-byte string comparison\n10. If name matches, extract address value and dispatch to command handler\n11. If no match in main list, call FUN_6f9e39b0() for alternate search path\n12. If alternate search succeeds, perform secondary string comparison against buffer\n13. If secondary comparison matches, dispatch command with alternate address\n14. Return 1 on successful dispatch, 0 on all error paths\n\nParameters:\n(None - uses global entity state)\n\nReturns:\nuint: 1 if command dispatched successfully, 0 if validation failed, entity not found, or error occurred\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Early return (0) if GetEntityModeFlags() returns 0 (entity not ready)\n- Early return (0) if ValidateAndGetObjectField() returns null (invalid entity reference)\n- Dual-path lookup: first tries direct peer address lookup, then entity list search\n- Alternate search path for entities not found in main list via FUN_6f9e39b0()\n- String comparison uses case-sensitive byte-by-byte matching after title case conversion\n- Magic constant 0x3b (59 decimal) is entity record stride in the entity list\n\nStructure Layout:\nEntity List Entry Structure (stride 0x3b):\nOffset | Size | Field Name      | Type       | Description\n------ | ---- | --------------- | ---------- | -----------\n0x00   | 59   | entityName      | char[59]   | Entity name string\n0x27   | 2    | entityAddr      | word       | Entity address/ID value\n0x29   | 30   | reserved        | byte[30]   | Remaining data in entry\n\nTotal size: 59 bytes (0x3b)",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
