      "name": "ProcessEntityConfiguration",
      "signature": "uint ProcessEntityConfiguration(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Processes entity configuration for local or remote clients\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check entity mode flags; return 0 if disabled\n2. Validate and retrieve primary object field (entity name)\n3. Validate that entity name is not empty\n4. Retrieve additional object fields (secondary name, level info)\n5. Check if peer connection exists (local vs remote determination)\n6. If peer connection exists:\n   - Retrieve object structure information\n   - Validate structure type and extract mode bytes\n   - Convert structure data to UTF-8 and parse numeric values\n7. Convert all name/level fields from Unicode to Windows encoding\n8. Apply title case conversion to string buffers\n9. Validate that converted name is not empty\n10. Branch on peer connection:\n    - Local: Apply mode flags to entity at 0x6fa09f14, dispatch command, render updates\n    - Remote: Set level/difficulty parameters via game config API, send to remote\n11. Get local IP address and process via network handler\n12. Verify peer connection still exists after processing\n13. If peer lost: cleanup and return error status\n14. If peer stable: finalize rendering and post-processing\n15. Check if config initialized before returning success\n\nReturns 0 on early validation failures, 1 on successful processing or error conditions",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "CAL",
