      "name": "InitializeLevelRestArea",
      "signature": "void InitializeLevelRestArea(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Initialize the game level rest area with conditional processing based on level type.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call level initialization check function (0x1018bd60) to determine if special processing is needed\n2. If check returns 0 (no special processing): Call simple level init function (0x1018bec0) with level name and game name, then return\n3. If check returns non-zero (special processing needed):\n   a. Load level type value from buffer at [ESP]\n   b. Compare level type to 0x29a (sentinel value for special level type)\n   c. If type matches 0x29a: Load game context from 0x6fa09d40, initialize with EDX=0, call 0x6f9d7c1a, then return\n   d. If type does not match: Format level name string with buffer, set buffer flags (0x34, 0x0), call string formatter (0x6f9d7b9c), process formatted string (0x6f9d7c44), load game context from 0x6fa09d3c, initialize with EDX=1, call 0x6f9d7c1a\n4. After all processing, call finalization function (0x6f9e3de0) and return\n\nParameters:\nNone - Function takes no parameters, uses global game context objects from 0x6fa09d40 and 0x6fa09d3c\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function performs initialization and returns no value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Level type 0x29a triggers simplified initialization path without string formatting\n- Magic constant 0x34 sets buffer format flags\n- Game context objects are loaded from fixed global addresses\n- The function supports two initialization modes: simple (EDX=0) and complex (EDX=1)",
