      "name": "ProcessNetworkInputMessage",
      "signature": "int ProcessNetworkInputMessage(void * pMessageData)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Processes incoming network input messages with throttling and Unicode conversion.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate message by checking structure field (offset +4) for type 0x201\n2. Retrieve current timestamp via GetTickCount()\n3. Check if message throttling limit (500ms) has elapsed since last process\n4. If throttling active, skip processing and return 0\n5. Update global timestamp and last processed message ID with current values\n6. Retrieve peer/connection address from linked list\n7. If peer not found, invoke cleanup handler FUN_6f9e1e20 and return 0\n8. Convert Unicode message string to Windows format into output buffer (256 bytes)\n9. Increment global message counter (with overflow wrap protection)\n10. Store counter value in global state variable\n11. Call ProcessUnicodeWithCallback to handle converted message\n12. Set active UI control to null (0)\n13. Return 0 on success\n\nParameters:\npMessageData (void*): Pointer to network message structure containing:\n  +0x4: Message type field (0x201 = valid input message)\n\nReturns:\nint: 0 on success or early exit (throttled/invalid)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Throttling: Messages processed no faster than 500ms intervals\n- Counter overflow: Message counter wraps from 0xFFFF to 0x0000\n- Peer address lookup: Returns early if peer not found in list\n- Type validation: Only processes messages with type field = 0x201",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
