      "name": "ProcessGameStateDispatch",
      "signature": "int ProcessGameStateDispatch(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Dispatcher function that routes to different game state handlers based on two global flags.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call initialization routine FUN_6f9e1510\n2. Load DAT_6fa09de8 and test if zero\n3. If DAT_6fa09de8 is zero:\n   - Load DAT_6fa09de4 and test if zero\n   - If zero: call FUN_6f9dd460 (both flags clear)\n   - If nonzero: call FUN_6f9dd330 (first flag set, second clear)\n4. If DAT_6fa09de8 is nonzero:\n   - Load DAT_6fa09de4 and test if zero\n   - If zero: call FUN_6f9dd200 (first flag clear, second set)\n   - If nonzero: call FUN_6f9dd0d0 (both flags set)\n5. Push registers EBX, ESI, EDI for FUN_6f9d8620\n6. Call finalization routine FUN_6f9d8620\n7. Restore registers\n8. Return 1 (success status)\n\nReturns:\n- int: Always returns 1 (success)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- The function uses four separate code paths to handle all combinations of two boolean flags\n- Registers EBX, ESI, EDI are preserved across the finalization call\n- DAT_6fa09dd4 is loaded into EBX, possibly for state context",
