      "name": "HexDigitToAscii",
      "signature": "char HexDigitToAscii(int hexValue)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Converts a hexadecimal digit (0-15) to its ASCII character representation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Isolate lower 4 bits of input value using AND 0xF\n2. Compare value with 0xA (10 in decimal)\n3. If less than 10, add 0x30 (ASCII '0') for digits 0-9\n4. If 10 or greater, add 0x37 (ASCII 'A') for hex digits A-F\n5. Return converted ASCII character in EAX\n\nParameters:\n- hexValue (EAX): Hexadecimal digit value (0-15)\n\nReturns:\n- EAX: ASCII character ('0'-'9' or 'A'-'F')\n- Returns '0' + value for 0-9\n- Returns 'A' + (value - 10) for 10-15 (A-F)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Input is masked to 4 bits to ensure value is in range 0-15\n- Magic number 0x30: ASCII code for '0' (48 decimal)\n- Magic number 0x37: ASCII code for '7' (55 decimal, which converts 10 to 'A' when added)\n- Typical usage: Converting binary data to hex string representation (e.g., 0x5C becomes \"5C\")",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:789a0b393b71516e2d61b7d7d26cdbe1",
