      "name": "ConvertHexCharToValue",
      "signature": "int ConvertHexCharToValue(char hexChar)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Converts a hexadecimal character to its numeric value (0-15).\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Sign-extends input character to 32-bit signed integer\\n2. Converts character to lowercase using _tolower\\n3. Checks if character is >= 'a' (0x61) to determine if it's a letter\\n4. If letter ('a'-'f'): returns value - 0x57 to get 10-15\\n5. If digit ('0'-'9'): returns value - 0x30 to get 0-9\\n\\nParameters:\\nhexChar - Character to convert (0-9, a-f, A-F)\\n\\nReturns:\\nint - Numeric value of hex digit (0-15), or undefined for invalid characters\\n\\nSpecial Cases:\\n- Automatically converts uppercase to lowercase via _tolower\\n- No validation of input range; invalid characters produce undefined results\\n- Magic values: 0x61 is 'a', 0x57 converts 'a' to 10, 0x30 converts '0' to 0",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:5af02255e6a0bc42f4ccd1d32cb89114",
