      "name": "LookupByteInTable",
      "signature": "int LookupByteInTable(byte inputByte)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Looks up a byte value in a mapping table and returns the mapped value.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Zero-extends the input byte to 32-bit value using MOVZX\n2. Uses the extended value as an index into the lookup table at DAT_6f9e8010\n3. Sign-extends the mapped byte to a 32-bit signed integer\n4. Returns the sign-extended result\n\nParameters:\n  inputByte: Input byte value to look up (range 0x00-0xFF)\n\nReturns:\n  Mapped byte value sign-extended to int. Returns 0xFF sign-extended (-1) for unmapped entries.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  The lookup table at 0x6f9e8010 (272 bytes) contains a mapping where most entries are 0xFF (sentinel/unmapped),\n  with valid mapped values scattered throughout (0x00-0x17). The table appears to be a character/byte classification\n  or encoding lookup. Most byte values (those with 0xFF in the table) map to -1.",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:af28e6b090ced4ae2e8ae29536c399de",
