      "name": "ValidateLicenseKey",
      "signature": "int ValidateLicenseKey(uint * pKeyValue, uint * pChecksum)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Validates a license key by verifying format, checksum, and cryptographic transformation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Copy input license key string to working buffer\n2. Validate all characters are in whitelist (check against 0x6f9e8010 lookup table)\n3. Convert 16 hex characters to checksum using iterative arithmetic (char value - offset)\n4. Verify calculated checksum matches input checksum parameter (lower byte only)\n5. Perform 16-byte shuffle operation (swap bytes at computed positions)\n6. Apply transformation loop: convert characters and XOR/shift with magic value 0x13ac9741\n7. Split transformed data into two segments (3 bytes and 7 bytes)\n8. Convert each segment from hex to 32-bit integer values\n9. Return success (1) or failure (0)\n\nParameters:\n  pKeyValue: Pointer to 32-bit output for decoded license value (first 3 bytes converted)\n  pChecksum: Pointer to 32-bit input checksum value to validate against (lower byte used)\n\nReturns:\n  1 if license key is valid and decoded successfully\n  0 if validation fails (invalid character, checksum mismatch, or format error)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Checksum algorithm uses 0x30 offset for digit characters ('0'-'9')\n  - Uses 0x57 offset for letter characters ('a'-'f' after tolower)\n  - Character validity checked against lookup table at 0x6f9e8010\n  - Byte shuffling uses stride calculation: offset = (position + (0x16 - position)) & 0xf\n  - Transform applies different XOR patterns based on transformed char value:\n    - If char < '8': XOR with (magic_low & 0x7), then shift magic right 3 bits\n    - If '8' <= char < 'A': XOR with (index & 0x1)\n    - Otherwise: no additional transform\n\nStructure Layout:\n  Working buffer layout (16 bytes total):\n    [0x00] Hex character 0 (digit 0)\n    [0x01] Hex character 1 (digit 1)\n    ...\n    [0x0f] Hex character 15 (digit 15)\n\n  After shuffle, buffer contains permuted hex values\n  After transform, split into:\n    [0x00-0x02] First segment (3 bytes -> 32-bit value)\n    [0x03-0x09] Second segment (7 bytes -> 32-bit value)",
