      "name": "ClearGameEntityStateAndReset",
      "signature": "void ClearGameEntityStateAndReset(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Clears game entity state and resets critical global pointers.\n\nThis function performs critical cleanup of active game entity state when shutting down or resetting the game. It validates the current entity state pointer, clears its data, and initializes game resources if needed.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if pEntityState (DAT_6fa09f08) is non-null\n2. If pEntityState exists, validate member at offset +0x9c (entity reference)\n3. If entity reference is null, call GetReturnAddress(0x84c) to get caller info\n4. Call CleanupAndAbort with error message and return address\n5. Call _exit(-1) to terminate (unreachable after CleanupAndAbort)\n6. If entity reference is valid, call ValidateAndDereferencePointer on it\n7. Load inventory bit mask from gdwInvBitMasks_exref+0x28\n8. AND the validated pointer with inventory bit mask\n9. Call StoreValueWithValidation with entity reference and masked value\n10. Clear pEntityState by setting DAT_6fa09f08 to 0\n11. Set DAT_6f9e9bc0 to 0xffffffff (invalid sentinel)\n12. Check if GameStateGlobalData is null\n13. If null, call FUN_6f9de760 to initialize game resources\n14. Return\n\nParameters:\nNone. Uses global pointers:\n- DAT_6fa09f08: Current entity state pointer (checked at +0x9c for entity reference)\n- gdwInvBitMasks_exref: Inventory bit mask array (field +0x28 used for masking)\n- GameStateGlobalData: Global game state context pointer\n- DAT_6f9e9bc0: Entity state tracking variable\n\nReturns:\nvoid. Always returns after completion or terminates via _exit(-1).\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If pEntityState->offset_9c is null, this is a fatal error condition\n- The function masks the entity reference with an inventory bit mask\n- DAT_6f9e9bc0 is set to 0xffffffff (32-bit all-ones, invalid sentinel)\n- If GameStateGlobalData is zero, FUN_6f9de760 is called for resource init",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
