      "name": "CompareWildcardStrings",
      "signature": "int CompareWildcardStrings(char * pFirstString, char * pSecondString)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Compares two strings, stripping leading wildcard characters ('*').\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Search for first '*' in the first string using strchr\n2. If found, skip past the wildcard character\n3. Search for first '*' in the second string using strchr\n4. If found, skip past the wildcard character\n5. Enter comparison loop: load one byte from each string\n6. Compare bytes; if unequal, return result based on comparison\n7. If byte is null terminator (0x00), strings are equal, return 0\n8. Load second byte from each string (lookahead)\n9. Compare second bytes; if unequal, return comparison result\n10. Advance both pointers by 2 bytes\n11. Check if second byte is null; if not, repeat loop\n12. Return 0 for equal strings, or -1/1 based on byte comparison\n\nParameters:\n  pFirstString [ECX]: First string to compare (char*)\n  pSecondString [EDX]: Second string to compare (char*)\n\nReturns:\n  EAX = 0 if strings are equal\n  EAX = -1 if first string is less than second string\n  EAX = 1 if first string is greater than second string\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Wildcard character '*' (0x2a) at string start is skipped\n  - Comparison processes two bytes at a time for efficiency\n  - Null terminator (0x00) signals end of string\n  - Returns signed comparison: -1 for less, 0 for equal, 1 for greater",
