      "name": "IsValidDispatchCode",
      "signature": "uint IsValidDispatchCode(uint dispatchCode)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Validates whether a dispatch code is in the recognized set.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if dispatch code is greater than 0x9 - return 1 (invalid) if true\n2. Use dispatch code as index into lookup table at 0x6f9de984\n3. Get the lookup byte value and use it as table index for jump table at 0x6f9de97c\n4. Jump to appropriate handler or return code path\n5. Return 0 for valid codes (0, 1, 6, 9), return 1 for invalid codes\n\nParameters:\n- dispatchCode (uint): The dispatch code value to validate (0-based, range 0-9)\n\nReturns:\n- 0 if the dispatch code is in the valid set {0, 1, 6, 9}\n- 1 if the dispatch code is outside valid range or not in recognized set\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Codes > 0x9 are immediately rejected with return value 1\n- Lookup table at 0x6f9de984 contains dispatch validation data\n- Jump table at 0x6f9de97c handles the dispatch branching",
