      "name": "SaveScreenshotFile",
      "signature": "uint SaveScreenshotFile(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Validates and writes screenshot file with extension conversion.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if global filepath buffer at 0x6fa09df0 contains non-empty string\n2. Call GetFileAttributesA to verify file exists and is accessible\n3. If file not found (returns 0xFFFFFFFF), jump to failure path\n4. Find last dot in filepath using _strrchr to locate extension\n5. Extract character after dot and convert to lowercase using _tolower\n6. Call WriteScreenshotToFile with global data pointer, filepath, and lowercase extension\n7. Return 1 on success, 0 if path empty or file not found\n\nParameters:\n(none - operates on global filepath buffer at 0x6fa09df0)\n\nReturns:\nuint - 1 if screenshot written successfully, 0 if filepath empty or file not found\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Global filepath buffer at 0x6fa09df0 must be pre-populated by caller\n- File extension is extracted as single character after dot and converted to lowercase\n- GetFileAttributesA returns 0xFFFFFFFF (-1) when file not found or not accessible\n- Data parameter at 0x6fa09178 passed to WriteScreenshotToFile (purpose unknown without analysis)",
