      "name": "FinalizeCharacterEvent",
      "signature": "int FinalizeCharacterEvent(void * pThis)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Finalizes character event processing by saving temporary files and initializing event modules.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Finalize previous event state for global event data pointer at DAT_6fa09178\n2. Get temporary directory path using GetTempPathA; use '.' as fallback if empty\n3. Create unique temporary file name using GetTempFileNameA with prefix 'BNetAd'\n4. If file creation succeeds (return value non-zero):\n   a. Delete existing temporary file at DAT_6fa09df0\n   b. Create file handle using CreateFileWrapper with flags 0x4, 0x8000000, 0\n   c. If handle valid (not -1):\n      - Write file data [pThis+0x14] to temporary file using WriteFileThunk\n      - Close file handle using CloseResourceHandle\n   d. Extract file extension from string at [pThis+0x8] using _strrchr for '.' character\n   e. Convert extension character to lowercase using _tolower\n   f. Write screenshot to temporary file using WriteScreenshotToFile with converted character\n   g. Copy temporary file path to global buffer DAT_6fa09df0 byte-by-byte until null terminator\n5. Store value from [pThis+0x0] to global DAT_6fa09184\n6. Initialize event modules using InitializeModule with ordinal IDs 0x375 and 0x376\n7. Return 1 indicating successful finalization\n\nParameters:\n  pThis (implicit in ESI) - Pointer to character event context structure with fields:\n    +0x0: dword - Event ID/identifier\n    +0x8: char* - Pointer to filename string (extension extracted using _strrchr)\n    +0x10: dword - Unknown data field (passed to WriteFileThunk)\n    +0x14: dword - File data to write (passed to WriteFileThunk)\n    +0xc: dword - Unknown context field\n\nReturns:\n  int - 1 indicating event finalization completed successfully\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Magic number 0x104 (260 decimal) is MAX_PATH buffer size for temporary path\n  - Magic number 0x2e is '.' character for path fallback and extension separator\n  - Magic number 0x8000000 is file creation flag for CreateFileWrapper\n  - Magic number 0x4 is file access mode parameter\n  - Event module ordinal IDs 0x375 and 0x376 are initialized at end for cleanup\n  - File operations use global buffers: DAT_6fa09178 for event state, DAT_6fa09184 for output ID, DAT_6fa09df0 for file path\n  - String copy loop iterates until null terminator is encountered",
