      "name": "RemoveCommandPrefixFromUnicodeText",
      "signature": "void RemoveCommandPrefixFromUnicodeText(Unicode * pText)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Removes all occurrences of a command prefix from a Unicode string.\n\nThis function validates the input Unicode string length (max 500 chars), retrieves\nthe command prefix from the command dispatcher, searches for and removes all\noccurrences of the prefix from the text, and handles buffer cleanup using memmove.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get input text length and validate it's less than 500 characters (0x1f4)\n2. If invalid (too long), call GetReturnAddress and CleanupAndAbort with error\n3. Retrieve the command prefix from dispatch_command_handler()\n4. Calculate the prefix length in Unicode characters (2 bytes per char)\n5. Search for first occurrence of prefix in text using strstr()\n6. While prefix found and not at null terminator:\n   - Calculate remaining text length after prefix position\n   - Use memmove to shift remaining text left by (prefixLen + 1) characters\n   - Search for next occurrence of prefix\n7. Return after all occurrences removed\n\nParameters:\n  pText (Unicode *): Pointer to null-terminated Unicode string to process\n\nReturns:\n  void: Function modifies input string in-place\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Max input length: 500 Unicode characters (0x1f4)\n  - Null terminator must follow after text for bounds check\n  - memmove used instead of strcpy to handle overlapping memory safely\n  - Command prefix is dynamic (obtained from dispatch_command_handler)",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:0a694ae2875ac098f09eae731545438f",
