      "name": "FormatAndAppendPriorityDecoration",
      "signature": "void FormatAndAppendPriorityDecoration(uint priorityLevel)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Formats and appends priority decoration to channel message output.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 1024-element Unicode buffer (messageBuffer, 2048 bytes) on stack\n2. Allocate 8-element Unicode buffer (priorityUnicodeBuffer, 16 bytes) on stack\n3. Initialize messageBuffer by calling Unicode constructor 512 times (1024 chars)\n4. Initialize priorityUnicodeBuffer by calling Unicode constructor 6 times (8 chars)\n5. Call dispatch_command_handler() to fetch base command string\n6. Copy command string to messageBuffer using strcpy\n7. Format priorityLevel as hexadecimal using wsprintfA into formatBuffer (4 bytes)\n8. Convert hex string to Unicode using toUnicode, store in priorityUnicodeBuffer (3 elements)\n9. Concatenate priority buffer to message using strcat\n10. Check if pOutputBuffer (EBX) contains non-null string at offset +0\n11. If non-null:\n    a. Get length of pOutputBuffer using strlen\n    b. Validate length <= 499 bytes (magic constant 0x1f4)\n    c. If exceeds limit, call GetReturnAddress, CleanupAndAbort, exit with code -1\n    d. Otherwise concatenate pOutputBuffer to messageBuffer\n12. Copy final formatted message from messageBuffer back to pOutputBuffer\n13. Return with callee cleanup (RET 0x4)\n\nParameters:\npriorityLevel (uint) - Priority value to format (typically 0-4 range for message priority tiers)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Formatted message written to pOutputBuffer (implicit EBX parameter)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- pOutputBuffer is implicit parameter in EBX (Diablo II custom convention)\n- formatBuffer allocated as 4 bytes for hex formatting up to 32-bit values\n- priorityUnicodeBuffer pre-allocated for 8 chars but only 3 used\n- messageBuffer allocated as 1024 Unicode characters (2048 bytes total)\n- Validates output buffer doesn't exceed 499 byte limit to prevent overflow\n- If size validation fails, function aborts entire application\n- Magic constant 0x1f4 = 500 decimal, used as buffer safety margin",
