      "name": "ProcessCharacterEventData",
      "signature": "int ProcessCharacterEventData(CharacterEventData * pEventData)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Processes character event data by dispatching to a type-specific handler function.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load event data pointer from parameter (in EAX/pEventData)\n2. Calculate address of event data string at offset +0x18\n3. Scan null-terminated string to find length\n4. Validate event type index at offset +0x0 is less than 0x18\n5. Look up function pointer from dispatch table PTR_LAB_6f9e9bc8 using event type as index\n6. If function pointer exists, call it with string pointer and length\n7. Return function result if non-zero, otherwise return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\n  pEventData - CharacterEventData pointer containing event type and string data\n    Offset +0x0: Event type index (0-23) for dispatch table lookup\n    Offset +0x18: Null-terminated event data string\n\nReturns:\n  int - Result from dispatch function if non-zero, otherwise 1 for success\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Event type 0x18 or higher causes function to skip dispatch and return 1\n  - Null function pointer in dispatch table skips dispatch and returns 1\n  - String scanning loop uses byte-by-byte search for null terminator\n  - Magic value 0x18 (24 decimal) is the dispatch table size limit",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
