      "name": "BuildCharacterPathAndTitle",
      "signature": "void BuildCharacterPathAndTitle(char * pOutputTitle, char * pOutputPath)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Builds character path and title strings by searching linked lists and extracting character attributes.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize both output buffers to empty strings (null terminator only)\n2. Check if input starts with wildcard (*), if yes copy full input and return\n3. Search input for @ symbol (0x40) and * character (0x2a) positions\n4. If @ appears before * (email-style format), truncate at * and return\n5. Iterate through primary linked list (DAT_6fa09ef8) with stride +0x44:\n   a. Compare entry name against input string (case-insensitive)\n   b. If match found, switch to secondary list (DAT_6fa09ef4)\n   c. Otherwise continue to next entry or exit if list empty\n6. Iterate through secondary linked list (DAT_6fa09ef4) with stride +0xb0:\n   a. Compare entry name at offset +4 against input (case-insensitive)\n   b. If match found, retrieve character title and flags:\n      - Load entity pointer from offset +0x9c\n      - Validate pointer state\n      - Check flag bits at offset +0x18 and +0x1c\n      - Extract character class bits (5,6,7,12 from entity flags)\n      - Call GetCharacterTitleString with class index\n      - Copy returned title to pOutputTitle\n   c. Load next entry from offset +0xb0\n7. Copy alternate path string (offset +0x32 from last list entry)\n8. Check if input contains * wildcard:\n   a. If yes, copy bytes before * to output path\n   b. If no, copy full input string to output path\n9. Return with both output buffers populated\n\nParameters:\npOutputTitle: char * - Output buffer for character title/class string (can be empty)\npOutputPath: char * - Output buffer for file path or entry name (always populated)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Both output buffers populated with null-terminated strings\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Magic value 0x7fffffff: Maximum length parameter for CopyMemoryWithAlignment (copy entire string)\n- Email format: @ before * triggers special handling (copy only path component)\n- Wildcard matching: * character acts as path separator and partial match indicator\n- Structure offsets: +0x44 (primary list next), +0xb0 (secondary list next), +0x86 (char class byte),\n  +0x9c (entity pointer), +0x18/+0x1c (flag mask registers), +0x32 (path offset)\n- Character class encoding: 3 bits from positions 5,6,7 combined with bit 12 to index GetCharacterTitleString",
