      "name": "CreateOrFindLinkedListNode",
      "signature": "void CreateOrFindLinkedListNode(char * secondString)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Creates or finds a node in a linked list by comparing two strings split at a separator character. If a matching node is found, copies the second string portion to the output. If not found, allocates a new node and links it to the list.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Parse firstString (in EBX) by finding separator (0x2a, '*'), extract portion before separator\n2. Parse secondString to find separator, extract portion after separator\n3. If list is not empty, search for existing node with matching first string portion\n4. For each node, perform byte-by-byte string comparison with 2-byte optimizations\n5. If match found, copy second string portion to output buffer at node + 0x32\n6. If no match found and list is full (>= 0x400 nodes), remove oldest node from list\n7. Allocate new 0x92c-byte memory block for new node\n8. Copy first string portion to offset 0x0 in new node\n9. Copy second string portion to offset 0x32 in new node\n10. Link new node to previous node (or set as list head if list was empty)\n11. Increment global node counter\n\nParameters:\n- secondString (char*): String to store at offset +0x32 of node; contains part after '*' separator\n\nReturns:\n- void (modifies global linked list structure and global counter at 0x6fa09efc)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Strings may contain separator character 0x2a ('*'); comparison stops at first separator\n- If string has no separator, uses entire string as portion (fallback in empty_string_check)\n- List management: maintains counter 0x6fa09efc and head pointer 0x6fa09ef8\n- When list exceeds 0x400 nodes, removes head node before adding new node\n- Node structure: 0x92c bytes total, strings at +0x0 and +0x32, next pointer at +0x44\n- Memory allocation requests 0x92c bytes via AllocateMemoryWithTracking\n- Returns early from multiple points (stdcall convention, callee cleans 4-byte arg)\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset  Size   Field Name       Type        Description\n0x0     0x32   firstString      char[50]    First string portion (before separator or full string)\n0x32    0xf8   secondString     char[248]   Second string portion (after separator)\n0x44    0x4    nextNode         Node*       Pointer to next node in linked list",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
