      "comment": "Initializes Unicode string arrays from entity template data and configures screenshot display settings.\n\nThis function processes an entity structure and prepares Unicode string representations of entity names, attributes, and paths for screenshot/display rendering. It handles path parsing with a '*' separator to extract path components.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize four Unicode string buffers (0x50 bytes each):\n   - entityNameBuffer: 0x50 bytes at ESP+0x40\n   - pathMask1Buffer: 0x22 bytes at ESP+0x1c\n   - pathExtractBuffer: 0x68 bytes at ESP+0x14c\n   - displayTextBuffer: 0x40 bytes at ESP+0xa8\n2. Check if entity path starts with '*' separator\n3. If path starts with '*', convert remaining path to Unicode in entityNameBuffer\n4. Otherwise, parse path to extract component before '*' separator\n5. If '*' found in path, calculate byte offset from path start to '*' using FindCharInString\n6. Copy bytes before '*' to pathComponentBuffer using word-aligned copy (MOVSD.REP)\n7. If no '*' found, use CopyMemoryWithAlignment to copy entire path (max 0x7fffffff bytes)\n8. Locate character after '*' separator and validate it exists\n9. Convert path component after '*' to Unicode in pathExtractBuffer\n10. Convert base entity name (from offset +0x77c) to Unicode in entityNameBuffer\n11. Concatenate pathExtractBuffer to entityNameBuffer using strncat (max 0x32 bytes)\n12. Convert path component before '*' to Unicode in pathMask1Buffer (max 0x10 bytes)\n13. Check entity type at offset +0x00 for three known entity type signatures:\n    - 0x44324456 (DV2D)\n    - 0x44325354 (TS2D)\n    - 0x44325850 (PX2D)\n14. If entity type matches, load quality flags from offset +0x88, else quality=0\n15. Call InitializeScreenshotConfig with entity structure and all prepared Unicode buffers\n\nParameters:\n- pEntity (Stack[0x4]): Pointer to entity structure containing template data\n  Layout:\n    Offset +0x00: Entity type signature (4 bytes) - checked for DV2D/TS2D/PX2D\n    Offset +0x27: Unit/Screenshot config pointer (4 bytes)\n    Offset +0x46: First display string pointer (4 bytes)\n    Offset +0x88: Quality flags (2 bytes)\n    Offset +0x97: Second display string pointer (4 bytes)\n    Offset +0x9c: Third display string pointer (4 bytes)\n\nReturns:\n- void: No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Path separator: Uses '*' as delimiter to split entity name from path components\n- Entity types: Only entity types matching DV2D/TS2D/PX2D have quality flags extracted\n- String conversion: All strings converted to Unicode format (UTF-16) for display\n- Buffer sizes: Fixed-size buffers prevent overflow (0x50, 0x22, 0x68, 0x40 bytes)\n- Memory alignment: Uses word-aligned (4-byte) copy for path data extraction",
