      "comment": "Parses entity template binary format and extracts configuration data.\n\nThis function decodes a packed binary template string containing entity type information,\nelement configurations, and attribute flags. It validates the format, extracts text fields\ndelimited by commas, decodes packed value fields, and populates the output buffer with\nparsed configuration data.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate input string length by scanning for null terminator\n2. Initialize output buffer word at offset +0x8a to 0\n3. Check flag bits 0x2 (detailed parse), 0x8, 0x1, 0x4, 0x101000 for early exit codes\n4. Validate minimum string length >= 4 bytes for magic value\n5. Load first DWORD (magic value) and compare against known type signatures:\n   - 0x4a535453 (TSTR): Complex template format\n   - 0x4a535452 (TSR): Simple template format\n   - 0x44325850 (XPD2), 0x44324456 (VD2), 0x44325354 (TS2): Expansion templates\n   - 0x43484154 (TACH): Character template\n   - 0x4452544c (LTRD), 0x44534852 (RHSD), 0x44545354 (TSTD): Special formats\n   - 0x5732424e (NB2W), 0x53455850 (PXES), 0x53534852 (RHSS), 0x53544152 (RATS): Standard types\n   - 0x5732424f (OB2W), 0x57335850 (PXSW), 0x57415233 (R3AW): Extended types\n6. For complex formats with comma-delimited structure:\n   a. Parse element name (bytes 0-0x46, delimited by comma)\n   b. Parse element ID string (bytes 0x36-0x46, delimited by comma)\n   c. Decode packed value at offset +0x66 (11 bytes, padded to 16 with 0xff)\n   d. If element defined (first byte != 0):\n      - Decode second packed section (11 bytes padded to 16)\n      - Extract individual bit flags at offsets +0xa0, +0xa4, +0xa8, +0xac\n      - Perform conditional switch on attribute value for type determination\n7. Initialize remaining arrays to default values (0xff padding)\n8. Return status code based on validation results\n\nParameters:\n- pTemplateString (ECX): Pointer to null-terminated binary template string in packed format\n- flagsMask (EDX): Configuration flags controlling parsing behavior (bits: 0x1=format1, 0x2=detailed,\n  0x4=format2, 0x8=format3, 0x101000=special)\n- pOutputBuffer (stack): Pointer to 0xa6-byte output structure where parsed data is written\n\nReturns:\n- EAX: Status/type code (0x0-0x18) indicating entity type and parse result:\n  0x0-0x4: Normal entity types\n  0x7: Invalid/unknown format\n  0x8-0x0d: Conditional type codes based on flags\n  0x0e-0x18: Special format type codes\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- String length < 4: Returns error code 0x7\n- Unknown magic value: Returns error code 0x7 if detailed parse enabled, else code 0x0\n- Missing comma delimiter: Calls CleanupAndAbort with line number 0x56b\n- Complex format with no second section: Skips second parsing, initializes to defaults\n- Attribute value 0xff: Converts to 0 (sentinel value)\n- Loop initialization: Fills array slots with 0xff for padding, slot 1 always set to 0\n\nStructure Layout (pOutputBuffer offsets):\n  Offset  Size  Field Name          Type      Description\n  +0x00   4     magicValue          uint      Entity type identifier (DWORD)\n  +0x04   64    elementName         char[64]  Element name string\n  +0x36   16    elementId           char[16]  Element ID/template string\n  +0x46   16    reserved1           byte[16]  Reserved/padding area\n  +0x66   16    flagsArray1         byte[16]  First packed flags array (11 bytes + 5 padding)\n  +0x76   16    flagsArray2         byte[16]  Second packed flags array (11 bytes + 5 padding)\n  +0x8a   2     statusFlags         ushort    Parse result flags\n  +0x8c   2     decodedField1       ushort    Decoded value from first section\n  +0x8e   2     decodedField2       ushort    Decoded value from second section\n  +0x94   1     attributeByte1      byte      Attribute value (0=normal, 0xff=invalid)\n  +0x95   1     attributeByte2      byte      Second attribute byte\n  +0x96   1     attributeByte3      byte      Third attribute byte\n  +0xa0   4     bitFlag1            dword     Bit 2 extract (0 or 1)\n  +0xa4   4     bitFlag2            dword     Bit 3 extract (0 or 1)\n  +0xa8   4     bitFlag3            dword     Bit 5 extract (0 or 1)\n  +0xac   4     bitFlag4            dword     Bit 6 extract (0 or 1)",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
