      "comment": "Inserts entities into a priority queue sorted by entity state priority.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if DAT_6fa09ef4 (queue head) is initialized\n2. If head exists: Extract entity from offset 0xb0, compute priority from state flags\n3. If no head: Iterate through all items in main list (DAT_6fa09ef4), process each item\n4. For each item: Compute priority value based on entity state flags (offset +0x90)\n5. For queue items: Compare computed priority against existing queue nodes using insertion sort\n6. For main list items: Call SetObjectProperty then StoreValueWithValidation with computed flags\n7. Calculate property type offset incrementally (starting 0x46, +0x3c per item)\n8. Loop until all items processed or queue becomes empty\n\nPriority Calculation:\n- Check flags at offset +0x90 (bits 1, 2, 8): determines priority value 0-4\n- Bit 2 set = priority 4, Bit 8 set = priority 3, Bit 1 set = priority 2\n- Bits 1,2,8 all clear = extract bit 2 from (value >> 2) & 1\n\nItem Processing Path Selection:\n- Main list items: range check at offset +0x10 (DAT_6fa09f04)\n- Queue items: fallback path with SetObjectProperty call\n- Property type field at offset +0x9c passed to SetObjectProperty\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Head pointer may be cleared during initial processing (offset 0xb0)\n- Sentinel check: DAT_6fa09f08 determines flag operations at offset +0x90 bit 5\n- Head reset to NULL after single item processing\n- Insertion sort maintains priority order in queue",
