      "name": "FormatAndRenderChannelMessage",
      "signature": "void FormatAndRenderChannelMessage(char * formattedMessage, char * destinationBuffer, uint outputPriority, uint outputType)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Formats and renders a Unicode chat/channel message with priority and type flags.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Allocate two Unicode buffers (0x240 chars = 1152 bytes each) on stack\\n2. Initialize first buffer by calling Unicode constructor 0x240 times (576 iterations of 2 chars)\\n3. Initialize second buffer by calling Unicode constructor 0x240 times\\n4. Convert formattedMessage ANSI string to Unicode in first buffer (max 0x240 chars)\\n5. Convert destinationBuffer ANSI string to Unicode in second buffer (max 0x240 chars)\\n6. Process first Unicode buffer (normalization/transformation via FUN_6f9deb70)\\n7. Process second Unicode buffer (normalization/transformation via FUN_6f9deb70)\\n8. Append second Unicode buffer to first buffer using strcat\\n9. Call FUN_6f9dec80 with outputPriority to format priority decoration\\n10. Call FUN_6f9ded60 with outputType to format type decoration\\n11. Check if callback pointer at DAT_6fa0a0c8 is non-null\\n12. If callback set, call RenderTextBoxUnicodeText with outputType, 0, 1\\n13. Return via RET 0x10 (callee cleanup of 4 params)\\n\\nParameters:\\nformattedMessage (char *) - ANSI string containing formatted message (e.g., \\\"<User>\\\")\\ndestinationBuffer (char *) - ANSI string for output destination/channel name\\noutputPriority (uint) - Priority flags controlling message rendering level (0-4 or 0-3)\\noutputType (uint) - Message type flags (0=normal, 1=error, 2=warning, 3=special)\\n\\nReturns:\\nvoid - Result rendered via RenderTextBoxUnicodeText callback if enabled\\n\\nSpecial Cases:\\n- Two-stage Unicode conversion: input formatting + destination buffering\\n- Unicode buffer size fixed at 0x240 (576 bytes per buffer, 1152 bytes total)\\n- Magic constant 0x240 (576 decimal) represents max Unicode string length\\n- If callback disabled (DAT_6fa0a0c8 = 0), text prepared but not rendered\\n- outputPriority values: 0=highest priority, 4=default, 3=special\\n- outputType values: encoded as bit flags, checked in conditional rendering\\n\\nStructure Layout:\\nUnicode strings accessed at offsets from ESP:\\nESP+0xc: first Unicode buffer (unicodeBuffer1, 1152 bytes)\\nESP+0x48c: second Unicode buffer (unicodeBuffer2, 1152 bytes)\\nDAT_6fa0a0c8: global callback pointer for text rendering",
