      "name": "ConvertUtf8TextToUnicodeAndRender",
      "signature": "int ConvertUtf8TextToUnicodeAndRender(char * pUtf8Text, uint displayHandle)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Convert UTF-8 text to Unicode format and optionally render to display.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 1152-element Unicode buffer on stack (0x480 bytes)\n2. Initialize all Unicode array elements via constructor loop (0x240 iterations)\n3. Convert input UTF-8 string to Unicode using utf8ToUnicode (max 0x240 elements)\n4. Process converted text via FUN_6f9deb70 text processing function\n5. Check global render flag (DAT_6fa0a0c8)\n6. If flag set: render Unicode text to display handle\n7. Return 1 (success code)\n\nParameters:\n- pUtf8Text (char*): Input UTF-8 encoded text string to convert\n- displayHandle (uint): Target display/window handle for rendering\n\nReturns:\n- 1 (int): Always returns success code\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Conditional rendering controlled by global flag DAT_6fa0a0c8\n- If flag is 0, text is converted and processed but not rendered\n- Buffer size fixed at 0x240 Unicode elements",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
