      "name": "DisplayChannelFullMessage",
      "signature": "int DisplayChannelFullMessage(int channelIndex, int param2)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Displays a \"channel is full\" error message to the player.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Retrieve the channel index from stack (param 1)\n2. Allocate 500-byte buffer on stack for message formatting\n3. Format message using sprintf with template string and channel index\n4. Call display function to render message to player\n5. Return success code (1)\n\nParameters:\n- channelIndex: Index of the chat channel that became full\n- displayMode: Display mode or flags parameter\n\nReturns:\n- 1: Success\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Uses fixed 500-byte buffer for message formatting\n- Calls internal display function (FUN_6f9dfc90) with display parameter\n\nStructure Layout:\n- Stack frame size: 500 bytes (0x1f4)\n- Message buffer: [ESP+4] to [ESP+4+500]",
