      "name": "FindMatchingEntryAndFormat",
      "signature": "void FindMatchingEntryAndFormat(char * pDestBuffer)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Finds matching entry from global linked list and formats output with entry name and flags.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize output priority to 4 and output type to 0 (default values)\n2. Call vtable function at DAT_6fa0917c[0x18] with 0x7fffffff to get initial data\n3. Copy returned data into local buffer using CopyMemoryWithAlignment\n4. Iterate through linked list starting at DAT_6fa09ef4 (offset +0xb0 is next pointer)\n5. For each entry, find '*' character in entry name at offset +4 using FindCharInString\n6. If '*' found and character after it exists, use substring after '*' for comparison\n7. Otherwise use full entry name from offset +4 for comparison\n8. Perform byte-by-byte string comparison against initial data buffer (case-sensitive)\n9. If match found, extract entry flags from offset +0x90\n10. Check flag bits: if bit 1 (0x2) set, output priority = 0; if bits 0 (0x1) or 3 (0x8) set, both priority and type = 3\n11. Copy matched entry name back into buffer, break from search loop\n12. Call FUN_6f9deea0 to build secondary output string in separate buffer\n13. Calculate length of secondary output string by scanning for null terminator\n14. If secondary string empty, use initial buffer data in format string\n15. Otherwise format as \"<%s,%s>\" with both strings using _sprintf\n16. Call FUN_6f9dfbb0 with formatted result, destination buffer, priority and type values\n\nParameters:\npDestBuffer: char * - Destination buffer for formatted output string\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Result written to pDestBuffer via FUN_6f9dfbb0 call\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Empty list (DAT_6fa09ef4 = 0): uses initial buffer data directly\n- Wildcard in entry name: matches substring after last '*' character\n- Flag byte at offset +0x90 controls output priority/type classification",
