      "name": "FormatChannelMessage",
      "signature": "void FormatChannelMessage(char * nickname, undefined4 messageParam2, undefined4 messageParam3)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Formats a channel message by prepending sender nickname in angle brackets format.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 256-byte buffer on stack (messageBuffer)\n2. Call sprintf to format message with pattern \"<%s> \" where %s is the nickname\n3. Call FUN_6f9dfbb0 with formatted buffer and original message parameters\n4. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\nnickname (char *) - The sender's nickname/username to prepend in angle brackets\nmessageParam2 (undefined4) - Additional message parameter passed to FUN_6f9dfbb0\nmessageParam3 (undefined4) - Additional message parameter passed to FUN_6f9dfbb0\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value; output handled through FUN_6f9dfbb0\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Buffer is fixed at 256 bytes; nickname + 4 characters (\"<%s> \") must fit\n- Format string is located at 0x6f9e7718 and contains pattern \"<%s> \"\n- Typical IRC/chat message formatting (e.g., \"<User> message content\")",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
