      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Wrapper function that converts a UTF-8 text string to Unicode format.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Accepts a pointer to a UTF-8 encoded text string as parameter\n2. Calls FUN_6f9dfc90 to process the string with conversion and initialization\n3. Passes 0 as the second parameter (no rendering/display mode)\n4. Returns success status (1)\n\nParameters:\n- pTextString (char*): Pointer to null-terminated UTF-8 encoded text string to process\n\nReturns:\n- 1: Success status (always returns success)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- The function always returns 1 regardless of input validity\n- No input validation is performed on the text pointer\n- The actual Unicode conversion is delegated to FUN_6f9dfc90\n- Second parameter to FUN_6f9dfc90 is always 0 (no rendering)",
