      "name": "InitializeEntityFromTemplate",
      "signature": "void InitializeEntityFromTemplate(uint * pEntity, uint entityId, byte * pTemplateName)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Initializes an entity from template data and sets up unit armor configuration.\n\nThis function is called when a matching entity template is found in the global entity list, or when allocating a new entity. It performs entity initialization including template loading, entity type determination, expansion data validation, and unit armor setup based on entity characteristics.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Store entityId at entity offset +0x90 (entity mode flags field)\n2. Call FUN_6f9df340 to determine entity type based on template\n3. Copy template data to entity using CopyMemoryWithAlignment with maximum buffer size (0x7fffffff)\n4. Check if entity has flags 0x4 (expansion) set and flag 0x8 (expansion2) NOT set\n5. If expansion conditions met, call FindAndValidateD2ExpMpq to validate expansion data\n6. If validation fails OR entity type is less than 5, set armorType to 1 (basic armor)\n7. Otherwise keep armorType as 5 (normal armor)\n8. Call InitializeUnitArmorData with armorType and entity structure offsets +0x66, +0x76, +0x9c\n9. Call FUN_6f9df170 to finalize entity setup\n10. Call FUN_6f9df750 to complete initialization sequence\n11. Return (RET 0x4 pops return address and 4-byte parameter)\n\nParameters:\n- pEntity (ECX): Implicit __fastcall pointer to entity structure (begins at offset 0x00)\n- entityId (EDX): Entity identifier/configuration flags (stored at offset +0x90)\n- pTemplateName (stack): Pointer to template name string (unused, for reference)\n\nReturns:\n- void: No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Expansion validation: Checks for Diablo II expansion compatibility before initializing armor\n- Armor type selection: Uses entity type (from FUN_6f9df340) to determine armor initialization mode\n- Template data: Copies all template data with 0x7fffffff limit for safety\n- Entity structure: Assumes entity structure with armor data at offsets +0x66, +0x76, +0x9c\n\nStructure Layout:\nEntity structure (inferred from offsets):\n  Offset  Size  Field Name         Type      Description\n  +0x00   4     pPrevious          void*     Previous entity in linked list\n  +0x04   256   szEntityName       char[]    Entity name string\n  +0x66   16    inventorySlots     byte[]    Inventory item slots (armor equipped)\n  +0x76   16    inventoryMasks     byte[]    Inventory masks (item flags)\n  +0x8a   2     flags              ushort    Entity mode/status flags\n  +0x90   4     entityId           uint      Entity ID and configuration\n  +0x9c   4     pUnit              void*     Pointer to allocated unit instance",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "CAL",
