      "name": "UpdateBoundedGameStateCounter",
      "signature": "void UpdateBoundedGameStateCounter(void * pUnused, int incrementValue)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Update a bounded game state counter with automatic clamping and state change notification.\n\nThis function manages a global game state counter with value bounds checking. It increments a counter\nby a specified amount while ensuring it stays within configured limits [0, max_threshold - 0xb].\nIf the counter value changes, it triggers a state update callback and modifies associated bitfield flags.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load current counter value and threshold limit from global state\n2. Check if threshold is below minimum (0xc); if so, reset counter to 0\n3. Otherwise, add increment value to current counter\n4. Clamp result to valid range [0, max_threshold - 0xb]\n5. If counter value changed from original, call update handler FUN_6f9df750\n6. Call ModifyObjectBitfield 4 times with change flags for state propagation\n7. Return with no value\n\nParameters:\n- pUnused: unused parameter (fastcall convention, ECX register)\n- incrementValue: amount to add to counter (EDX register)\n\nReturns: void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Threshold < 0xc: counter immediately reset to 0 (early exit path)\n- Negative increment or zero: result clamped to [0, max - 0xb] range\n- Counter unchanged: update handler not called, only bitfield operations execute\n- Bitfield flags indicate counter changed state for 4 related objects",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:46aa4ecb88d4daf50598d9fed1bf364e",
