      "name": "ValidateWildcardPattern",
      "signature": "void ValidateWildcardPattern(byte * pPatternString)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Validates a wildcard pattern string and outputs formatted validation message.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Copy base string from EDI to buffer at 0x6fa09198 until null terminator\n2. Check if pPatternString is empty (first byte is 0x00)\n   - If empty: use default format string\n   - If not empty: check for wildcard asterisk (0x2a) as first character\n3. For non-asterisk patterns:\n   - Format and output the pattern string directly\n4. For asterisk patterns (wildcard matching):\n   - Find asterisk position in base string using FindCharInString\n   - Use character after asterisk (or entire base string if no asterisk)\n   - Find asterisk position in pPatternString\n   - Use character after asterisk (or entire pPatternString if no asterisk)\n   - Compare pattern strings byte-by-byte in pairs\n   - Perform two-byte comparison loop with character-by-character validation\n   - If all characters match and both strings end: match success (iVar3 = 0)\n   - If any mismatch: match failed (iVar3 = -1 or 1)\n5. If match result is non-zero: output formatted pattern string\n6. Call FUN_6f9dfc90 with formatted buffer and parameter 2 for output/logging\n\nParameters:\npPatternString (byte *): Pointer to pattern string to validate; supports asterisk (*) as wildcard character\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value; outputs formatted validation message via FUN_6f9dfc90\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Empty pattern string: Uses default format from 0x6f9e7608\n- Wildcard patterns (containing *): Performs pattern matching comparison logic\n- Pattern format strings: Located at 0x6f9e75f0 (default) and 0x6f9e7608 (empty)\n- Two-byte comparison optimization in main loop\n- Null terminator handling: Strings must be null-terminated for safe processing",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
