      "name": "FindListNodeByString",
      "signature": "uint FindListNodeByString(void * this, void * pListContext, byte * pSearchString)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Searches a linked list for a node containing a matching string.\n\nThis function performs a case-sensitive byte-pair comparison against string data\nstored at offset +4 in each linked list node. For each node in the linked list\nstarting from DAT_6fa09ef4, it compares the input search string against the node's\nstring data using an optimized 2-byte-at-a-time comparison loop. When a match is\nfound, it calls FUN_6f9e0410 (presumably a handler function) and returns 1 to\nindicate success. If no matching node is found after traversing the entire list,\nit returns 0.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load the head of the linked list from DAT_6fa09ef4\n2. If the list is empty (null), jump to return_not_found (return 0)\n3. For each node in the list:\n   a. Load the string data from offset +4 of the current node\n   b. Initialize both pointers to the start of their respective strings\n   c. Compare the strings byte-pair-wise (2 bytes per iteration for efficiency)\n   d. If any byte pair differs, mark comparison as failed and advance to next node\n   e. If a null terminator is found (indicating end of string), strings match\n   f. If all bytes match completely, call FUN_6f9e0410 with this and search\n      string, then return 1\n4. If strings don't match, load the next node pointer from offset +0xb0 of\n   current node\n5. If next node pointer is non-null, repeat step 3 with next node\n6. If next node pointer is null, exit loop and return 0\n\nParameters:\n- this (ECX): Implicit context pointer, passed to FUN_6f9e0410 if match found\n- pListContext: Unused parameter (reserved)\n- pSearchString: Pointer to null-terminated search string (null-terminated ASCII)\n\nReturns:\n- EAX: 1 if matching node found and handler called, 0 if no match found\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Empty list: Returns 0 immediately\n- Handler invocation: FUN_6f9e0410 is called when a match is found before returning\n- String matching: Uses optimized 2-byte comparison for efficiency; matching is\n  case-sensitive and null-terminator sensitive\n- List traversal: Continues through all nodes via the next pointer at offset\n  +0xb0 until end of list (null pointer)\n\nStructure Layout:\nList Node structure (inferred from offsets):\n  Offset  Size  Field Name      Type        Description\n  +0x00   4     pPrevious       void*       Previous node pointer (not used)\n  +0x04   N     szString        char[]      Null-terminated string data\n  +0xb0   4     pNext           void*       Next node pointer in linked list",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
