      "name": "ClearGameEntityState",
      "signature": "void ClearGameEntityState(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Clears and resets all game entity state structures during game state transitions.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize local buffer (256 bytes) and register variables (EBX=0, EDI, ESI)\n2. Call FUN_6f9de860 (unknown function, likely state initialization)\n3. Load first entity list pointer from global DAT_6fa09ef4\n4. If first entity list exists (ESI != 0):\n   a. Loop through first entity list (DAT_6fa09ef4)\n   b. For each entity: extract pointer at offset +0xb0 as next entity\n   c. Call function at 0x6f9d7d22 with entity+0x9c parameter\n   d. Call function at 0x6f9d7bf0 with error code 0x814\n   e. Zero out entity+0x9c field\n   f. Continue until next pointer (EDI) is null\n5. Load second entity list pointer from global DAT_6fa09ef8\n6. Zero out first entity list pointer (DAT_6fa09ef4)\n7. If second entity list exists (ECX != 0):\n   a. Loop through second entity list (DAT_6fa09ef8)\n   b. For each entity: extract pointer at offset +0x44 as next entity\n   c. Call function at 0x6f9d7bf0 with error code 0x81c\n   d. Continue until next pointer (ESI) is null\n8. Zero out second entity list pointer (DAT_6fa09ef8)\n9. Call function at 0x6f9d1000 (sprintf-like with format string)\n10. Call FUN_6f9dfb40 (unknown function, likely UI processing)\n11. Call FUN_6f9e04d0 (unknown function)\n12. Zero out globals at DAT_6fa09efc, DAT_6fa09f00, DAT_6fa09f04\n13. Return (via RET instruction, stdcall cleanup)\n\nParameters:\nNone (void function)\n\nReturns:\nvoid (no return value)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Global state structure pointers: DAT_6fa09ef4, DAT_6fa09ef8, DAT_6fa09efc, DAT_6fa09f00, DAT_6fa09f04\n- Magic error codes: 0x814 and 0x81c used in cleanup operations\n- First entity list structure: next pointer at offset +0xb0, field to clear at offset +0x9c\n- Second entity list structure: next pointer at offset +0x44\n- Function always returns (not noreturn), used in both join and shutdown sequences\n- Called after JoinChannel (game state transition) and during game shutdown (FUN_6f9de150)",
