      "name": "RemoveNodeFromListByName",
      "signature": "void RemoveNodeFromListByName(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Searches linked list and removes node matching by name.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Load head node from global pointer DAT_6fa09ef4\\n2. If list is empty (head is null), skip search loop\\n3. For each node in linked list (iterate via offset 0xb0):\\n   a. Extract node name from offset +4\\n   b. Perform case-insensitive string comparison with wildcard support\\n   c. If names match, proceed to removal step (break loop)\\n   d. If names don't match, load next node via offset 0xb0\\n4. When match found:\\n   a. If logging enabled (DAT_6fa0a090 non-zero):\\n      - Format message \\\"%s has left the channel\\\" using node name\\n      - Call logging function FUN_6f9dfc90\\n   b. Unlink node from linked list (update predecessor)\\n   c. If node is current (DAT_6fa09f08 equals node), call FUN_6f9de860\\n   d. Cleanup screenshot resource at offset 0x9c\\n   e. Call InitializeModule(0x7f0, 0) for cleanup\\n5. Decrement global counter DAT_6fa09f00\\n6. Format and output status message with counter value\\n7. Call final cleanup functions FUN_6f9dfb40, FUN_6f9e04d0, FUN_6f9df750\\n\\nReturns: void\\n\\nSpecial Cases:\\n- Empty list: head pointer is null (DAT_6fa09ef4 == 0), skips search loop\\n- Wildcard support: asterisk (*) at start of names skips prefix matching\\n- Logging flag: DAT_6fa0a090 controls whether removal message is logged\\n- Current node cleanup: If removing currently active node, additional cleanup required\\n- Uninitialized counter: Decrements global counter regardless of removal success\\n\\nStructure Layout (Node at EBP):\\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description\\n0x0    | 4    | reserved   | uint | Padding/reserved\\n0x4    | var  | nodeName   | char*| Null-terminated node name string\\n0x36   | var  | extName    | char*| Extended name field (may be null)\\n0x9c   | 4    | screenshot | ptr  | Screenshot resource pointer\\n0xb0   | 4    | nextNode   | ptr  | Next node in linked list (offset from head)",
