      "name": "JoinChannel",
      "signature": "int JoinChannel(int channelId, char * channelName)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Handles channel join operation by updating game state structures with channel name.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Format and display \"You have joined channel: <name>\" message\n2. Copy channel name to primary game state location (offset from global DAT_6fa08d48)\n3. Copy channel name to alternate game state structure (offset from DAT_6fa09f14)\n4. If flag at gameStatePtr+0x37d is clear, copy to additional state location\n5. Iterate through entity bitfield array (DAT_6fa08e50 to DAT_6fa08e7c) and modify bitfields\n6. Update entity state flags via ModifyEntityStateBitFlags()\n7. Execute post-join processing via FUN_6f9e0aa0()\n8. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\n  channelId (int) - Channel identifier (unused in visible code, may be context parameter)\n  channelName (char *) - Pointer to channel name string to join\n\nReturns:\n  1 - Operation completed successfully\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Conditional state copy at offset gameStatePtr+0x37d checks if location already populated\n  - Array bounds: 0x6fa08e50 to 0x6fa08e7c (44 bytes, likely 11 dwords)\n  - String copy operations use null terminator for length determination",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
