      "name": "RemoveNodeByName",
      "signature": "int RemoveNodeByName(char * pSearchName)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Removes a node from a linked list by matching its name against a search string.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Preserve EBX register (contains implicit context)\n2. Load search name parameter from stack into EBX\n3. Call linked list traversal function to find and remove matching node\n4. Return success status (1)\n5. Restore EBX and clean up stack\n\nParameters:\npSearchName - Pointer to null-terminated search string used to locate the node to remove\n\nReturns:\n1 (success) in EAX. The actual removal is performed by FUN_6f9e0b70 which handles linked list manipulation.\n\nSpecial Cases:\nThe function uses __stdcall convention with EBX as an implicit parameter register passed to the called function. The return value is always 1, regardless of whether a matching node was found or not.",
