      "comment": "Notifies observers when a user joins a channel by formatting and displaying a join message.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Call FUN_6f9e0d10 to retrieve user structure for given userId\\n2. Check if DAT_6fa0a090 (logging enabled) flag is set\\n3. If disabled, skip to function exit\\n4. Extract username string from user structure at offset +0x36\\n5. Calculate string length by scanning until null terminator\\n6. Check if username length is non-zero\\n7. Call sprintf to format message with username into local buffer\\n8. Call FUN_6f9dfc90 to output formatted message to chat system\\n9. Return to caller\\n\\nParameters:\\nuserId (uint) - The user ID to create join notification for; passed in ECX register\\n\\nReturns:\\nvoid - No return value\\n\\nSpecial Cases:\\n- If DAT_6fa0a090 is 0, logging is disabled and function exits without output\\n- Username string must be null-terminated at user_struct + 0x36\\n- If username length is 0, sprintf is called without length parameter\\n- Otherwise sprintf uses calculated length to format the message properly\\n\\nStructure Layout:\\nUserData Structure (partial):\\nOffset  Size  Field Name  Type    Description\\n------  ----  ----------  ------  -----------\\n+0x36   var   username    char[]  Null-terminated username string",
