      "name": "InitializeEntityFromScript",
      "signature": "void InitializeEntityFromScript(uint configValue, byte * configString)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Adapter function that initializes an entity from script configuration parameters.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Preserve EAX, ECX (configValue), and EDX (configString) registers on stack\n2. Call InitializeEntityConfiguration with three implicit parameters:\n   - EAX: carries additional state/return value from caller\n   - ECX (configValue): numeric configuration parameter\n   - EDX (configString): configuration string reference\n3. Return to caller after entity initialization\n\nParameters:\nconfigValue (ECX): Configuration numeric value or identifier passed from caller\nconfigString (EDX): Pointer to configuration string or script directive\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No explicit return value; side effects are entity initialization\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- EAX is implicitly preserved and passed to callee, indicating return value forwarding\n- Register preservation pattern (PUSH EAX/ECX/EDX) maintains caller's register state\n- Function acts as a thunking layer between script execution and internal initialization",
