      "signature": "undefined4 CreateOrFindEntityByName(void * this, void * pEntityManager, byte * pEntityName, uint entityId)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Factory wrapper to create or find an entity by name.\\n\\nThis function wraps the entity initialization logic (FUN_6f9e0d10)\\nand reorders parameters to match the called function's signature.\\nIt always returns 1 to indicate successful creation/lookup.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Load pEntityName from stack [ESP+0x8]\\n2. Push this pointer (implicit in __thiscall)\\n3. Load entityId from stack [ESP+0x8] (adjusted after PUSH)\\n4. Push pEntityName as second parameter\\n5. Push entityId as third parameter\\n6. Call FUN_6f9e0d10 to create or find entity\\n7. Set return value to 1 (success)\\n8. Return to caller with 0x8 bytes cleanup\\n\\nParameters:\\n- pEntityManager: void* - Manager object (implicit this in ECX)\\n- pEntityName: byte* - Name identifier for the entity\\n- entityId: uint - Entity ID or reference value\\n\\nReturns:\\n- undefined4: Always 1 (success status)",
