      "name": "InitializeGameConfig",
      "signature": "int InitializeGameConfig(int configMode)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Initializes game configuration parameters based on system initialization status.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call initialize_system_state() to initialize core system resources\n2. Check if initialization returned status code 9 (success condition)\n3. If successful (status == 9), populate 20 global configuration variables with predefined values:\n   - Color palette values (0x62, 0x151, 0x177, 0x74, 0x65, 0x60, 0x81, 0xb7, 0xee, 0x12d, 0xcd)\n   - Display and rendering parameters (0x82, 0xb6)\n4. Store the input configMode parameter to global _DAT_6fa0a0f4\n5. Return success status (1) regardless of initialization result\n\nParameters:\n  configMode (int): Game configuration mode or parameter passed as stack argument\n\nReturns:\n  1 - Always returns 1 (success) whether configuration values were applied or not\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - The function assigns configuration values only when initialize_system_state() returns exactly 9\n  - The configMode parameter is always stored to global _DAT_6fa0a0f4 regardless of initialization status\n  - Multiple global variables receive hardcoded values that appear to be display/color configuration constants\n  - Magic numbers: 0x9 is the success code from initialize_system_state()\n\nCalling Convention: __stdcall (parameters on stack, callee cleanup with RET 0xc)",
