      "name": "InitializeUIRenderingParameters",
      "signature": "int InitializeUIRenderingParameters(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Initializes rendering system parameters for UI display.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocates stack space for three 4-byte local buffers\n2. Sets buffer parameters: bufferSize1=8, bufferSize2=0x28, bufferSize3=0xc8\n3. Retrieves virtual method pointer from DAT_6fa0917c+0x7c\n4. Calls virtual method with DAT_6fa09188 address and buffer parameters\n5. Tests result: if non-zero, jumps to rendering initialization\n6. Otherwise checks DAT_6fa09118 flag: if non-zero, calls InitializeRenderingState\n7. Loads return value 1 into EAX\n8. Cleans stack and returns with callee cleanup\n\nParameters:\n- None: Function takes no parameters\n\nReturns:\n- EAX (int): Returns 1 (success) after initialization\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Initializes rendering even if virtual method returns 0 when DAT_6fa09118 is non-zero\n- Uses callee cleanup (RET 0x4) indicating __stdcall convention\n- Buffer sizes (8, 40, 200 bytes) are hardcoded configuration values\n- Virtual method pointer indirection allows runtime resolution of rendering backend",
