      "name": "DisplaySecurityErrorDialog",
      "signature": "void DisplaySecurityErrorDialog(int nErrorType)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Displays a modal dialog showing security error messages and exits the program.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save security cookie for stack overflow detection (loaded from g_dwStackGuardSeed)\n2. Check if custom security error handler is installed (g_pfnSecurityErrorHandler)\n3. If custom handler exists, call it with errorType and return early\n4. If no custom handler, determine error message based on errorType:\n   - errorType == 1: Buffer overrun (use szBufferOverrunDetected title, szBufferOverrunDescription body)\n   - errorType != 1: Unknown security failure (use szUnknownSecurityFailure title, szUnknownSecurityErrorDescription body)\n5. Retrieve module path using GetModuleFileNameA via g_pfnGetModuleFileNameA\n6. If module path retrieval fails, use szUnknownProgramName as fallback\n7. Truncate module path if length exceeds 0x31 bytes (keeps relative path)\n8. Allocate stack buffer for concatenated error message\n9. Build message by concatenating: error title, module path, ellipsis (szEllipsis), error description\n10. Display message box with MessageBoxA via g_pfnStringConcatenate (indirect call)\n11. Call runtime library error handler (address at 0x6fbfdbe8)\n12. Exit program with code 3 via __exit\n\nParameters:\n  errorType (int) - Error type indicator: 1 = buffer overrun, other values = unknown security failure\n\nReturns:\n  void - Function never returns (calls exit)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Custom handler path (g_pfnSecurityErrorHandler != 0): Jumps to custom handler and exits early\n  - Module path too long (length > 0x31): Truncates path, only keeps later portion\n  - GetModuleFileNameA failure: Falls back to szUnknownProgramName constant\n\nStructure Layout - Error message buffer (stack-allocated):\n  Offset  Size  Field Name              Type    Description\n  -----   ----  ---------               ----    -----------\n  0       var   Message concatenation  char[]  Built from multiple string constants\n  \nSecurity Cookie: Stored at [EBP - 0x1c] and XORed with EBP for stack canary verification",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.12a",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:fc3cda58cd680b9e2abaa9dc52c76c11",
