      "name": "InitializeGameUICommandSystem",
      "signature": "void InitializeGameUICommandSystem(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Initializes the game UI command system and renders player status display.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Zero-initialize 16 global command result slots (0x6fa09138-0x6fa09178)\n2. Call ProcessGameCommand for each of 7 command buffer addresses (0x6f9e9e50, 0x6f9e9e80, 0x6f9e9eb0, 0x6f9e9ee0, 0x6f9e9f10, 0x6f9ea000, 0x6f9ea030) and store results\n3. Call ModifyObjectBitfield() to update object state\n4. Loop through 5 command buffers at 0x6f9ea060 with stride 0x30, calling ProcessGameCommand for each and storing results in 0x6fa0912c-0x6fa09130\n5. Call ProcessGameCommand for final buffer at 0x6f9ea0c0, store at 0x6fa09f7c\n6. Initialize 100-element Unicode buffer at ESP+0x148 with default constructors\n7. Retrieve skill tier string from player data at 0x6fa09f14+0x1ea (skill class), 0x1eb (skill info word), extracting tier bits [15:13] and flags at [2] and [5]\n8. Copy skill tier string to temporary buffer at ESP+0x1c using dword-aligned copy\n9. Copy player description from 0x6fa09f14+0xb9 to temporary buffer using dword-aligned copy\n10. Call RenderTextBoxWithUnicodeConversion with display flag from 0x6fa09f14+0x3c7 bit [2]\n11. Call DispatchCommandHandler (implicit ECX, EDI, ESI parameters)\n12. Initialize 100-element and 10-element Unicode buffers at ESP+0x80 and ESP+0x8\n13. Format skill level value from 0x6fa09f14+0x3bd (default 1 if zero) to temporary string buffer using sprintf\n14. Convert formatted string to Unicode at ESP+0xc using win2Unicode (max 9 chars)\n15. Call dispatch_command_handler to get base text string, copy to Unicode buffer at ESP+0x80\n16. Concatenate skill level Unicode string and player description to main text buffer\n17. Call RenderTextBoxUnicodeText(0, 0, 0) for initial render\n18. Retrieve skill tier ordinal from skill info word [15:13], determine dispatch handler ordinal (0x2b75 base + tier offset), call dispatch_command_handler and RenderTextBoxUnicodeText\n19. Repeat render calls (0x2b74, 0x1422-0x1424 based on tier)\n20. Call ProcessGameCommand for final command at 0x6f9ea180, if non-zero result, call dispatch_command_handler(3,0,0) and final RenderTextBoxUnicodeText(3, 0, 0)\n\nParameters:\nNone (stdcall void function)\n\nReturns:\nNone (void return)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Skill level defaults to 1 if player data contains 0 at offset 0x3bd\n- Skill tier extracted as bits [15:13] from player info word at offset 0x1eb\n- Skill class byte at offset 0x1ea used to retrieve skill string\n- Display flag controlled by bit [2] of byte at offset 0x3c7\n- Uses ordinal identifiers 0x1422-0x1425, 0x2b73-0x2b75 for dispatcher command routing\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset  Size  Field Name              Type     Description\n0x1ea   1     skillClass              byte     Player character skill class (0-6)\n0x1eb   2     skillInfoWord           word     Bits [15:13]=tier, [5]=flag, [2]=flag\n0x3bd   1     skillLevel              byte     Skill proficiency level (1-n)\n0x3c7   1     displayFlags            byte     Bit [2]=unicode conversion flag\n0xb9    var   playerDescription       char*    C-string with player status text",
