      "name": "InitializeGameEngine",
      "signature": "int InitializeGameEngine(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Initializes the game engine and processes startup commands.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check engine status via vtable function at offset 0x68\n2. If status is 0 (not running):\n   - Dispatch command handler to process pending commands\n   - Call game initialization cleanup routine\n   - Return 1 (success)\n3. If status is non-zero (already initialized):\n   - Call vtable function at offset 0xac to handle engine state\n   - Execute pre-game initialization sequence\n   - Run secondary initialization routine\n   - Log initialization to channel using logging function\n   - Call final engine handler with result\n   - Return 1 (success)\n4. Both paths return 1 to indicate successful processing\n\nParameters:\nvoid - No parameters\n\nReturns:\nint - Always returns 1 to indicate successful initialization\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Function always returns 1 regardless of branch taken\n- Uses conditional logic to handle two different initialization paths\n- Allocates 32 bytes of stack space for logging buffer\n- Memory at 0x6fa0917c contains pointer to vtable with function pointers\n- Function at 0x1018bca0 is external logging function (ordinal import)\n- String pointers reference game names and channel identifiers",
