      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Conditionally render Unicode text if rendering system is enabled.\n\nALGORITHM:\n1. Load global rendering system pointer from DAT_6fa0a0c8\n2. Check if pointer is non-null (rendering system active)\n3. If active: call RenderTextBoxUnicodeText with textbox pointer, offset 0, and mode 1\n4. Return success code (1)\n\nPARAMETERS:\n- pTextBox (EAX): Pointer to text box structure to render\n\nRETURNS:\n- uint: Always returns 1 (success)\n\nSPECIAL CASES:\n- If rendering system is disabled (global pointer is null), text rendering is skipped\n- The function is a conditional wrapper that guards text rendering behind a system-enabled check",
