      "name": "ProcessGameFrame",
      "signature": "int ProcessGameFrame(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Main game frame processing function that executes each game loop iteration.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load address of first entity mode state (0x6fa09154) into ECX\n2. Clear EDX to 0 as second parameter\n3. Call ValidateAndSetEntityMode to update entity mode state\n4. Repeat steps 1-3 for second entity state at address 0x6fa09150\n5. Repeat steps 1-3 for third entity state at address 0x6fa09158\n6. Call CleanupGameUIAndState to reset UI and state flags from previous frame\n7. Call ProcessCommandQueue to process pending game commands (input, events, etc.)\n8. Load return value 1 into EAX indicating successful frame processing\n9. Return to caller with standard cleanup (RET 0x4)\n\nReturns:\nint - Status code (1 indicates successful frame completion)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Processes three separate entity mode states sequentially, suggesting multiple entity types or zones\n- Returns constant success value (1), indicating no error checking at frame level\n- The RET 0x4 instruction cleans up stack despite no parameters, suggesting function is called indirectly",
