      "name": "AcquireStreamLock",
      "signature": "void AcquireStreamLock(int nStreamIndex, FILE * pFileStream)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Acquires the appropriate synchronization lock for a file stream based on stream index. Uses different locking strategies for low-index (< 20) and high-index streams (>= 20).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load streamIndex parameter from stack [ESP + 0x4]\n2. Compare streamIndex against threshold 0x14 (20 decimal)\n3. If streamIndex < 0x14: Add 0x10 offset and call __lock() (fast path)\n4. If streamIndex >= 0x14: Load FILE pointer, add 0x20 offset to CRITICAL_SECTION, call EnterCriticalSection() (critical section path)\n\nParameters:\nstreamIndex (int) - Stream index (0-31+). Determines lock strategy. 0-19 use __lock, 20+ use CRITICAL_SECTION.\npFileStream (FILE*) - Pointer to FILE structure with CRITICAL_SECTION at offset +0x20\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value",
