      "name": "CrtFlushAllFileStreams",
      "signature": "int CrtFlushAllFileStreams(int nFlushMode)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Flushes open file streams based on the specified flush mode.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize flushed count and error flag to 0\n2. Acquire global stream table lock via __lock(1) to prevent concurrent access\n3. Iterate through all stream table entries from index 0 to g_dwStreamTableSize\n4. For each stream in the table, check if it's valid (non-null) and has pending operations (flag & 0x83)\n5. Skip to next stream if conditions aren't met\n6. Acquire per-stream lock to safely access stream data\n7. Re-check flag field after acquiring lock to handle race conditions\n8. If flushMode == 1 (flush all): Call FlushFileAndCheckFlags on stream, increment flushedCount on success (-1 return indicates error)\n9. If flushMode == 0 (flush dirty only): Test write-dirty bit (flag & 0x2), call FlushFileAndCheckFlags only if dirty, set errorFlag to -1 on failure\n10. Release per-stream lock\n11. Continue to next stream\n12. After loop completes, release global stream table lock via ReleaseStreamTableLock()\n13. Select return value: if flushMode==1 return flushedCount (count of successfully flushed streams), else return errorFlag (-1 on error or count)\n\nParameters:\n  flushMode (int): Flush operation mode\n    1 = Flush all pending streams (regardless of dirty state)\n    0 = Flush only dirty streams (write-dirty bit must be set)\n\nReturns:\n  int: If flushMode==1, returns non-negative count of successfully flushed streams\n       If flushMode==0, returns -1 on error or non-negative count on success\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Flag field uses mask 0x83 (bits 0, 1, 7) to detect streams with pending read/write/eof operations\n  - Flag field bit 2 (0x2) indicates write-dirty state for mode 0 filtering\n  - FlushFileAndCheckFlags() returns -1 to indicate flush failure\n  - Per-stream locks acquired before re-checking flags to prevent use-after-free and race conditions\n  - Global lock released at end even if individual flush operations fail\n\nStructure Layout (FILE structure accessed via g_pStreamTableBase[streamIndex]):\n  Offset  Size  Field Name        Type     Description\n  0x0     4     reserved          void*    Stream pointer\n  0xc     1     _flag             byte     Status flags (bit 0=read, bit 1=write, bit 2=dirty, bit 7=eof)",
