      "name": "CloseFileStreamIfNotLocked",
      "signature": "int CloseFileStreamIfNotLocked(FILE * pStream)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Conditionally closes a FILE stream if it is not already locked.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize closeStatus variable to -1 (failure sentinel value)\n2. Check FILE._flag field at offset 0xc for LOCK flag (0x40 bitmask)\n3. If stream is not locked (zero flag test):\n   a. Call AcquireSynchronizationLock to acquire synchronization lock on stream\n   b. Call __fclose_lk to perform actual close operation (returns status in EAX)\n   c. Clear exception state tracking variable (EBP + -0x4)\n   d. Call LeaveCriticalSectionAfterCloseDispatcher for post-close cleanup\n   e. Store close status from EAX into closeStatus variable\n   f. Set exception state tracking flag and jump to prepare_return\n4. If stream is already locked (zero flag test not taken):\n   a. Clear FILE._flag field to 0 (reset all status flags)\n5. Move closeStatus to EAX as return value\n6. Call __SEH_epilog for structured exception handling cleanup\n7. Return to caller with status code in EAX\n\nParameters:\n- pStream (FILE*): Pointer to FILE stream structure to conditionally close. Contains _flag field at offset 0xc for lock status tracking.\n\nReturns:\nint - Status code from close operation: 0 for success, -1 for failure or pre-locked condition\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Streams with LOCK flag (0x40) set are not closed; their _flag is cleared to 0 instead\n- Pre-locked streams return -1 (failure sentinel) without attempting close\n- __fclose_lk performs actual close and returns status directly\n- LeaveCriticalSectionAfterCloseDispatcher handles critical section cleanup after close\n- Structured Exception Handling (SEH) provides error recovery and context preservation\n- Used by FlushAndCloseStreamHandles during cleanup operations\n\nStructure Layout:\nFILE stream structure at offset 0 from pStream:\n  Offset | Size | Field Name | Type             | Description\n  -------|------|------------|------------------|------------------------------------------\n  +0x0c  |  4   | _flag      | uint (dword)     | Stream status flags (0x40=LOCK bit)\n  +0x20  |  ptr | CritSect   | CRITICAL_SECTION*| Synchronization object for thread safety",
