      "name": "ResetInventoryPanelState_Thunk",
      "signature": "int ResetInventoryPanelState_Thunk(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Initializes game state by validating and updating game entity modes.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load 4 entity pointers from global memory locations (0x6fa09154, 0x6fa09150, 0x6fa09158, 0x6fa0915c)\n2. Call ValidateAndSetEntityMode() for each entity pointer with EDX=0\n3. Load configuration flags from global state (0x6fa09f14 + 0x1eb)\n4. Test flag bits 0x8 and 0x4: if either is clear, call ModifyObjectBitfield() on 2 entities with EDX=1\n5. Load entity state byte from (0x6fa09f14 + 0x35d) for primary entity\n6. If state byte is non-zero, set EDX=1; otherwise check global flag (0x6fa09f34) and set EDX if it's zero\n7. Call ModifyObjectBitfield() on primary entity with computed EDX value\n8. Check global flag (0x6fa0a094) and set EDX=1 if flag is zero\n9. Call ModifyObjectBitfield() on final entity with computed EDX value\n10. Return 1 to indicate success\n\nReturns:\nAlways returns 1 (success status code)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If configuration flag bits 0x8 and 0x4 are both set, skips intermediate ModifyObjectBitfield calls\n- Uses inverted flag logic for two global checks: sets EDX=1 when flag is zero (SETZ instruction)\n- State machine for entity processing: validates all entities first, then conditionally modifies subset\n\nStructure Layout:\nGame Configuration Block (offset +0x1eb from 0x6fa09f14):\n- Offset 0x1eb: Flags word (bit 0x8=validation, bit 0x4=update)\n\nEntity State Block (offset +0x35d from 0x6fa09f14):\n- Offset 0x35d: Primary entity state byte (0=use global, non-zero=active)",
