      "name": "UpdateUIElementsOnTextChange",
      "signature": "void UpdateUIElementsOnTextChange(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Destroys all UI controls in the control array and resets UI state.\nIterates through the control array (g_UIControlArray), calling DestroyUIControl on each pointer,\nthen resets the control count, restores the previous global state, and clears the UI flag.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load the control count from g_UIControlCount (0x6fa09f24)\n2. If count is 0 or negative, jump to exit\n3. Initialize loop: ESI = 0, EDI = address of g_UIControlArray (0x6fa08e80)\n4. Loop iteration:\n   - Push current control pointer onto stack\n   - Call DestroyUIControl(pControl) to clean up the control\n   - Increment control index (ESI)\n   - Advance to next control pointer in array (EDI += 4 bytes)\n   - Compare index with total count\n   - If not done, jump to next iteration\n5. After loop: Pop control array base address\n6. Load g_PreviousGlobalState from 0x6fa09160\n7. Set g_UIControlCount to 0\n8. Call SetGlobalState(savedState) to restore previous state\n9. Clear g_UIStateFlag at 0x6fa09f2c to 0\n10. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\nNone - operates on global UI control array\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nGlobal Variables:\n- g_UIControlArray (0x6fa08e80): Array of UI control pointers\n- g_UIControlCount (0x6fa09f24): Number of controls in array\n- g_PreviousGlobalState (0x6fa09160): Saved global state value\n- g_UIStateFlag (0x6fa09f2c): UI state flag (cleared after cleanup)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If g_UIControlCount is 0 or negative, the function skips the loop entirely\n- Each control pointer is assumed to be 4 bytes (32-bit architecture)\n- The array is contiguous in memory with 4-byte stride between elements\n- After cleanup, both count and flag are reset to prepare for next UI initialization",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
