      "name": "ValidateAndConvertObjectFieldToWin",
      "signature": "void ValidateAndConvertObjectFieldToWin(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Validates and converts a Unicode object field to Windows format.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Retrieve Unicode string pointer from object field via ValidateAndGetObjectField()\\n2. If pointer is valid (not NULL), convert Unicode to Windows format using unicode2Win()\\n   into a 32-byte stack buffer with maximum length 0x1f (31 chars)\\n3. Calculate actual length of converted string by iterating until null terminator\\n4. If converted string length is greater than 0 (non-empty), set bitfield flag to 1\\n5. Call ModifyObjectBitfield() with the flag status to update object state\\n6. Return to caller\\n\\nParameters:\\nNone (uses implicit global context pointers at 0x6fa0a030 and 0x6fa0a028)\\n\\nReturns:\\nvoid\\n\\nSpecial Cases:\\n- If ValidateAndGetObjectField() returns NULL, bitfield is set to 0 (empty string case)\\n- String conversion is limited to 0x1f (31) characters maximum\\n- The function uses an optimized length calculation loop that counts bytes until null terminator",
