      "name": "InitializeUIResources",
      "signature": "void InitializeUIResources(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Initializes all UI resource pointers by building localized file paths and storing them in global variables.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 260-byte local buffer for format string output\n2. For each UI resource template string:\n   - Format the template string with localized path prefix using sprintf/wsprintf\n   - Call BuildLocalizedFilePath() to convert to full resource path\n   - Store returned pointer in corresponding global variable\n3. Load two final overlay resources (SquelchAura and SelectAura)\n4. Call InitializeFrameData() with the two overlay resource pointers\n5. Clean up and return\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Uses 260-byte buffer (local_104) for all format string operations\n- Stores 40+ UI resource pointers in global data section (DAT_6fa09f40-DAT_6fa0a088)\n- Uses both sprintf (for most resources) and wsprintf (for some logo/button resources)\n- Calls BuildLocalizedFilePath for each resource to resolve localized asset paths\n- Final operation initializes frame data with overlay resources (auras)",
