      "name": "AppendNodeToLinkedList",
      "signature": "void AppendNodeToLinkedList(int nodeType, void * secondParam)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Appends a newly created node to a global doubly-linked list in a thread-safe manner.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Create a new linked list node using CreateLinkedListNode with nodeType parameter\\n2. Check if node creation succeeded (non-null pointer returned)\\n3. Enter critical section to protect list modification\\n4. Check if the list is empty (head pointer is null)\\n5. If list is not empty: insert new node at tail by updating previous node's next pointer at offset +0xC\\n6. Update tail pointer to point to new node\\n7. If list is empty: initialize both head and tail pointers to new node\\n8. Exit critical section and return\\n9. If node creation failed: return without modification\\n\\nParameters:\\nnodeType: Type identifier for the node (typically 0 or 4), passed to CreateLinkedListNode\\nsecondParam: Additional parameter from __fastcall convention (passed in EDX)\\n\\nReturns:\\nvoid - No return value\\n\\nStructure Layout:\\nLinkedListNode structure accessed via offset +0xC for next pointer linkage\\nHead/Tail pointers stored at global addresses 0x6fa0a0e8 and 0x6fa0a0ec\\nCritical section object at 0x6fa08f00 for thread synchronization\\n\\nSpecial Cases:\\nEmpty list initialization: When head is null, both head and tail are set to the new node\\nThread safety: All list modifications protected by critical section to prevent race conditions\\nNode creation failure: Function silently returns without modifying list if CreateLinkedListNode returns null",
