      "name": "CleanupAndRestoreUI",
      "signature": "void CleanupAndRestoreUI(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Cleans up UI controls and restores the previous UI state. Destroys all active UI control references and restores the previously saved UI control to active status if available.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Destroy eight UI control pointers stored in global data locations (0x6fa0a018 through 0x6fa0a038)\n2. Load the saved global UI state from 0x6fa09160 and apply it via SetGlobalState\n3. Load the saved active UI control from 0x6fa0a0d0\n4. If a saved control exists, restore it as the active UI control via SetActiveUIControl\n5. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\nvoid - No parameters\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No explicit return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If DAT_6fa0a0d0 is null (no saved control), skip control restoration (jump at 0x6f9db962)\n- All eight control pointers must be destroyed in sequence before state restoration\n- Global state restoration occurs after all controls destroyed, before control reactivation\n\nStructure Layout:\nThis function manages global UI state stored at fixed addresses:\n  0x6fa0a018 - UI Control 1\n  0x6fa0a01c - UI Control 2\n  0x6fa0a020 - UI Control 3\n  0x6fa0a024 - UI Control 4\n  0x6fa0a028 - UI Control 5\n  0x6fa0a02c - UI Control 6\n  0x6fa0a030 - UI Control 7\n  0x6fa0a038 - UI Control 8\n  0x6fa09160 - Saved Global State\n  0x6fa0a0d0 - Saved Active UI Control",
