      "name": "ResetGameStateAndCleanup",
      "signature": "void ResetGameStateAndCleanup(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Resets game state and cleans up UI resources.\n\nPerforms a comprehensive shutdown sequence that cleans up the game UI\nand resets entity mode configurations for all game entities. This function\nis typically called during game transitions, session cleanup, or when\nshutting down the game state.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call CleanupGameUIAndState() to release UI resources and clean up any\n   pending UI operations\n2. Load first entity mode configuration (0x6fa09154) and call\n   ValidateAndSetEntityMode() with EDX = 0 (reset/clear operation)\n3. Load second entity mode configuration (0x6fa09150) and call\n   ValidateAndSetEntityMode() with EDX = 0\n4. Load third entity mode configuration (0x6fa09158) and call\n   ValidateAndSetEntityMode() with EDX = 0\n5. Load fourth entity mode configuration (0x6fa0915c) and call\n   ValidateAndSetEntityMode() with EDX = 0\n6. Clear global game state flag at 0x6fa09f20 to 0 (indicates no active\n   operations or pending state transitions)\n\nParameters:\nNone - This function takes no parameters and operates on global state data.\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value; modifies global game state as a side effect.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- The four identical calls to ValidateAndSetEntityMode() suggest the game\n  manages multiple entity configurations that must all be reset in sequence\n- The EDX register is always cleared (XOR EDX, EDX) before each call,\n  indicating a reset/zero operation mode\n- The final write to 0x6fa09f20 acts as a completion flag that signals\n  the game state reset is complete",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:ad3738c9c75bc5d11089b9e8e770a74d",
