      "name": "CheckPeerStateAndProcess",
      "signature": "void CheckPeerStateAndProcess(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Checks peer/network state flags and conditionally processes peer address with main game handler.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load game state pointer from global DAT_6fa09f14\n2. Read state flags at offset 0x1eb (word with status bits)\n3. Check if bits 3 and 2 are both set (state = 0xC): if yes, return early\n4. Read peer state flag at offset 0x229 (byte boolean)\n5. If peer flag is set, call GetPeerAddress() to validate peer connection\n6. Load result into ESI (0 if peer valid, 1 if peer failed)\n7. Call FUN_6f9dce70() main handler with EAX = peer status result\n8. Return to caller\n\nReturns:\nNo return value (void). Result passed in EAX to FUN_6f9dce70() handler.\nESI holds 0=peer_valid or 1=peer_failed during processing.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Early exit (RET) if state flags indicate bit pattern 0xC (both flags 3 and 4 set)\n- Peer validation only occurs if offset 0x229 flag is non-zero\n- Handler FUN_6f9dce70 branches based on EAX peer validation result",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:8bae38a70423487b823e61140d91a63e",
