      "name": "ProcessGameCommand",
      "signature": "int ProcessGameCommand(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Processes periodic game commands with time-based throttling.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if command buffer pointer (0x6fa09f08) is non-null\n2. If null, return 1 (no command available)\n3. Copy command buffer from offset +4 to local stack buffer (256 bytes)\n4. Get current tick count via GetTickCount()\n5. Compare against last update time (0x6fa09f10) with 1000ms threshold\n6. If threshold not exceeded, return 1 (throttled)\n7. Update last timestamp to current time\n8. Search for '*' wildcard character in command buffer\n9. If wildcard found, use substring after wildcard; otherwise use full buffer\n10. Format command string using sprintf with format string at 0x6f9e77e8\n11. Call FUN_6f9de860() to process command\n12. Query handler state via virtual method at offset 0x68\n13. If handler not ready (return value != 0):\n    - Call handler method at offset 0x14\n    - Call ProcessUnicodeWithCallback()\n    - Return 0 (success)\n14. If handler ready (return value == 0):\n    - Call dispatch_command_handler()\n    - Call FUN_6f9dacb0()\n    - Return 0 (success)\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nint - 1 if command unavailable or throttled; 0 if command processed successfully\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Wildcard filtering: '*' character used as delimiter to extract command portion\n- Time throttling: Commands processed at most once per 1000 milliseconds\n- Handler state checking: Behavior differs based on virtual method at offset 0x68",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
