      "name": "HandleCharacterEventDispatch",
      "signature": "int HandleCharacterEventDispatch(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Dispatch character event handler based on event type from vtable callback.\n\nCalls a vtable function pointer to retrieve the current character event type, then dispatches\nto the appropriate handler (type 0, 2, or 3). Type 0 processes character finalization, type 2\ncopies character data buffer (0x32 bytes of \"Xer_Hanna\" resource), and type 3 handles character\nevent cleanup. Returns success status (1) for all dispatches, or 0 if vtable callback returns null.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load global vtable pointer from DAT_6fa0917c\n2. Allocate 288-byte stack buffer for event data\n3. Call vtable function at offset +0x24 to get event type\n4. Return 0 if callback returns null\n5. Load dispatched type value from stack\n6. Switch on event type:\n   - Type 0: Call FUN_6f9dee50() for character finalization\n   - Type 2: Call CopyMemoryWithAlignment() to copy 0x32 bytes of Xer_Hanna resource\n   - Type 3: Call FUN_6f9dea50() for event cleanup\n7. Return success status 1\n\nParameters:\n  None (uses global state and implicit parameters via vtable callback)\n\nReturns:\n  int - 1 if event dispatch succeeds, 0 if vtable callback fails\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Magic number 0x32 (50 decimal) is the byte count for character resource buffer\n  - Magic number 0x124 (292 decimal) is the total stack allocation including alignment\n  - Stack buffer base at ESP stores the dispatched event type\n  - EDX at ESP+4 is passed to vtable callback (unused in this analysis)\n  - Unknown event types default to return 1 (success without action)",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:62a4a2a17f9742f1a7afb47de6a9ba71",
