      "name": "ProcessAndRenderUI",
      "signature": "int ProcessAndRenderUI(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Processes and renders the game UI interface.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calls RenderAndProcessGameUI() to render all UI elements and handle input\n2. Loads the active UI control pointer from global variable DAT_6fa0a0d0\n3. Tests if a control is queued for activation (non-zero pointer)\n4. If control pointer exists, calls SetActiveUIControl() to apply the pending control change\n5. Returns status code 1 to indicate successful completion\n\nParameters:\nNone. Uses global state variable DAT_6fa0a0d0 for pending control changes.\n\nReturns:\nint - Status code (always 1 indicating success)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If no UI control is pending (DAT_6fa0a0d0 == 0), skips the SetActiveUIControl() call\n- Uses __stdcall convention indicating caller-provided parameters on stack\n\nGlobal Dependencies:\nDAT_6fa0a0d0 - Pointer to pending active UI control to activate",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
