      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Destroys all UI control objects and restores the previous active control.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Destroy 30 UI control objects stored at fixed addresses in data segment (0x6fa09cec through 0x6fa09d60)\n2. Call special cleanup routine on control at 0x6fa09d28 (different cleanup handler)\n3. Set global game state from value stored at 0x6fa09160\n4. Check if previous active control pointer at 0x6fa0a0d0 is non-null\n5. If non-null, restore the previous active control\n6. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\nNone - operates on global UI state variables\n\nReturns:\nNone (void)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- The control at 0x6fa09d28 uses a separate cleanup routine (func_0x10204370) instead of DestroyUIControl\n- Global state restoration ensures UI consistency after cleanup\n- Previous active control may be null, handled by TEST/JZ check",
